Mr. Nuon Chanrith, a member in charge of operations at the Preah Vihear Provincial Election Secretariat, also mentioned about Mr. Dim Sovannarom's presentation that he had gained a lot of good knowledge and kept it as a key to his work. In the future. The other participants also applauded his presentation and suggested that such training be continued in the coming days.
Mr. Mok Dara, Deputy Secretary General of the NEC, said at the closing ceremony that this is an important event and an opportunity for all NEC civil servants to gain more knowledge related to their skills. Body to be the basis for performing work more efficiently and with high quality.
He highly appreciated and highly appreciated all the NEC officials who worked hard to gain knowledge during these 4 days successfully. He said that in every election, every examination of the voter list and voter registration, the NEC always provides training to its officials at all levels on laws, regulations and procedures, ethics and other instructions related to skills. Prepare to perform work more efficiently.
The NEC is not only the supreme body enshrined in the Constitution; Respect the Constitution, respect the law because the NEC is a technical institution.
This training course took place immediately after the 19-day review of the 2020 voter list and registration ended with excellent results. At the same time, the NEC observed that the implementation of regulations and procedures was still lacking, so the NEC assigned to organize training courses for NEC civil servants and secretariat officials. Capital, provinces organize elections.
This is to strengthen the capacity of NEC civil servants, and the NEC will collect all the recommendations of the 25 CECs on the lessons and experiences encountered recently to propose amendments and submissions. The 11 stakeholders will review before the NEC releases the public and to review the voter list and voter registration as well as the upcoming election.
Please be informed that this is the second time that the Department of Voter Training and Education has organized this 4-day training course from 26 to 29 October 2020, with a total of approximately participants. 131 people, including 23 women who are officials from the NEC office and the 25 provincial election secretaries.
