(Siem Reap): Senior officials from the Ministry of Rural Development and officials from the Siem Reap Provincial Development Department have begun repairing roads and inspected some rural roads in Siem Reap province to prepare for rehabilitation after being damaged by floods. People can easily travel and transport agricultural crops as the harvest and harvest season approaches.
During the action on October 28, 2020, Mr. Phuong Sophea, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Rural Development, stated that the road that was urgently repaired was for rural roads that were damaged by floods in Angkor Chum District, Siem Reap Province.
The floods of 2020 have damaged rural road infrastructure in some districts in the province, making it difficult for people to travel.
He added that with the care of the people from the Royal Government, Mr. Phuong Sophea and Mr. Kheng Nhol, Director of the Department of Rural Development led a technical team on rural roads to repair a 7,600-lane red gravel road. The meter connects from Char Chhouk commune to Koul commune, Angkor Chum district.
At the same time, the team also inspected the road from Kdey Run commune to Prey Chrouk commune, Puok district, 15,000 meters long, after being damaged by the floods of 2020 to connect people to traffic as well as transport agricultural products. Same as before.
The director of the Siem Reap Provincial Department of Rural Development said that the inspection and repair of rural roads damaged by the floods was an immediate response to the recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
He added that across Siem Reap, 20 roads in four districts, including Puok Varin, Angkor Thom and Angkor Chum districts, were affected, with four roads in Angkor Chum district being the most severely damaged.
He said the roads damaged by the floods were nearly 200 kilometers out of a total length of nearly 5,000 kilometers.
