(Banteay Meanchey): A drunken man who chased people all over the village with a knife and did not give up and chased after another car that was left silent was arrested by the police force at 4:30 pm on October 27, 2020 In Veal Hat village, Malai commune, Malai district, Banteay Meanchey province.
Local police said that the suspect was named Sieng Veasna, 36 years old, living in Veal Hat village, Malai commune, Banteay Meanchey province. Local police confirmed that the perpetrator, when drunk, could not control his emotions and used a knife to threaten the neighbors who wanted to kill the people, but did not dare to complain to the authorities because they were afraid of the suspects.
Undeterred, he chased after a 67-year-old man named Chey Chim, but the victim escaped and continued to chase after Oeur Savoeun, the owner of the car, causing two minor injuries.
After the action, the suspect was arrested by the local police force and sent to the Malai District Police Inspectorate to prepare a case to be sent to the provincial police commission and build a case to be sent to the provincial court for legal proceedings.
