What is different is that in the past, the boss of the demonstration was in the country, while now the boss of the demonstration is abroad, but the process of organizing the demonstration is still the same, nothing has changed at all.
The structure of the "mercenary demonstration" in Cambodia is: there are bosses or demonstrators, there are mercenaries to demonstrate, there are people to help behind the demonstration to encourage shelter under the label of civil society organizations and there are people to capture the view of Performing scenes in the "mercenary demonstration" to be broadcast by this group under the banner of independent media.
Behold, the demonstration on October 23 in front of the Chinese Embassy was organized by a group of overseas demonstrators. Domestic demonstrators, on the other hand, are only waiting to perform in scenes directed by outsiders. Both the demonstrators, the delivery service staff, the banner organizers, etc. And etc. They are all hired to perform. And at the end of the show, they will get money back home.
After the scene in front of the Chinese Embassy failed, Ho Van ordered the mercenaries to return to perform in front of the US Embassy. Hovan ordered his staff to line up in front of the US Embassy and not rush to the petition to the embassy, but to read the petition first to extend the time for the photographers to capture the photos and content.
At this point, it is remembered that since the emergence of the extremist opposition party, the leader of this party, who has the title of "boss" of the demonstrators, has always raised the mercenaries to protest. At the party headquarters, there is a group of protesting women who live in the party headquarters on a regular basis. The group is always present at demonstrations.
For example, if there is a slight clash with the authorities, they pretend to fall or faint, and their companions come to the moment, which seems to have been knocked unconscious by the authorities, but in reality it is all the scenes. Sometimes they even hire small children to stand in the procession to make the scene even more miserable.
The scenes were filmed by their network, which hired photographers and took refuge under the banner of an independent newspaper, to spread propaganda to slander the authorities. Protesters, who have taken refuge under the banner of civil society or independent analysts, have expressed sympathy and condemned the authorities for using violence against women and children.
These scenes have been performed for decades and have damaged the image of government authorities. Now is the time to unravel the structure of those "mercenary demonstrations." The leaking of Ho Van's order to protest in front of the Chinese Embassy is a clear indication of the true face of the "mercenary demonstration" movement in Cambodia.
In the past, extremist opponents often boasted that "demonstrations are an expression of the will of the real people", as they came voluntarily and did not receive any money. But now the structure of the "mercenary demonstration" in Cambodia has been peeled off.
