"Bakong" electronic payment system has been officially launched in Cambodia!
(Phnom Penh): The National Bank of Cambodia has decided to officially launch and launch the electronic payment operating system "Bakong System" on October 28, 2020.
Ms. Chea Serey said that the Bakong system provides the ability to pay through the institution efficiently, securely and reduce operating costs. Therefore, all these suffixes will be the driving force to promote the financial environment in the country more widely.
"For the future direction, the 'Bakong system' will examine the possibility of cross-border payments and transfers with other countries in the region to make it easier for foreign workers to send money to their families through the low-cost, convenient and secure Bakong system," she said. "
He added that under the wise leadership and long-term vision of Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, who recommended the initiative to develop the core payment system infrastructure to enable banking and financial institutions to conduct payment transactions. Interoperability, secure, efficient card, reduce operating costs and boost the financial environment.
"At the same time, the development of the Bakong system is a contribution to economic development towards the digital economy of the Fourth Industrial Revolution in line with the digital economy in the ASEAN region," she said.
Please be informed that on June 5, 2018, the National Bank of Cambodia organized a promotion ceremony for banking and financial institutions and payment service providers about this project to develop the Bakong system. After the publication, 39 institutions have expressed interest in participating in this project.
Following the support of banking and financial institutions as well as payment institutions, the National Bank of Cambodia announced the launch of the Bakong system on 18 July 2019 with the participation of four banking and financial institutions: ACLEDA Bank , Vattanac Bank, Overseas Commercial Bank of Cambodia and Wing Specialized Bank.
From July 18, 2019 to October 28, 2020, the number of participating members has increased to 18 (16 banking and financial institutions and 2 payment service providers). Banks and finance, as well as about 24 other payment service institutions, have been granted in principle membership in the Bakong system and are preparing to study the technicalities of connecting the system.
