(Prey Veng): Mr. Steng Sokhom, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group on Kamchay Mear District, noted that public forums are an excellent way to find the difficulties and problems of the people and respond effectively. Efficiency. In this regard, he urged the working group to continue to expand this public forum to grasp the problem and put measures to solve the people.
Mr. Steung Sokhom introduced this during the meeting to summarize the work results for the first 9 months of 2020 and set the direction for implementation for the national working group to help Kamchay Mear district on the morning of October 28, 2020 at the meeting hall of Kamchay Mear district. The ceremony was held with the participation of the chairperson, deputy chairperson of the Royal Government working group to visit local districts, communes and villages.
After listening to the 9-month summary report read by Mr. Soeung Socheat, Kamchay Mear District Governor, Dr. Steung Sokhom also allowed the members who attended the meeting to comment on the work done during the period. 9 months ago to be the input for setting the direction to continue in the future.
Dr. Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group spoke about the work scenario that has been set out in the past, stating that 2020 is the beginning of the work to be observed and the plan for measures to continue to work in 2021, which is the year To strive to solve all the challenges.
In a democratic meeting with cross-examination between the chairperson and the participants, a number of challenges were raised, including irregularities in the selection of poor families to be supported by the Royal Government. .
The Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group instructed the working group officials and the district administration to work with a high degree of internal consensus, to clearly define the principles for the subjects to be assisted and not to follow political tendencies.
Dr. Steng Sokhom said that in a society, it is not different from a family, jealousy, greed, desire still exists, even if you already have it, still want it is inevitable, but not true. That leave it as it is, there must be a solution. In order to be fair to the poor, the working group must adhere to the principles of good governance, transparency, equity, and justice as a priority in selection.
At the same time, the Chairman of the Working Group also urged all working groups to continue to pay attention to the organization of public forums to be held in the commune regularly to be able to grasp the concerns of the people and suggestions. And be able to respond and explain to them exactly what their concerns are and also be able to know the shortcomings and participate in resolving issues that occur at the local time.
On the same day, after the meeting, Dr. Steng Sokhom handed over 10 tons of rice donated by Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng and his wife to Kamchay Mear District Party to help the poor and needy families. Sponsorship.
