Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khi Instructs Private Security Agencies to Change Work Behavior After Receiving Professional Training from Police
(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khi, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, on the occasion of closing the training course for private security agents on the evening of October 28, 2020, instructed all private security agencies to change their working attitude. What is right after receiving professional training from the Department of Private Security Management.
Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khi emphasized that the change in work attitude after receiving this training is to make the company or institution where it works to be interested in its work capacity, because in companies or establishments not yet. Sent agents to study a lot yet.
The Deputy Chief of the National Police noted that private security agents, when on duty, should think that even if they work for a different company or institution, they should be considered as a model citizen by using the word Gestures, responses to customers, etc.
In addition, General Er Sok Khi considered the role of private security agencies as an important support force to the competent authorities. If you see or suspect any illegal activity, whether in your standing position or where, you must immediately report it to the nearest competent authority or to the Department of Private Security Management directly by phone. Teachers as well as the team.
He added that the private security sector is also an important sector that must actively contribute to maintaining security, social order, as well as protecting national interests and national development. He said private security agencies have a role not only in protecting private property or private enterprises, but also in obliging to protect public property, social security and the lives of citizens.
Meanwhile, Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey, Director of the Private Security Management Department, said that the 29th Private Security Agency Training Course will be held for two days from October 27 to 28, 2020 with the Deputy Chief of Staff. National Police of the Department of Private Security Management, 5 members and 169 trainees (4 females).
Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey confirmed that up to now, 29 private security agency training courses have been conducted, with a total of 110 (5 females) Deputy Chiefs of the National Police of the Department of Private Security Management and the Capital-Provincial Police Commission (5 females). A total of 5,373 participants (135 females) participated.
He stated that the participants received the lessons carefully prepared, focusing on lessons such as:
First, the roles and responsibilities of private security agents, second: objective prevention methods, third: firefighting measures and fire evacuation, fourth: cooperation with private security agencies with local authorities, fifth: understanding Crimes and criminal procedures for private security agencies, 6: Protection and security of the scene of private security agencies, 7: Inspect and analyze the scene and the annex road traffic.
