US official: "North Korea could face the same fate as Vietnam if Kim Jong Un looks at the situation around him"
Marc Knapper, US Deputy Assistant Secretary of State for Korea and Japan, also stressed the importance of the United States and South Korea working together to eliminate North Korea's nuclear program.
At a seminar hosted by the Washington-based Atlantic Council with Seoul-based analysts, Marc said it was important for both countries to work together. Together to find a solution to maintain stability on the Korean Peninsula. His remarks came as nuclear disarmament talks between the United States and North Korea stalled.
He added that Kim Jong Un was still able to maintain security and power, even as the country entered a free market regime, as we see in Vietnam, which is still a communist country but has become. Is the 16th largest trading partner of the United States, and he thinks the same thing could happen to North Korea if Kim Jong Un is open-minded and looks around.
In the first nine months of this year, Cambodia had 2.05 million international arrivals and departures, down 77% due to Kovid 19
(Phnom Penh): In the first nine months of 2020, Cambodia received 2.05 million international arrivals and departures, down 77 percent compared to the same period in 2019. This is according to the achievement report of the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation.
The report on the achievements of the Secretariat of Civil Aviation was presented on the occasion that General Dr. Mao Havanal, Minister in Charge of the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation, led a delegation to defend the draft law with the Fifth Committee and the Ninth Committee of the National Assembly on This October 28.
The Undersecretary of State said that during the meeting, the Minister mentioned the achievements of Civil Aviation in 2019 and the current situation in 2020, including:
After Cambodia achieved peace, political stability, national security and national unity on all sides under the win-win policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian People's Party, the Cambodian civil aviation sector has grown significantly. Proud of 2019:
* There are three international airports by international standards and two new international airport investments.
* Equipped with state-of-the-art, regional and most secure aviation equipment in line with international standards.
* Human resources are given priority in strengthening and expanding capacity through regular training of international standards.
However, under the guidance of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, the air transport sector must be in a new mode of operation and participate in the fight against Kovid-19 to allow investors. Foreigners entered and exited by air regularly and allowed their Cambodian compatriots to return home.
On the morning of October 28, 2020, Ms. Claire Conan confirmed her position in cooperation with the Ministry of Social Affairs on social assistance to help vulnerable people.
"The World Food Program (WFP) is pleased to work with the Ministry of Social Affairs on technical assistance on social work, as this is the main work of WFP and the organization has a lot of experience in this work," she said.
Regarding the presentation of such a position, Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation also expressed his gratitude for what she said.
"In the future and in the future, the Ministry of Social Affairs has a lot of work to do, which can be supported and cooperated with the World Food Organization as well as other partner organizations," he said.
The minister also said that the ministry also plans to set up a center for thousands of vulnerable people, hoping that the World Food Program can co-operate in this work.
In this morning's meeting, Mr. Vong Soth also mentioned many tasks that the Ministry of Social Affairs is working on this social assistance work. For example, the implementation of cash support for pregnant women and children under 2 years of age, and another important task is to provide cash support to poor and vulnerable families during the fight against Kovid 19.
The meat subsidy program has facilitated the livelihood of tens of thousands of poor families, and the Royal Government has decided to continue implementing this program until the end of 2020. This is an additional confirmation of the Minister to the Director of the World Food Organization in Cambodia.
UN Special Rapporteur on Human Rights and Environment Praises Cambodia for Taking Action to Improve Environment
The Special Rapporteur's remarks came on October 27, 2020, during an interactive dialogue of the Third Committee of the 75th Session of the United Nations General Assembly. He also believes that the best practices of the Royal Government of Cambodia provide a model that encourages other countries to address global environmental crises.
* In Cambodia, the right to a clean, safe, hygienic and sustainable environment is protected by the Constitution, which in particular encourages the importance of nature, ecosystems and biodiversity.
In accordance with Cambodia's environmental governance reforms for sustainable development programs, some forest areas have been designated as protected areas and areas for integrated conservation and environmental governance reform. As a result, Cambodia's current protected area system covers 39% of the country's land area.
More than 70,000 hectares of rice fields in Banteay Meanchey affected by floods, Agriculture Minister distributes rice seeds to farmers ready to replant
(Banteay Meanchey): According to the preliminary report of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Banteay Meanchey Province, as of October 28, 2020, 71,489 hectares of rice fields have been affected by the floods, including light paddy. At the beginning of the middle rice season, upland rice and heavy paddy, of which 15,708 hectares were damaged.
On the morning of October 28, 2020, Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, came to meet and bring 29,800 kg of rice seeds to distribute to 298 affected farmers (100 kg). Poor / Family) The ceremony was held in Wat Char, Rohat Teuk Village, Rohat Teuk Commune, Mongkul Borei District.
Therefore, the Minister and the provincial governors, local authorities and colleagues brought the precious gift of Samdech Techo in the form of rice seeds and 20,000 Riels / family to distribute to farmers to alleviate livelihood problems and restore food production.
Separately, for provinces or areas that are not affected, the Minister advised the Department to cooperate with the farmers to take care of crops and protect water in case of water shortage at the end of the season. Farmers must be encouraged to grow mixed crops, raise chickens, fish and frogs to ensure future food security.
Mr. Run Sophannara, Deputy Director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, said that due to the effects of the floods, 55 businesses, including chickens, fish, rice, cassava and maize, were affected by the floods. 2327 family members throughout the province, including 975 families severely affected, 519 families on average and 150 families lightly).
In this regard, the department as well as the ASPIRE team have worked hard to encourage the members of the group to restore all production after the water recedes.
Regarding the above program, the Minister thanked the Royal Government through the Ministry of Economy and Finance and the IFAD Foundation for supporting and financing the implementation of this program.
He added that the program is currently having a positive impact on poverty reduction and increasing resilience to climate change for poor, small-scale and vulnerable farmers, with a focus on improving the efficiency of input services. Agriculture responds to the needs of smallholder farmers and helps them to engage in agribusiness from subsistence to commercial agriculture based on the principles of sustainable and sustainable development.
The Minister confirmed that the current agricultural inputs have fully contributed to the implementation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's high recommendation on October 24, ordering the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to come down and restore food production. Especially rice after the water recedes.
He advised the program implementation unit and project beneficiaries to update on new activities in line with the current situation (Kovid-19 epidemic and floods) in order to seize the golden opportunity. Increase production, ensure supply both now and in the future, reduce costs, reduce labor, use appropriate technology.
Chief of Wat Teuk Thla Donates to the Cambodian Red Cross in Khan Sen Sok, 1 Ton Rice, 50 Boxes of Noodles, 4 million Riels
Expressing gratitude to the Chief Bishop of the pagoda, Mr. Sak Kanharith, Honorary President of the Sub-Branch and Representative of Mr. Mov Manit, said that under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has made a tangible development. Every day, people have a better life than before, especially the achievements in the pagodas lead Buddhists to participate in the celebration of the promotion of Buddhism to flourish and worship.
After the monks received a lot of gifts, the monks did not forget the authorities and also shared those gifts back to the authorities to distribute to the poor people, which makes the owners of the alms double.
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Kampong Thom Province and Chairman of the Provincial Disaster Management Committee, received a donation from Mr. Ly Sihanon.
He said this on October 28, 2020, on the occasion of the representation of the Minister of Justice, Mr. Keut Rith, who signed an agreement with OXFAM to receive assistance in setting up a non-judicial dispute resolution mechanism in Cambodia at the Ministry.
The non-judicial dispute resolution mechanism in Cambodia has already prepared the draft Zero Draft. Further work is that the Ministry of Justice will organize consultative workshops from all stakeholders, including civil society organizations, to make the drafting of this mechanism as thorough as possible.
A senior official at the Ministry of Justice stated: "Some minor crimes, especially traffic offenses, can be mediated by compensation without going to court. "So in other countries, they determine the type of case that can be reconciled, and most of them are civil cases."
"For the Cambodian context, we will continue to discuss what cases can be reconciled," he said. At that point, we look forward to consulting meetings in many workshops in the near future.
According to Mr. Chin Malin, the Ministry of Justice wants all stakeholders to consult and draft a non-judicial dispute resolution mechanism in Cambodia so that it will not be criticized as an achievement of the Ministry of Justice alone. He added that the out-of-court settlement mechanism, the ministry does not know whether to make a law or just a policy, but to wait for more input from all parties before deciding later.
If the law is made, it will take a long time, but if it is a policy, it will be ready soon, and the Ministry of Justice wants it to be launched in 2021. This is according to Mr. Chin Malin, adding that this mechanism will help speed up the resolution of congestion cases as well.
Mr. Malin said the benefit of out-of-court dispute resolution was that it was quick, uncomplicated and did not waste time for the parties to the dispute. In addition, the main benefit is that the arbitrator's decision is not as public as the court's decision, so that the privacy of the parties to the dispute is not disclosed.
