Chbar Ampov District Governor Orders Officers and Authorities to Suspend Illegal Fencing
(Phnom Penh): Chbar Ampov district governor Cheng Monira has ordered professional officers and local authorities to suspend illegal fencing in order to privatize the banks of the Mekong River in Chbar Ampov district's Prek Eang commune.
According to the report, the fencing took place in Kbal Chroy village, Sangkat Prek Eang, Khan Chbar Ampov, about 200 meters on the banks of the Mekong River, which the villagers allegedly violated.
According to a report from Chbar Ampov district officials, the construction of the steel fence has not yet received a construction permit from the competent authorities. Therefore, the team decided to ask the fence owners to temporarily suspend the construction of the fence, waiting for the dispute to be resolved first.
According to district officials, the authorities had banned and dismantled the fence posts on the site, calling them illegal constructions and encroaching on the riverbank, but the perpetrators continued.
Authorities report that the owner of the fence, Lim Vuthy, was the representative and acknowledged that the siege was on a riverbank that was prohibited by law from being privately owned. In the report, Mr. Lim Vuthy confirmed that the sale and purchase documents have only the signature and seal of the village chief. But for the land along the river, no one can take ownership and the authorities have no right to sell.
