(Pursat): On October 28, 2020, the working group of the Electricity of Cambodia Alliance and the Electricity Authority of Cambodia jointly brought some food items with a total amount of nearly 20,000 USD to the officers, soldiers and intervention brigade. No. 14 standing in Tnaot Chum commune, Krakor district, Pursat province.
The handing over of food to the officers of the 14th Intervention Brigade under the leadership of Mr. Keo Rattanak, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister in charge of the Director General of Electricite du Cambodge, on behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
On that occasion, Minister Keo Rattanak sent a message from Samdech Techo Prime Minister to the officers and soldiers standing in the 14th Intervention Brigade.
Mr. Keo Rattanak said that the Solidarity Unit between EDC and the Electricity Authority of Cambodia regularly visited and supported the officers and soldiers of the 14th Intervention Brigade, and he thanked all the troops. Helping people during the floods as well as rescuing people from the dangers of flooding.
(Phnom Penh): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, delivered a message to His Excellency Dr. Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, who wished him a happy birthday. The 16th year of the accession to the throne.
In His Majesty the King's message: "I am pleased to receive the letter from Samdech Kittipritthbandit dated October 26, 2020 and a beautiful flower basket with deep meaning." Blessings on the occasion of the 16th anniversary of my accession to the throne.
I would like to express my deep gratitude to Samdech Kittipritthbandit for appreciating my Royal Highness's activities, supporting and supporting the Cambodian Red Cross in order to be able to strengthen the mechanism to rescue people affected by various disasters throughout God. The Kingdom of Cambodia.
The following is a message from His Majesty the King to Samdech Kittipritthbandit: The death toll from the floods has risen to 44 (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The report of the National Committee for Disaster Management shows that as of October 27, 2020 The death toll from floods rises to 44. In Banteay Meanchey province, there are up to 26 people.
It should be noted that in order to offer condolences and solve the difficulties of the families of the corpses, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has decided to support the families of the corpses with 10 million Riels per corpse and Duke Lao Bunpa with 4 million Riels.
Senior Minister Kun Kim, first vice chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, said that the families of 41 bodies had already received the donation.
The report of the National Committee for Disaster Management also said that the floods affected 20 capitals and provinces, including: Pursat, Pailin, Banteay Meanchey, Phnom Penh, Battambang, Svay Rieng, Tbong Khmum, Oddar Meanchey, Siem Reap, Takeo, Kampong Speu, Mondulkiri, Sihanoukville, Koh Kong, Preah Vihear, Stung Treng, Kampong Cham, Kandal. Kampong Chhnang and Kampong Thom.
According to the National Committee for Disaster Management, 272,263 hectares of paddy fields and 96,945 hectares of mixed crops were flooded.
