The World Health Organization (WHO) is currently discussing with the Chinese authorities the conditions for internationally approved and recognized conditions. But experts say the WHO should wait to see the effectiveness and safety of the third phase of the human vaccine trial.
The COVID-19 pandemic could be a "situation changer" for the Chinese vaccine industry, which has long focused on the domestic market, even though it is one of the world's largest vaccine suppliers. Get 700 million doses a year, or more than 20 percent of the world's vaccine production.
Such a decision is seen by experts as China's intention to increase international confidence to be able to penetrate the world market in the long run. Not only that, China also wants to use this participation to eliminate criticism that its vaccines are ineffective and unsafe, and if this can be done, it will help China promote and sell its vaccines internationally.
Two Thais die after stepping on a mine while driving a tractor to cut grass near the Cambodian-Thai border
(Banteay Meanchey): Two Thai nationals died instantly when a tractor was driving to cut grass near the border post No. 43, stepping on a mine, causing the tractor to explode. This incident happened at 1 pm on October 27, 2020.
Colonel So Sovannary, Commander of the 911th Border Guard Battalion, said that at the border at the 43rd border post in Thai territory in Non Sung village, Kork Thung commune, Kork Thung district, Sa Kaeo province, opposite Prey Chan village, Or Bei Choan district. O'Chrov, Banteay Meanchey Province, Cambodia, found a tractor stepped on a mine, causing two deaths and completely damaged the tractor.
According to the commander, the victims were Khieu Prumma, 70, father and son Khieu Phongsak, 37, both of Non Sung village, Kork Thung commune, Kork Thung district, Sa Kaeo province, Thailand.
According to relatives before the incident, they drove two tractors, a father and son, to cut grass at the 43rd border post, and landed on the mine. The bodies of the victims were taken to the funeral home by the Thai Squadron 124 and their families for a traditional ceremony at the funeral home.
