(Banteay Meanchey): From the flood until the water receded gradually, 65,700 hectares of rice and 666 hectares of mixed crops were damaged. But immediately, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Chacho Hun Sen, ordered the Ministry of Agriculture and all authorities to provide rice seeds, potatoes, six crops to farmers affected by the floods. This is according to Mr. Ou Rathrey, Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province.
The statement by the Banteay Meanchey provincial governor was made at a meeting on the effects of the floods, chaired by Dr. Vith Sandab, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, Chairman of the Secretariat of the Cambodian Food Reserve System, relevant officials and municipal administrations, as well as commune officials. Many communes on October 27.
The provincial governor claimed that Banteay Meanchey province was affected by the floods and inundated rice and mixed crops in Mongkul Borei, Serey Sophorn, Poipet and O'Chrov districts.
Speaking at the meeting, Dr. Vong Sandab said that after the floods recede, there is a lot of work to continue to restore the impact. "Our thing to continue to do to farmers who have been damaged and affected crops is to provide six varieties of rice seeds to grow after the flood, and also have agricultural machinery to serve farmers." .
In that, Dr. Vong Sandab also asked all relevant officials to assess the damage of the people during the flood, especially the Provincial Department of Agriculture to deal only with the people who actually damaged rice.
Dr. also pointed out that in addition to recovering from the damage caused by the floods, the necessary work that people do more is to continue the fight against Kovid-19, which has destroyed many of us.
