This was stated by Mr. Song Saran, President of the Cambodian Rice Federation during a meeting with Mr. Wu Guoquan, Consul General of Economy and Trade of the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia on October 27, 2020 at the Embassy of China, focusing on promoting imports. Export more Cambodian rice to China
Duke Song Saran emphasized to the Consul General and the meeting about Cambodia's joy and admiration for cooperation on Cambodian rice exports to China. He stated that since 2014, five Memoranda of Understanding (MoUs) have been signed between Cambodia and China and have been continuing to export until September 2020. The volume of Cambodian rice exports to the Chinese market is An increase of nearly 1 million tons and will reach 1.2 million tons in the near future.
Oknha, President of the Cambodian Rice Federation, also mentioned the work and ambition of Cambodia's exports, which aims to boost Cambodian rice exports to international markets to 1 million tons from 2021, a significant increase. With profitable and sustainable market.
Achieving this export target is an indispensable part of China's market share. For 2020, according to the expectations and assessment of the Cambodian Rice Federation, Cambodia's rice exports will reach 800,000 tons, Cambodia needs to work closely with China in the first nine months of 2020, the market of China accounts for 35% of Cambodia's total rice exports.
In addition to highlighting the potential of the Chinese market and opportunities to expand Cambodia's exports to China, Ms. Kim Srey Roth, Vice President of the Cambodian Rice Federation and Chairman of the Executive Committee for Marketing and Export Promotion of the United States. A proposed and discussed with the meeting counterpart on the following work:
1. Examine the possibility of setting an annual date for the implementation of the MoU, which should begin in early May and end in late April, as Cambodia's main rice harvest is generally in November and December, during which time This is a very busy time for drying and storing, and at the end of the year, there are many holidays that make it difficult to supply on time the amount of rice to be exported by the end of the season.
2. Examine the possibility of establishing a joint Cambodian-Chinese arbitration panel to resolve disputes in the rice trade, which may have a joint Cambodian-Chinese composition or a consular representative of the Chinese Embassy.
3. Request the Chinese side to examine the possibility of promoting the promotion of Cambodian rice in China, especially "Jasmine Angkor" through the Chinese media more.
4: Examine the feasibility of assisting agricultural laboratories to cover more criteria than before, as inspections are currently limited, especially in terms of taste and odor, which has led to problems with some past supply contracts. Some rice.
5. Request to push for more orders in the fourth quarter of 2020 to be completed as soon as the MoU is signed and to reach the preparation of a new MoU.
Wu Guoquan hailed the past achievements and accepted to explore possible solutions and work together to expand the two countries' trade, especially rice trade.
