Garment Manufacturers Association of Cambodia provides humanitarian aid to flood victims
(Pursat): As part of the social work of the Garment Manufacturers Association of Cambodia (GMAC), on October 28, 2020, the leaders of the Association distributed donations to 1,000 flood-affected families in Pursat Province, where this program is organized directly on the premises of Pursat Provincial Hall.
According to the report of the National Committee for Disaster Management, floods caused by rain for several days since the beginning of October 2020 have seriously affected the lives of Cambodians in In 19 provinces, Pursat is also one of the provinces hardest hit by the floods.
The floods not only damaged homes and people's livelihoods, they also wreaked havoc on human and animal life and damaged tens of thousands of hectares of farmland. Many families in the flooded areas have been evacuated to temporary shelters and temporary shelters and other food items from the government and philanthropists.
Seeing this situation and in order to contribute to alleviate the suffering of the suffering people, the leaders of the Garment Manufacturers Association in Cambodia brought gifts to distribute to the affected people in Pursat town in 7 communes and to From Kandieng district, 3 communes. Donations include clothes, blankets, noodles, packaged fish, rice, water and other groceries.
It should also be noted that these donations are donations from factories that are members of the association (GMAC) and partly the direct budget of the association, as well as donations from members of the executive committee of the association, managers and staff at all levels. Of the Secretariat of the Singapore Association and Community of Cambodia (SCC).
The association's leaders and members hope that these gifts will help alleviate the hardships of our people who are suffering in this difficult time.
