New tourist destinations will be created to attract 7 million international tourists to Siem Reap-Angkor by 2035
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, said that in order to attract about 7 million international tourists to Siem Reap-Angkor by 2035, new major tourist destinations around Angkor will be established. Included in the Siem Reap Tourism Development Master Plan.
After the meeting to review the results of the first nine months of 2020 and the direction of implementation in the fourth quarter of 2020 during the crisis on the afternoon of October 26, 2020, Mr. Thong Khon told reporters that the master plan for tourism development. Siem Reap has been submitted to the National Commission for Tourism Development, and the Ministry of Tourism is preparing to shorten it to be submitted to the Royal Government for review and approval in the future.
The minister said that four new major tourist destinations on two existing destinations could be established, including the Tonle Sap Lake, Phnom Kulen, Banteay Srei and Siem Reap Thmey.
The Minister stated that the establishment of the new city of Siem Reap is in order to support the current city of Siem Reap, which can not build high-rise buildings or structures that affect the cultural heritage.
On the other hand, the Royal Government of Cambodia has set out its vision to attract 7 million international tourists to Siem Reap by 2035, creating about 900,000 direct jobs and generating an estimated $ 5 billion in revenue over the period. Same as that. To achieve this vision, the current city of Siem Reap is not sustainable enough, it is necessary to create a new city.
