Spokesman for the General Commission: On October 27, another 1,078 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 180 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to October 27, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected And fined a total of 199,664 vehicles, including 147,542 motorcycles and 52,122 vehicles of all types.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 180 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine vehicles for offenses has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
It should be noted that for October 27, 2020, there were 8 traffic accidents throughout Cambodia, in which 2 people were killed and 10 people were injured (9 people were seriously injured).
