Son beats father because he was angry because he did not cook in Banteay Ampil district, Oddar Meanchey province
(Oddar Meanchey): A man used a corner stick to beat his father, causing serious injuries because he was angry that his father did not cook for him. This incident happened on the night of October 26, 2020 in Kork Key village, Beng commune, Banteay Ampil district, Oddar Meanchey province.
Banteay Ampil district police told Fresh News on the afternoon of October 27, 2020 that under the command of Brigadier General Huot Sothy, the provincial police commissioner, the suspect was arrested by the specialized police force after causing the violence. .
The perpetrator was named Thien Phal, 33 years old, while the victim's father was named Dok Thien, 68 years old, living in Kork Key village, Beng commune, Banteay Ampil district, Oddar Meanchey province.
The cause of the violence was that the suspect was angry with his father for not cooking, so he hit him with a wooden stick, injuring three eyebrows. The suspects are now in charge of building a case to be sent for legal action.
