(Phnom Penh): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, said that the Ministry of Tourism is currently working to transform the Kovid-19 crisis into an opportunity to improve the quality of existing tourism products and create new tourism products to promote domestic tourism and tourism. Promote tourism safety internationally.
Minister Thong Khon made this statement during a meeting to review the work results for the first nine months of 2020 and the direction for implementation in the fourth quarter of 2020 during the crisis phase on the afternoon of October 26, 2020 at Office of the Ministry of Tourism.
After the meeting, the Minister told reporters that during the Kovid-19 crisis, the Ministry of Tourism is working to promote domestic tourism with the implementation of tourism safety rules and guidelines of the Ministry of Health. He said that no matter what the circumstances, the opening of the local tourism movement could not deviate from the introduction of these tourist safety.
He added that only 36% of tourism businesses have participated in the campaign, which seems to be a race. The Ministry of Tourism will award the label to any business that responds to this safety rule, but only 16% of the businesses that have received this label, so the Ministry of Tourism will continue to work hard to promote this competition.
Along with the implementation of tourism safety rules, the Ministry of Tourism is also working to improve the quality of sanitation, hospitality and other services.
Mr. Thong Khon said, "We take this opportunity to improve the quality of tourism and hospitality services to promote domestic tourism, even though we have not yet received international tourists. "Receiving local tourists is an opportunity to improve the quality and create new tourism products."
What is the strategy of the Royal Government is implementing is to protect jobs in the tourism sector to ensure that employees working in this sector remain stable and stable.
