(Siem Reap): In the afternoon of October 27, 2020, on behalf of Samdech Techo Prime Minister and Chairman of the Mine Authority, Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Vice President of the Mine Authority, presided over the closing ceremony of the workshop to summarize the results of 2020 and Raise the work direction for 2021 within the framework of the Mine Authority.
The workshop was chaired by General Sem Sovanny, Second Vice President of the Mines Authority and attended by Mr. Prum Sopheak Mongkul, Secretary General of the Mines Authority, leaders of civil servants, staff of the Mines Authority, leaders of the National Center for Peacekeeping Management. Demining and Remnants of War (NPMEC) Representative of UNDP and the DFID-NPA project.
He added that with the results of peace, the Royal Government of Cambodia has considered demining work as an important part of contributing to peacekeeping.
In addition to the outstanding achievements in the field of mines in Cambodia and to implement the vision statement and mission statement for the mine sector in Cambodia to achieve more success, on behalf of Samdech Techo, President of the Mines Authority, the Senior Minister introduced 10 principles. Of the work ahead to all leaders, civil servants, staff of the Mine Authority as follows:
* First: Continue to implement the National Strategic Plan for Mine Action 2018-2025 to achieve the Royal Government's Rectangular Strategy and achieve the goal of sustainable development towards a mine-free Cambodia by 2025.
* Second, continue to seek support and collaboration with GICHD, the NPA, as well as other stakeholders to ensure that the mine database system is fully responsive to the needs of use and analysis, and to provide operator guidance. The need for timely data transmission and quality assurance.
* Third: Continue to promote and promote gender mainstreaming in the field of mine action, as well as work to help people with disabilities due to landmines more strongly in accordance with the strategic plan of the Royal Government.
* Fourth, to prepare a three-year action plan for the mine sector 2021-2023, as well as guidelines on demining-affected villages to promote the implementation of the National Strategic Plan for Mine Action 2018-2025 achieved as expected.
* Fifth: Continue to work hard to find ways to strengthen humanitarian deminers.
* Sixth: Seek further cooperation with the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces to resolve demining work along the border as soon as possible.
* Seventh: Seek financial and technical support from donors to successfully implement data verification and research projects.
* Eighth: Promote the establishment of a library at the Mine Authority as soon as possible so that staff officers can study and gain more comprehensive knowledge in the field of mine action.
* Ninth: Prepare a manual on administration to facilitate daily work.
* 10th: Orientation in the work of the department and in each department to ensure a transparent and efficient workflow.
Tomorrow, the whole workshop will participate in building the strength of group solidarity, closer communication through joint trips, eating solidarity, discussing life issues, social issues and general issues. To find out more about each other's minds after being tired of working for the past 10 months.
