When the Apollo astronauts first returned from the moon in 1969, it was supposed to be a dry, waterless place. In particular, in the last 20 years, water in the form of ice has been found by scientists in large craters that have never known sunlight at both poles of the moon, especially in the polar regions. Gems.
In particular, the question of how water is stored on the surface of the moon is also an interesting question. Water can form in the moonlight, which is formed by the intense heat of asteroids hitting the surface of the moon. Another possibility is that the water may be between the moon's surface and not exposed to sunlight. In this case, the water is easier to extract than the first possibility.
The next SOFIA flight will continue to monitor the presence of water in other light-sensitive areas on the moon to help scientists better understand. In addition to finding water in light-sensitive areas, new research has found that there may be frozen water in small pits that are not exposed to light and have colder temperatures on the moon's surface than previously thought. Also.
Cambodia exports more than 200,000 tons of rubber, earning more than 270 million dollars in the first 9 months of this year!
In the past nine months, the average price of rubber was $ 1,292 per tonne, the report said. Therefore, the revenue from rubber exports in the first nine months of 2020 is more than 270 million US dollars.
According to the General Department of Rubber, Cambodia currently has 402,313 hectares of rubber products, of which 290,007 hectares, or 72 percent, and 112,306 hectares, or 28 percent, are rubber plantations.
