The Ministry of Education issued a directive on the opening of the third phase of public schools from November 2 (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports on October 27, 2020 One on the reopening of public schools (public schools) in the third phase, starting from November 2 until the end of December 2020.
The Ministry of Education also recommends that all kindergartens and early childhood education facilities be fully operational, teaching and learning at all levels, five days a week, with a limit of 25 children per class.
In particular, the implementation of the curriculum for the ninth and twelfth grade secondary schools must continue as in the second phase, while the seventh, eighth, tenth and 11th grades must be taught and taught three days a week. More than 30 people will practice mixed learning, focusing on at least 6 core subjects in accordance with the actual situation of the number of classrooms and the number of teachers.
