The announcement to the United States was made by the Chinese Embassy in Colombo, Sri Lanka, shortly after the Chinese diplomatic mission received information that Mike Pompeo was visiting India to discuss strategies with the country. This is the second largest in Asia against China, the number one power in the region.
"We strongly oppose the United States taking the opportunity of a foreign ministerial visit to sow and intervene in Sino-Sri Lankan relations and coercion and intimidation," the statement said. "Threaten Sri Lanka." The Chinese embassy also stressed that the traditional relationship between China and Sri Lanka dates back more than 2,000 years, with no third party able to break it down.
US Secretary of State Mike Pompeo and US Secretary of Defense Mark Esper began their visit to India on Monday and Tuesday. During the visit, a number of agreements were reached, particularly on the defense sector, including the sale of military equipment and the sharing of intelligence from military satellites between the United States and India.
