(Phnom Penh): After taking measures to pump water from the New World Borey in Trapeang Thleung 4 village in Sangkat Choam Chao I, Khan Por Sen Chey, the water level has dropped from the Borey so far.
But all that is left is the waste and dirty water on the streets, and the Phnom Penh authorities have used all their strength to clean up all the waste and dirty water on the streets in this Borey from now on. Also spray disinfectant for the well-being of the people.
On that occasion, Mr. Khuong Sreng also appealed to all residents who have been staying in Borey Piphop Thmey, Project 2, Trapeang Thleung 4 Village, to cooperate with Phnom Penh authorities to clean and restore sewage. Available on the streets after the water has receded.
Mr. Khuong Sreng also ordered the Phnom Penh Municipal Public Works Department to replace the small pipes, which were blocked by some residents, while officials confirmed that the flooding was also caused by this problem.
It should be noted that in the past, after heavy rainfall due to the effects of low pressure and storms from September 1 to October 17, 2020, some areas in Phnom Penh were flooded and More than 10,000 families have been affected by the floods.
During this morning's campaign, Mr. Khuong Sreng ordered more fire trucks to help spray and clean, including spraying and cleaning with soap, using a total of about 20 vehicles in That is the car of the Department of Public Works, the car of the Capital Police and the car of the military as well.
Please be informed that the people living in Borey Piphop Thmey, Trapeang Thleung, also suffered severe flooding of about 1,000 houses out of 3,113 flats.
Ministry of Environment Holds Consultation Workshop on 4th National Environmental Situation Report
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of October 27, 2020, the leaders of the Ministry of Environment, relevant ministries, institutions, relevant units, universities, national and international organizations in charge of work related to the environment and natural resources met in a workshop to finalize the draft. Fourth National Environmental Situation Report at Cambodiana Hotel.
On that occasion, Mr. Chuob Paris, Director General of the General Department of Knowledge and Environmental Information of the Ministry of Environment, thanked all the stakeholder working groups, which were the driving force behind the richness of the report, with easy access to in-depth analysis. Scientific and reliable.
"This is the fourth time we have done this, but this is the first time we have done it internationally, because we have national and international advisors involved in making the report available internationally," he said.
He hopes that after the report is released to relevant institutions, partner organizations use this data as a basis to avoid the use of different data. In addition, the report will be published in two languages, Khmer and English.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra continued that the environment is a multidisciplinary and multidisciplinary work, which in this sense requires the participation of ideas, opinions, as well as: sharing data and information for the preparation of reports on the national environmental situation.
Please note that the Ministry of Environment has completed the preparation of this national environmental situation report and has already implemented this work three times. The General Department of Environmental Knowledge and Information has partnered with the United Nations Development Program in Cambodia and the Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations in Cambodia to prepare the fourth National Environmental Situation Report.
