Ministry of Interior Establishes Anti-Drug Committee and Joint HIV / AIDS Committee on Local Drug and HIV / AIDS
(Phnom Penh): Two other committees of the newly formed Ministry of Interior will work together to fight drugs and HIV / AIDS across the country to promote the policy of safe villages, communes / communes and avoid this disease. Based on a high sense of responsibility and efficiency.
With this, Mr. Kao Khon Dara added: "In the fight against HIV / STI, we have focused on education, prevention and care only on the National Police, but from now on we need to pay attention to All officials of all kinds within the framework of the entire Ministry of Interior.
According to Lt. Gen. Yuthea, Deputy Secretary General of the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs and Chairman of the Secretariat of the Anti-Drug Committee of the Ministry of Interior, the fight against drugs and the fight against HIV / AIDS without the participation of the public No, it can not be successful, so the public must join with all relevant authorities and officials for these works to be successful.
At the same time, Lt. Gen. Yuthea also called on the people to cooperate with local authorities to crack down on drugs in a timely manner. And to continue to educate their children about the effects of drugs and understanding of HIV infection, if a child uses drugs, take him to the treatment center, do not let him continue to use drugs.
