(Kampong Thom): Mrs. Khuon Khun Dy, Senator, Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Kampong Thom Province, and Mrs. and Mr. Oknha Kuy Leang Ky, as well as the monks of the Acharya Committee of Wat Kampong Svay Pagoda in Kampong Svay Village, Kampong Svay Commune, Kampong Svay District, Kampong Thom Province, initiated the ceremony. Solidarity Kathina to collect donations for monks to build a bridge across Stung Sen, Stung Sen City, Kampong Thom Province, which is planned to cost more than $ 400,000.
During a donation ceremony for monks on the afternoon of October 26, 2020, Ms. Khuon Khundy stated that the Solidarity Charity Fund collected $ 187,771.
She said that because the country is peaceful, the national economy is growing, people have the opportunity to celebrate from the sincerity of the people, businessmen, government officials, forces and people in some provinces to build.
At the same time, Ms. Khuon Khun Dy also thanked Mr. Oknha, Ladies and Gentlemen, Government Officials, Forces, Departments, All Institutions, and Grandmothers, Grandfathers and Buddhists who came from all provinces and cities and all who participated in this Solidarity Charity. Bring suffixes to build achievements in this Kampong Thom pagoda.
She also said that the Kathina is a contribution to the promotion of Buddhism, the state religion, and this is to show the next generation to see the celebration of Buddhism, which is a good tradition of Cambodia. We will join in building the country with the Royal Government for development as well.
Mr. Im Chung, Chairman of the Pagoda Committee, said that the construction of this bridge is in collaboration with the Buddhists with generous force, since 2018, and the construction of the stone bridge is 151.2 meters long, 4.50 meters wide and 8 meters high. Meters, with a project costing more than $ 400,000.
He added that the construction of this bridge is to make it easier for students to go to school and people to transport agricultural products from one side to the other or from one district to another. The new bridge will be completed by the end of February 2021.
