(Phnom Penh): The bridge across the Bassac River connecting Koh Pich to Koh Nora satellite city and from Koh Nora to National Road No. 1 officially opened this morning, October 26, 2020. The groundbreaking ceremony for another historic bridge across the river in Phnom Penh was presided over by Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Currently, traveling on National Road No. 1 across the Monivong Bridge from Chbar Ampov to Phnom Penh is often congested. Especially morning and evening trips.
Ms. Yoeun Ratana said that every time she gets stuck, she feels anxious, and this blockage leads to a waste of time and even to lose gas.
MP Pen Leakena is currently living in Koh Nora village, Niroth commune, Chbar Ampov district. This girl has to travel from Chbar Ampov to learn Chinese at Toun Fa School in Sangkat Toul Svay Prey I, Khan Chamkar Mon, Phnom Penh every day.
Both bridges, once completed, are expected to contribute to facilitating people's travel from Phnom Penh to National Road No. 1. In particular, reduce congestion at the Monivong Bridge.
Residents of Chbar Ampov district, who used to be tired of traveling to and from Phnom Penh due to traffic congestion, have expressed their admiration for the construction of a bridge connecting Koh Pich to Koh Nora and from Koh Nora to National Road No. 1. What they expect is that it will help ease traffic congestion.
Ms. M. Pen Leakena said that after the appearance of this bridge, the journey to study Chinese at Toun Fa School will not be difficult and will save time. "I think building a bridge helps us a lot in traveling, saves us time, saves money, and makes it easier to travel far and near."
The people of Nora Island feel the same way. They saw that without peace, there would have been no bridges and other achievements in Phnom Penh.
During the groundbreaking ceremony for the bridge across the Bassac River connecting Koh Pich to Koh Nora and from Koh Nora to National Road No. 1, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also praised and highly appreciated Duke Pong Khieu Se for his important contribution to Developed in Phnom Penh.
