On that occasion, the Governor of Preah Vihear Province urged the Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport to repair this road as soon as possible to facilitate the passage of our people.
Separately, Mr. Samleang Try said that the road that is being repaired is 13 kilometers long, an ancient road connecting Phnom Dek village, Romney commune, through Poem Phal village, Svay Damnak village, to Ranasir commune, Sangkum Thmei district.
He stated that the distance from National Road No. 62 from Phnom Dek village to Ranasir commune, Sangkum Thmei district, Preah Khan temple is 36 kilometers, but now we only repair 13 kilometers to Svay Damnak village.
Mr. Samleang Try stated that under the guidance of Senior Minister Sun Chanthol and Mr. Prak Sovann, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, the Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport cooperated with the technical team of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport. Repair this road immediately to make it available to the people.
The Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Preah Vihear Province stated that the budget for repairing this road is a reserve fund for emergency flood work, which was received from the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to the Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport to Do emergency work.
