Kratie Fisheries Administration and WWF jointly manage and protect Mekong dolphins, so far nearly 100 dolphins are present in Cambodia's Mekong River
According to the results confirmed by the director of WWF Cambodia, the results of the dolphin census in 2017, Cambodia has about 92 dolphins. This is the first increase of 15% in the last 20 years of conservation, compared with 80 in the 2015 census.
The results of the 2020 dolphin census, which were officially released by the National Fisheries Administration last week, show that the total number of dolphins in Cambodia in 2020 is similar to the number of dolphins in the year. In 2017, the number was about 89.
