(Kampong Chhnang): On October 26, 2020, a delegation from the Ministry of Economy and Finance and related institutions visited and inspected the construction process of Phnom Chamray Military Police Training Center in Kampong Chhnang Province to evaluate the use of state budget. Dropped since the initial construction process.
The Phnom Chamray Gendarmerie Training Center covers an area of more than 5,000 hectares, and the construction process so far has achieved the planned plan and will be completed in 2022. According to the plan, the center could spend tens of millions of dollars.
It should be noted that this visit was also attended by Mr. Keo Rattanak, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of Electricite du Cambodge, General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander and Commander of the National Gendarmerie, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander-in-Chief and Commander of the Army and Tycoon Ly Hour, as well as many other stakeholders.
Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, led the delegation to inspect the construction process. Standards also set.
Mr. Vongsey Visoth expressed his happiness when he saw the construction process of this large training center as planned. However, he could not confirm what percentage of the process has been completed, as there are up to seven different training facilities in the center.
Accompanying the Prime Minister Vongsey Visoth said, "As a fundraiser and as a helper, we are all very happy with today's achievements. "We have found that what we have spent on the construction of this center is really satisfactory and efficient to spend, and the construction is done according to plan, high quality, good standards."
He added that the training center will help strengthen the capabilities of all troops, because this location is not only for the Royal Gendarmerie, but for the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces as a whole. In the future, the center will be a major training ground in Cambodia that can help the army become more capable of carrying out national defense and rescue missions.
According to Mr. Vongsey Visoth so far (from the date of opening the construction site for 4 years), the state budget is more than 10 million dollars, but in 2021 plans to spend about 3 million dollars to complete the construction. The shooting range is real, but the amount of money to complete the construction is much more. He added that many philanthropists have also donated money to build the center.
It should be informed that the infrastructure of Phnom Chamray Gendarmerie Training Center started construction in 2013 and according to the planned plan, this construction is scheduled to be completed in 2022.
The Phnom Chamray Gendarmerie Training Center is also preparing to host the upcoming ASEAN Land Rifle Meeting (AARM) and the technical team is working hard to build the main structures in This training center as well.
So far, the technical team of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) has been working hard to coordinate all matters to expedite the signing of the bilateral agreement (Cambodia-China). Planned.
Lt. Gen. Phuong Siphin, Chief of the Technical Working Group of the Royal Cambodian Gendarmerie Engineering Project, said that the locations to be presented to the delegation were: the actual firing range, the ammunition depot, the weapons depot, the second water treatment plant, and the technical logistics depot. Construction site of multi-technical exhibition center, office building, reservoir, forum, study of trainees and accommodation building.
The third ceasefire failed! Azerbaijan and Armenia continue bloody fighting on Monday
Armenia and Azerbaijan have twice agreed on humanitarian ceasefires under the auspices of Russia and France, but they have also failed. The Azerbaijani Ministry of Foreign Affairs claimed that the Armenian army fired shells into the city of Terter and several nearby villages, while the Armenians countered that the Azerbaijani army fired several shots at its bases on the battlefield.
According to AFP, just as the new ceasefire took effect on Sunday night, Monday, gunfire erupted and smoke billowed through the air. However, there were no immediate reports of injuries or deaths.
