(Banteay Meanchey): Major General Pich Vanna, Director of the Cambodia-Thailand Border Liaison Office, on October 26, 2020, led a working group to distribute donations from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, to flood victims. 70 families in Tuol Prasat village, Sangkat Poipet and Seila Khmer village in Ochrov district, Banteay Meanchey province.
Lt. Gen. Pich Vanna said that natural disasters, floods and floods from Thailand have affected the homes of tens of thousands of families affected by the floods, but they have received donations from Samdech Techo Hun Sen National, provincial, municipal, district and many other philanthropists.
