500 Families Affected by Flood in Kampong Thom Province
The distribution ceremony for the victims took place on October 25, 2020 in front of Stong District Hall under the presidency of Kampong Thom Provincial Governor Mr. Sok Loo and Mrs. Club as well.
Stong District Governor Neth Sary said that during the floods, 8039 houses were affected in seven communes along the Stong River. Rainfed rice affected 4,454 hectares, completely damaged 991 hectares and caused 3 deaths by drowning.
He added that although the water situation has not decreased, the people affected by the floods are warm, with the leadership of the Royal Government at all levels to pay attention and rescue in time. In fact, today, 500 families affected by the floods will receive emergency aid, leaders and philanthropists.
"On behalf of the district administration and on behalf of the people of Stoung district, I would like to express my deepest gratitude to all the philanthropists who have always taken great care of the well-being and livelihood of the people at the local level," he said. "People all over Stong district."
On the occasion, Ms. Tbeng Phally, President of the Rotary Club of Chaktomuk Phnom Penh, said that due to the continuous rain in Cambodia, some provinces have caused severe floods and people's biological resources are lacking.
Therefore, Roth Thary immediately started donating materials to alleviate the hardships of 500 affected families, each family received: 10 kg of white rice, 1 box of noodles, 5 cans of canned fish, 1 can of salt Kg, 1 bottle of fish sauce, 1 blanket, 1 mosquito net, 1 bar of soap, 1 bottle of fruit juice.
Rotary Club is an international organization formed from a group of companies about 100 years old with a mission to do humanitarian work to help society in the fields of education, hospitals, baby and mother care, clean water, community. Poor and poor orphans.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces the temporary commissioning of the Chom Chao flyover from today (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, on October 26, 2020. Temporarily the Chom Chao flyover from today after the construction process is completed to reduce traffic congestion and facilitate the movement of people.
The announcement of the subway was made on the occasion that Samdech presided over the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of a cable-stayed concrete bridge across the Bassac River connecting Phnom Penh from Koh Pich to the satellite city of Koh Nora and from Koh Nora towards National Road No. 1 in Sangkat Niroth, Khan Chbar Ampov this morning, October 26, 2020.
Along with the announcement of the temporary opening of the subway, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also emphasized that the people can also use the subway area as a tourist area, some children may be parents who want to see The long tunnel is another new achievement of Cambodia under the shadow of peace that Cambodia has achieved.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also instructed the telephone company to connect its service network in the subway of Chom Chao, so that when people come to visit or travel there, it should not be disconnected while in other countries. Already done this work. Therefore, let the phone companies go to study to see if it is possible to put their service network in this subway or not.
At the same time, Samdech Techo also confirmed that according to his observation, in the Council of Ministers, 95% of the cellcard system of Duke Kith Meng is already used. Not only that, Cellcard has relationships with foreign phone companies that can provide easy access to Cambodia.
Please note that the flyover and subway at the Chaom Chao roundabout use a construction budget of 22 million US dollars, the construction period is 30 months, from June 29, 2018 to December 29, 2020. The contractor is the Overseas Cambodian Investment Company (OCIC).
