At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised and urged the Phnom Penh Capital Administration to continue to develop according to this formula to take palm leaves and pack sugar. The Prime Minister said that the development of Koh Pich, the satellite city of Chroy Changvar and the city of Koh Nora has taken advantage of the construction of roads, bridges and other structures in Phnom Penh.
Samdech Techo Prime Minister said that when the two new bridges are completed, the traffic situation on the boulevard near the Independence Monument, especially in front of Samdech's house, including traffic in the city of Koh Pich, etc. will be busier because of the people. Travel back and forth, including relatives traveling to Kandal, Prey Veng and Svay Rieng. At the same time, these two bridges will also help reduce congestion at the Monivong Bridge.
The first bridge is a 60-meter-long, 21-meter-wide concrete bridge connecting National Road No. 1 to Koh Nora Development Project, with three lanes for vehicles and one lane for pedestrians at a cost of 1.6 million. US $ 12 months to build this bridge, built by Cambodian engineers and built by 100% Cambodian company.
Bridge 2: A cable-stayed concrete bridge connecting the Koh Nora Development Zone to the Koh Pich satellite city, 824 meters long and 24.50 meters wide, with three lanes for vehicles and one lane for pedestrians. The bridge is up to 8 meters high in the rainy season and can be navigated, with a construction cost of 35 months and a budget of $ 38 million. The bridge was designed by a Chinese company and built by a Cambodian-Chinese joint venture.
