(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia plans to introduce a social security system on occupational risk for individuals in the public sector in early 2021 to ensure security and income in the event of occupational hazards, occupational accidents or occupational diseases.
In the weekly special guest program of Fresh News TV, Mr. John Narith, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Secretary General of the National Council for Social Protection stated that "In the 4th meeting on September 29, 2020 The National Council has decided to respect the request of the head of the Royal Government to implement the social security system on occupational risk soon may start from 2021 onwards.
Mr. John Narith said that in order to benefit from the social security system in terms of occupational risk, individuals in the public sector must register with the Occupational Risk Registry with the National Social Security Fund (NSSF) and pay regime contributions. Social Security in Occupational Risk. For individuals in the public sector who receive social security in the form of occupational risk, all the burden of contribution is borne by the state, not the pay cut.
