NEC Secretary-General: Skills training for election officials is a must
(Prey Veng): On the occasion of the opening of the training course on "Effectiveness of Training, Education, Dissemination of Information, Submission, Receipt and Resolution of Complaints in the Election Process" to NEC Civil Servants on October 26, 2020 NEC Secretary-General Tep Nytha said that vocational training for election officials was a must.
He said that this is the second time that the NEC has organized this training course in order to strengthen the capacity of NEC civil servants, especially the leadership of the Capital and Provincial Secretariat to organize the election process. Vote to prepare to participate in the upcoming election to be successful in accordance with the laws, regulations and procedures of the NEC.
He stated that this is another new step in the framework of the reform of the NEC to strengthen the capacity of NEC civil servants in the field of responsibility to ensure high efficiency of work through Train NEC officials at all levels to acquire sufficient knowledge, skills and information to carry out their work successfully.
At the same time, he strongly believes that all NEC civil servants will gain more new knowledge as a basis for better performance. Electoral management is a complex organizational process that requires sufficient resources, technical officers, and a clear understanding of election affairs in the electoral body. Not to be missed.
He added that after completing the training, all leaders of the NEC Secretariat will review the amendments to regulations and procedures and codes of conduct for political parties to amend before reaching the submission. All 11 stakeholders to review and to prepare for the work in 2021.
Please be informed that this training course is held for 4 days from October 26 to 29, 2020 at the Cambodian Red Cross branch in Prey Veng province with about 120 participants who are officials from the office. The NEC and the 25 provincial capitals.
