Thousands of Thai protesters return to protest after three days deadline for Prayuth to step down
BANGKOK, Oct. 25 (Xinhua) - Thousands of people rallied again in central Bangkok on Sunday, the first time since Prime Minister Prayuth Chan-o-cha ignored the protests. Their three-day deadline for the prime minister to step down expired on Saturday. This is according to the release by CNA on Sunday, October 25, 2020.
Sunday's demonstration was also the first major rally after Prayuth Chan-o-cha announced the repeal of the "state of emergency" and other relevant regulations, which in the past had only angered protesters. Well.
The prime minister's office posted a note on Twitter stating that Prayut would not step down and that the crisis should be discussed in parliament, which will hold a special session next Monday and Tuesday next week.
Last week, Prayuth issued an appeal to allow parliament to find a solution to the political crisis, and he also announced the cancellation of the state of emergency he had declared a week ago. But the protesters are still not satisfied, they have announced three days for Mr. Prayuth to step down as Prime Minister, otherwise he will face a bigger demonstration.
