In addition, General Sem Sovanny also reminded all officers who go out on missions and are carrying out humanitarian missions abroad, please take care of your health, follow the instructions of the Ministry of Health, the instructions of UN officials in In the area of fulfilling its mission and following the instructions of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Ministry of National Defense on measures to prevent and prevent Kovid-19 disease.
In addition, General Sem Sovanny also instructed the Gendarmerie to go on missions abroad to preserve the beautiful traditions of Cambodia to enhance the honor of Cambodia on the international stage. In particular, be able to love and care for each other like brothers and sisters in all circumstances.
It should be noted that since 2006, Cambodia has sent nearly 5,000 troops, including more than 200 women, to participate in UN missions.
In addition, on May 29, 2020, a Cambodian peacekeeper died after contracting Kovid 19 in Mali. The soldier who died was 63-year-old General Tos Savy, a resident of Chong Boeng village, Makak commune, Ang Snoul district, Kandal province.
So far, Cambodia has a total of 787 five peacekeeping missions under the auspices of the United Nations, including Lebanon, Sudan, South Sudan, Mali and Central Africa. All of these Blue Hat forces make Cambodia the second largest donor of peacekeeping forces in ASEAN.
