Key remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of the bridge across the Bassac River connecting Koh Pich to Koh Nora, from Koh Nora to National Road No. 1
On the occasion of the opening of the bridge construction site, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also gave a speech for more than an hour. The following are the main contents of Samdech:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the achievement of the bridge across the new river in Phnom Penh will contribute significantly to reducing traffic congestion on National Road No. 1 at the base of the Monivong Bridge.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the area of Phnom Penh has now increased to nearly 700 square kilometers, and many areas of Kandal province have been cut into Phnom Penh.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech was very tired of not wanting to have buildings taller than the Council of Ministers or taller than other historical buildings, such as Wat Phnom, taller than Sakyamuni Stupa. Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that because of such boredom, during 2004, Samdech announced who built the tallest building, Samdech handed over the medal.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised OCIC for participating in the development of the construction sector in Cambodia, including the development of the Koh Pich Center, the airport, the satellite city of Chroy Changva, and now on Koh Nora. Samdech Techo considered that this is an important contribution to the Royal Government in the development of the country.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the current situation of the people is clear that there are still people who are poor but not as poor as the country after the liberation in 1979.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the private sector plays an important role in the context of the Kovid 19 epidemic. Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in the meantime, Samdech must make sure that these companies do not close during the Kovid 19 crisis.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that if private companies close, it will cause Cambodians to lose their jobs. Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that so far about 300,000 Cambodians have lost their jobs.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Water Festival is not celebrated, but the moon worship ceremony is still held and the holiday is still practiced.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in the first half of 2020, Cambodia has a surplus of about 200 million dollars. But for the second half, income and expenses are the same.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that although the 19 cases of Kovid in Cambodia are stagnant, it must not be neglected, but caution must be exercised. Samdech Techo noted that in Myanmar, at first, it was similar to Cambodia, but now it has increased significantly.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Phnom Penh must continue to develop according to the formula of palm leaves wrapped in palm sugar. Samdech Techo said that the development of Koh Pich, Koh Nora took advantage of this to build other buildings in Phnom Penh.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen warns Mr. Ho Van about planning to order a demonstration at the Chinese Embassy.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech was tired of some foreigners and Cambodians who accused the presence of Chinese troops in Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen questioned foreigners about the Chinese military presence in Cambodia and what they wanted, as 1970 pushed Cambodia into the flames of war.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen broke the voice of Mr. Ho Van ordering his group to protest at the Chinese Embassy.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech currently uses 18 mobile phones.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that climate change and the flooding of the Mekong River should not be blamed on Cambodia because it is a global issue.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the floods damaged national roads, trails and dams. Samdech Techo instructed the Minister of Public Works and Transport, the Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, the Minister of Rural Development and the Minister of Agriculture not to wait for the evaluation from the various departments, to assign the Secretary of State to directly evaluate.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the four ministers must take immediate action to repair and connect the damaged roads and bridges to the people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen noted that the Minister of Rural Development does not seem to be seen in rural areas.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the main solution for the flood victims is to create opportunities for them to replant.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen has ordered an urgent study on the impact of the people and issued an urgent solution. Samdech Techo stressed that no matter how much money is needed, it must be dropped to solve.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he will wait to see the impact of the four ministers. Samdech Techo added that if the Minister takes slow action, Samdech will go down directly and wait to see what the Minister will do?
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the construction of 38 roads in Siem Reap at a cost of 150 million dollars will open on November 16, 2020.
