(Kampong Thom): At the same time as Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, announced to provide 100 kg of rice seeds per family and all kinds of 6 crops to the people affected by the flood, the Governor of Kampong Thom Province, Mr. Sok Lou urged all people to be ready to grow crops after the low water season.
Speaking at the distribution ceremony on October 24, 2020 in Stung Sen City, Mr. Sok Lou confirmed that the flood situation in Kampong Thom province has affected the people of the nine districts, causing damage to various crops and Rainfed rice to be harvested in November and December.
Observing the difficulties and shortage of rice seeds and other mixed crops, Samdech Prakas will provide 100 kg of rice seeds per family and 6 other vegetable varieties for replanting. This is also the attention of the Royal Government to support the family economy to the general population, not only in Kampong Thom, Samdech will provide throughout the country to the affected people in 2020.
The Governor of Kampong Thom Province requested the local authorities and all relevant parties to go to the local level and study the number of people's needs in order to report to the Royal Government in accordance with the vision and guidance of Samdech Techo to facilitate The hardships of the people were real.
