Legal Awareness: Contract Termination
(Phnom Penh): In principle, a contract is formed by expressing the will of the parties through a corresponding request and consultation and will establish mutual rights and obligations. However, in the event that one party of the contract expresses the will, with a disability or by reason of its ability to comprehend, or by the wrongdoing of the other party, which is detrimental to the interests of that party.
Last week, the Legal Awareness Program raised the topic of contract termination and contract annulment, so for this week, FRESH NEWS Legal Awareness Program, in collaboration with the Cambodian Lawyers for International Cooperation, would like to present Take the topic of "cancellation of contract" to present to the people, students as follows:
According to the Civil Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia, the other party who has suffered the benefits of entering into a contract with a disability or contract made by an incompetent person may cancel the contract.
In this sense, a contract cannot be effective if it is made improperly as required by law or a contract that results in a loss of the interests of any party, and that party or related person may Exercise the right to cancel the contract.
The revocable action is valid until you have the right to cancel the revocation, and after that the revocation is considered null and void, but the cancellation shall be made by way of notification to the parties. The other side and will be effective from the moment the news reaches the other side.
According to the Civil Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia, the reasons for termination of a contract are two (2) conditions: (1) in the case where the contract is made by an incompetent person (a person who has no will or ability to act) and (2) In case the contract is made with a defect in expressing the will.
2 * Termination of contract due to a defect in the will: In the case where the contract is made by a defect in the party: the parties to the contract can cancel the contract. Defects of expression of will include cases of mistakenly entering into a contract, fraud, misinformation, breach of status, threats and grounds for excessive profiteering.
Mistakes: A party may terminate a contract for reasons of confusion only if the misunderstanding is based on key points or points that the parties consider important in the contract and the other party is aware of or may be aware of. This confusion or in case both parties have the same confusion. However, the termination of a contract by mistake cannot be claimed by a third party if the third party is honest and innocent.
Fraud: A party who has entered into a contract through the fraud of the other party or from a third party may cancel the contract, but only in the case of fraud committed by a third party may the contract be terminated unless the other party is aware of it. Or be aware of that scam.
False information: In the event that one party of the contract expresses its will by believing the false information from the other party after realizing that the information is false, that party can cancel the contract with a reason to show goodwill. There is a disability. However, the termination of the contract due to false information cannot be claimed by a third party if the third party is honest and innocent.
Violation of the situation: At the time of entering into the contract, if one party to the contract improperly uses the position in which he or she prioritizes the other party economically or socially, or improperly uses another situation that the other party does not Can not counter, the other party can cancel the contract. Termination of a contract for reasons of violation of the status of a party cannot be claimed by a third party if the third party is honest and innocent.
Intimidation: A party who enters into a contract under threat from the other party or by a third party may terminate the contract due to a disability.
According to the Civil Code, the right to terminate a contract shall be terminated within 3 years from the date of its becoming a ratifier, however, after 10 years from the date of action. The right to cancel the contract was also revoked.
In summary, the termination of a contract is a legal right to protect the other party who has voluntarily expressed a disability or to a contract made by a disabled person that leads to a loss of interest to the party or the disabled person. That.
In this case, the cancellation shall be made by the party who has expressed the will to the disabled person or the person who has the right to cancel as determined by law for the disabled person and those who have the right to cancel.
The termination of this contract shall take place within the period prescribed by law and after the parties have exercised their right to cancel, the contract shall be deemed to be null and void from the beginning and all acts of the contract which have been applied shall be revoked. Repeat.
