(Phnom Penh): The "Draft Law on Finance for Management 2021" or "National Budget Law 2021" was fully approved by the Council of Ministers in a plenary session chaired by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister Of Cambodia this week.
The National Budget Law 2021 was issued by the Royal Government of Cambodia, stating that it plans to spend 30,491,336 million riels, equivalent to approximately 7,500 million dollars, a decrease of 1.9% compared to the 2020 budget law.
For staff costs in 2021, which include basic salaries, severance pay, benefits, bonuses and social allowances for leaders of public institutions, permanent staff, contract staff, is projected at 8,565,574 million Riels, equivalent to approximately 21 $ 7 million, down 0.3 percent from 2020.
In 2021, the minimum (minimum) salaries of civil servants and members of the armed forces will be kept at 2020 to save money for the Kovid-19 epidemic and the 2020 monsoon floods.
National capital expenditure is planned at 13,044,495 million riels, equivalent to approximately 3,208 million US dollars, a decrease of 0.1% compared to 2020 in order to support the continued implementation of the three-year rolling investment program 2021-2023. In particular, the rehabilitation and promotion of economic growth.
Non-tax revenue is projected at 2,185,983 million riels, equivalent to approximately $ 537 million. In 2021, the Royal Government did not introduce new taxes or increase tax rates.
Please be informed that in the National Budget Law 2020, the Royal Government plans to spend about 8,223 million dollars, but due to the disease of Kovid 19, the Royal Government has reduced the second expenditure, saving more than 900 million dollars. By 2020, the government plans to raise $ 6,496 million.
The 2021 budget is considered by the Royal Government to be an effective tool that can help the Royal Government respond to both challenges and risks, both inside and outside the country, in order to ensure the socio-economic stability of Cambodia and protect the lives of the people from The Kovid-19 pandemic, as well as the restoration and promotion of economic growth after the Kovid-19 crisis has subsided.
