(Svay Rieng): Mr. Nguon Meng Tech, Director General of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, stated that the preparation and publication of the Svay Rieng Investment Guide Book will be able to cooperate to implement other projects effectively.
He said this at the official announcement ceremony of cooperation in the preparation and publication of the Svay Rieng Investment Guide on the afternoon of October 24, 2020. The ceremony was attended by Mr. Oknha Sok Rado, President of Svay Rieng Chamber of Commerce, as well as many members of the Chamber of Commerce.
Mr. Oknha continued that Svay Rieng is a potential province with a geographical location on the Cambodia-Vietnam border, which is a favorable factor for cross-border transportation and rich in special economic zones. And now there are many factories and are running their production in various sectors such as garments and garments, pigments, cassava, rice mills, bicycles, motorcycles, construction and tourism.
He added that there are many other potential sectors that investors are interested in and should study investment possibilities, including food processing, light industry, agriculture and hospitality.
The favorable geographical location combined with labor, electricity, affordable prices and infrastructure development are making Svay Rieng an investment and business destination, especially the Phnom Penh Bavet Expressway project.
"Svay Rieng has many other investment potentials that require us to study, research and compile, so the preparation and publication of the Svay Rieng Investment Guide is very important for national and international business to use as a document," he said. "Guidelines for doing business and finding investment partners. Publishing guides and providing complete and targeted data."
The tycoon hopes that this book will be a useful achievement for the Svay Rieng Chamber of Commerce as well as for the Chamber of Commerce across the country.
Mr. Oknha also requested Mr. Oknha Sok Rado and all members of Svay Rieng Chamber of Commerce to continue this good cooperation and support the successful and efficient preparation of Svay Rieng Investment Guidebook. In particular, there must be honesty, cooperation and solidarity to attract more investors for Svay Rieng.
