Spokesman for the General Commission: On October 24, another 878 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 177 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to October 24, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected And fined a total of 197,041 vehicles, including 145,595 motorcycles and 51,446 vehicles of all types.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 177 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine vehicles for offenses has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
Please note that for October 24, 2020, traffic accidents across Cambodia also occurred 7 times, in which 3 people died and 08 people were injured (05 people were seriously injured).
(Banteay Meanchey): Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, told Fresh News on October 24 that the floods in Banteay Meanchey province have eased.
Mr. Kun Kim said that in Banteay Meanchey province, as of October 24, 2020, all the affected districts have been relieved, leaving only Poipet, Ochrov, Mongkul Borei and Serey Sophorn. These districts are not relieved by the water that flows and flows and flows out of nowhere.
The senior minister added that in order to release the water, some places had to be pumped out so that the dirty water would not cause disease to the people. He said that more than 40,000 families in Banteay Meanchey province have been distributed emergency aid to 36,000 families, the remaining 4,000 families will be distributed to them in the next two days. Once.
According to Kun Kim, not only Banteay Meanchey but also Phnom Penh and other flood-affected provinces have been relieved.
It should be noted that according to the report of the National Committee for Disaster Management, obtained by Fresh News, as of the evening of October 23, 2020, yesterday, the impact of floods on 20 provincial capitals was equal to 117 cities. Khan district. It affected 133,794 families, equivalent to about 535,176 people.
