National Road No. 94 from Chep District to the Lao Border has been rehabilitated, while National Road No. 92.95 and other roads will continue to be repaired after the water recedes.
(Preah Vihear): National Road No. 94 from Chhep district to Kampong Sralou commune on the border with Laos has been repaired after being damaged in some places due to floods so that people as well as national and international tourists can Easy to travel.
Mr. Samleang Try, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Preah Vihear Province, said on the afternoon of October 24, 2020 that National Road No. 94 from Chep District to Kampong Sralou One Commune, Kampong Sralou II Commune, bordering Laos, is 65 km long. Meters This road is a kind of red gravel road.
He said that during the rainy season, heavy rains caused damage to the road, making it difficult to travel, but now the team of the Department of Public Works and Transport has repaired the road and allowed people to do. Easy travel again.
He stated that in the near future, the road maintenance team of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Preah Vihear Province will continue to repair National Road 92, National Road 95, as well as many other roads in the direction for people to travel. Easy, but to this day, some roads are not flooded.
He reminded that following the instructions of Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport and Mr. Prak Sovann, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, during the floods, the Department was ready to assign a team to stand in some locations. Adequate machinery and equipment to be ready to intervene to save people from being affected by floods.
"I am very happy to have established a blood donation program to save the lives of Cambodians in collaboration with the National Blood Transfusion Center of the Ministry of Health."
The main reason for creating this program is due to the observation that in Cambodia, as well as around the world, there are deaths due to anemia or any health accident, such as traffic accidents, severe anemia and surgery that causes a lot of blood loss. Not only in Cambodia, but also in other countries, there is always a shortage of blood to save those who need blood to survive.
Mr. Haiko Vandermarel stated that donating blood can not only save the lives of patients and society, but also benefit those who donate. Blood transfusions automatically increase the production of red blood cells in the human body.
He thanked the blood donors today: "We will continue to create this blood donation program because donating blood is easy and saves lives, especially without affecting and making us healthier. "
Among the above blood donors mentioned similarly, this blood donation is to give life to patients who need blood to live and not make us regret and regret by letting us die of anemia. .
On that occasion, Dr. Meksa Mean, Deputy Director of the National Blood Transfusion Center, said that on behalf of the National Blood Transfusion Center of the Ministry of Health, all civil servants, staff, "I am very happy for all the philanthropists who have made gifts for life and "All kinds of activities to promote voluntary and free blood donation contribute to saving the lives of victims with kindness."
"In the first nine months of 2020, 54,000 people donated blood," she said. "This year, globally, including Cambodia, in the case of Kovid, voluntary blood donations have dropped slightly by only 15% for 85% of family blood transfusions."
Therefore, responding to the need for blood is not enough to save patients who need blood. She called on people to donate blood voluntarily to ensure blood safety and adequate blood supply, as in other countries.
Dr. Meksa Mean said that if all our people participated, around 1% of the population across the country, the National Blood Transfusion Center would not lack blood and the quality of blood would be better. Because people are the raw material of blood, there is no factory to produce blood, so let's all join in donating blood so there is no need to donate blood immediately to exchange blood to help their families.
She explained the health benefits of donating blood:
* Donate blood, get a health check-up to let us know about diseases: hepatitis B, syphilis, AIDS, etc., and the team of the National Blood Transfusion Center.
It also reduces the risk of cancer.
Reduces blood pressure and iron overload, which affects the liver and pancreas.
* Helps improve heart health, reduce weight gain, stroke.
* You will have fun when you can become an indispensable assistant for the doctor in saving the patient's life. Donating blood does not affect health.
Preah Sihanouk Province: Police in Preah Sihanouk Province were searching for and arresting two perpetrators in the morning. October 24, 2020 in Group 7, Village 1, Sangkat 3.
The seized items included seven 1-meter-long red copper wires, some wire sheaths, a machete for a wire harness, and a wire rod for a wire roll.
A urine test was then performed to find out that the two suspects had actually used drugs. The two suspects are currently being held at the Sihanoukville Police Inspectorate to build a case to be sent to the provincial court to proceed with the procedure.
Senior Minister Kun Kim, Representative of Samdech Techo, Delivers Donations to More Than 6,000 Families Affected by Floods in Mongkul Borei District and Serey Sophorn City, Banteay Meanchey Province
(Banteay Meanchey): Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice President of the National Committee for Disaster Management, representing Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on October 24, 2020, handed over gifts to more than 6,000 flood victims in Mongkul Borei district (4,000 families) and Serey Sophorn city (2,000 families), Banteay Meanchey province.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Kun Kim informed the people of Mongkul Borei district that before boarding the plane back to Phnom Penh, Samdech Techo brought a message to send greetings through him to the people throughout the district. Samdech regrets not coming to see them in person, as when he visited 5,000 families before, because Samdech has a lot of national affairs to solve, so please understand.
The Senior Minister said that Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit are constantly monitoring the well-being and hardships of the people affected by the floods. Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit never forgot or left any people. Although the two Samdechs have not yet arrived in person, the Samdech has issued strict orders to him and the provincial authorities to take care of all these difficulties.
Oum Rath, Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, said that Banteay Meanchey is the second province after Battambang among the 20 affected capitals and provinces, with about 40,000 families affected by the floods and about 5,000 families were evacuated as 22 people drowned.
