General knowledge: Which nation produced the first champagne?
In fact, champagne was first made in the 16th century by a British man. It is made from bubbly wine with added sugar and molasses. In addition, the artisans have created clear and rigid glass bottles and designed cork for bottle caps.
In later times, the French added techniques to the production and use of marketing skills to make champagne popular. It was not until 1876 that the French were able to produce a modern Brut style champagne, which tasted less sweet and was sold on the world market.
The United Kingdom is one of France's largest consumers of champagne, with 34 million people consuming 34 million bottles of champagne in 2004, more than double the United States. Germany 3 times and 20 times Spain.
