Anti-Drug Department Detains Suspect, Seizes Over 1kg of Drugs
(Phnom Penh): The Anti-Drug Department cracked down on a drug trafficking case in Phnom Penh, detaining a suspect and confiscating more than 1 kg of drugs.
A senior official of the Anti-Drug Department confirmed to Fresh News on October 24 that the crackdown on drug trafficking took place on October 21, 2020 at the intersection of concrete road in Sangkat Choam Chao 2, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
The crackdown was led by Mr. Kheng Sarath, Deputy Director of the Anti-Drug Department (A4), under the command of General Santebandit Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner General, General Mak Chito, Deputy National Police Commissioner and General. Ek Lek Vannak, Director of the Anti-Drug Department, with the coordination of Mr. Seang Moniroth, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
The suspect was Kith Sokha, a 31-year-old Cambodian male, and the seized items were 1035.41 grams of methamphetamine (ICE). Suspects and exhibits are being processed and sent to court.
Please be informed that for the past few days, the Anti-Drug Department (A4) has been working hard to investigate and crack down on major drug trafficking cases in Phnom Penh and other provinces.
