During the trip to solve the problems caused by these floods, Senior Minister Kun Kim was seen holding a cane regularly, which led to the question of what was wrong with his legs?
An official from the National Committee for Disaster Management said his left leg sprained during a visit to the army on Phnom Trop in Preah Vihear province some time ago. According to the same official, the senior minister was banned from walking much by doctors.
But while treating and caring for the sprained ankle, the floodwaters came. Despite doctors banning and warning of severe leg pain, Senior Minister Kun Kim did not choose the doctor's advice to rest and walk.
As the staff of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Senior Minister Kun Kim was forced to carry a crutch and travel to the flooded area to check the plight of the people and set out solutions for the people.
Through this gesture, some people who knew about this problem when the Senior Minister visited, expressed his appreciation and appreciation for Senior Minister Kun Kim's attention to the people's problems in the flood by Regardless of his sore leg.
This gesture shows that as Samdech Techo's staff on disaster work, Senior Minister Kun Kim pays high attention to the work ahead of Samdech Techo. In particular, consider the well-being of the people, especially the pain of their feet.
