Samdech Techo Prime Minister expressed his deep gratitude to the philanthropists who have contributed to help the people who are suffering from the floods. Mr. Jean Malin mentioned 5 points about the price and legal validity of the Paris Agreement of October 23
(Phnom Penh): On the 29th anniversary of the Paris Peace Agreement (October 23, 1991-October 23, 2020), Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Justice, Jean Malin, made five points on the value and legal validity of the peace agreement. Paris, October 23.
Some historical events of Samdech Tramram's negotiations led to the Paris Agreement of October 23, 1991, which had four signatories: Samdech Techo Hun Sen representing the Cambodian government, the FUNCINPEC movement represented by Samdech Preah Norodom Sihanouk and Samdech Krom Preah. Norodom Ranariddh, National Front for the Liberation of the Khmer People, represented by Ta Son San, and the Democratic Kampuchea Movement (Pol Pot), represented by Khieu Samphan.
The 5 points that Mr. Jean Malin mentioned include:
First, the Paris Agreement aimed at ending the civil war in Cambodia and establishing a temporary legal mechanism and institution to govern the country during the transition period from 1991 to 1993, before Cambodia had a coalition government and a constitution to lead the country.
Third, the spirit of the Paris Agreement on ending the war in Cambodia was not fully implemented and respected, nor did it bring true peace to Cambodia. Because the Khmer Rouge did not abide by this agreement, did not participate in the election and continued to wage war until 1998, when Cambodia achieved complete and real peace throughout the country through the victorious policies of Samdech Techo.
