(Phnom Penh): As of March 18, 1970, when the group of General Lon Nol and Prince Sisowath Sirimat staged a coup to overthrow Samdech Norodom Sihanouk as the great head of the Sangkum Reastr Niyum. As the flames of war raged on Cambodian territory, flames began to erupt.
It is a noble fortune for the Cambodian people that the dark pages of the war are slowly fading after Samdech Norodom Sihanouk and Samdech Techo Hun Sen tried to find a negotiation to end the flames of war. This Cambodian society.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the founder of the peace talks, once stressed that peace talks could not have taken place without Samdech Norodom Sihanouk and his statue. Samdech Techo confirmed that both characters are the most important characters.
Through Samdech Techo Hun Sen's message, it is clear that the talks of October 23, 1991 were born out of the spirit of national unity, born of Khmer and Khmer.
Overall, October 23, 1991 was a clear demonstration of the steps taken to end the conflict between Cambodians and Cambodians under Cambodian family negotiations, not foreigners. October 23 has become a mirror of the spirit of unity that Cambodian politicians of all persuasions and all Cambodians should adhere to in solving national problems to avoid the flames of war and push the nation forward.
October 23 is also an event to remind the Cambodian people of the suffering of the Cambodian people because of the flames of war and the importance of peace that must be jointly protected and maintained.
