(Phnom Penh): Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, stated that Cambodia must train the Chinese language at the highest level, in addition, Cambodia must also train Korean and Japanese to increase employment opportunities and other social work Currently, Cambodia has received a lot of investment inflows from Chinese investors.
Dr. Sok Touch made this statement on the occasion that he chaired a roundtable discussion on "Chinese pedagogical training" at the Royal Academy of Cambodia on October 23, 2020.
Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, thanked the Chinese Association in Cambodia for supporting the Chinese language pedagogical initiative in Cambodia. He said that this support is a history for Cambodia, where Cambodia-China has been in contact for more than a thousand years, but there is no such Chinese language pedagogical class in Cambodia yet.
Dr. Sok Touch continued that the establishment of Chinese language pedagogical classes in Cambodia has changed the history. On behalf of the President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, I would like to thank Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, for giving the Royal Academy of Cambodia the opportunity to open a pedagogical class in Cambodia.
According to the President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, in order not to overwhelm the Chinese language like some other languages, the Royal Academy of Cambodia has established three main pedagogical classes, namely: first, pedagogical in teaching, second: pedagogical in grammar and second. 3: Pedagogical class on book writing. In addition, standardized Chinese translation skills can be used officially on each section as well.
Dr. Sok Touch emphasized that in the future, the Royal Academy of Cambodia will cooperate with Chinese universities to train on 4 points: 1: Business, 2: Management in each warehouse, 3: Hospitality and Fourth: Food. This is to increase the employment of its professional Cambodians, so Cambodia needs to build a nation based on knowledge, not on natural resources.
Dr. Sok Touch recalled that in 2018, Cambodia and China signed an agreement, and this agreement was signed by the President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia with the Chinese side of Hantan with three parties: Tianjin University, Shanghai University and Peking University and the Royal Academy of Cambodia have opened their hearts to accept these three major universities and other associations working in the same direction for the benefit of society.
Mr. Sot Samnang continued that in this context, Cambodia has observed that the teaching of Chinese language, which depends only on Chinese teachers, has made Cambodia face a number of challenges, including: The number of Mon teachers can respond to the current situation. Some Chinese volunteer teachers do not go through actual pedagogy.
Speaking at the ceremony, Lt. Gen. Lor Soleng said that this charitable donation is a noble gesture from the Chinese Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia, and this is a testament to the spirit of contribution to help the victims. Experiencing natural phenomena, floods.
