Council of Ministers approves "Draft Law on General State Budget Payment for 2019"
(Phnom Penh): "Draft Law on the Payment of the General State Budget for Management 2019" was fully approved by the Council of Ministers in a plenary session chaired by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia at the Peace Palace this morning. October 23, 2020. This is according to the announcement of Mr. Phay Siphan, the spokesman of the Royal Government of Cambodia on Facebook.
He added that the implementation of the 2019 budget has contributed to support the implementation of the following priority policies of the Royal Government:
* Continue to strengthen peace, political stability, security, public order and the safety of villages and communes for the protection of the people's livelihood, as well as the protection of independence, sovereignty and territorial integrity from being violated and destroyed by any force.
* Ensure the implementation of policies to promote employment growth, equity and efficiency, build the base towards achieving the vision of Cambodia by 2050 to continue to reduce poverty of the people and distribute the fruits of equitable growth to all classes of people.
* Continue to ensure strong, sustainable, and resilient economic growth, as well as ensure overall financial stability in the context of manageable low inflation and a stable exchange rate.
In the reform of decentralization and deconcentration of sub-national administrations, the Ministry of Economy and Finance has developed a strategy for the reform of the sub-national administrative budget system 2019-2025 to prepare a sub-national budget system that responds to the establishment. "Public services, the environment and the value of money."
* Continue to consider and increase the salaries of civil servants and the armed forces at an appropriate level to general civil servants, as well as increase the pensions of retirees and veterans and give priority to increase the salaries of civil servants at the management level and Advanced skills in the framework of linking public administration reform to public financial management reform.
In 2019, the basic salary and other allowances were gradually increased as follows: (1) - The basic salary increase at the rate of 10.0% by increasing the basic salary according to the unit price index of 2,340 Riels from January 2019 (2) - Increase of additional salary of 30,000 Riels for all civil servants and members of the Armed Forces with a salary of 750,000 Riels or less, which has been implemented since April 2019.
This policy framework plays an important role in increasing access to social assistance and social security for public and private sector officials and the population of the informal economy. The Cambodian social protection system has two pillars: (1) - the social security system and (2) - the social assistance system.
Accelerate the implementation of the Cambodian Industrial Development Policy Measures 2015-2025, which is a new economic growth strategy by promoting adequate public investment in infrastructure and the provision of public services necessary to support industrial activities.
In fact, in 2019, about 100 million US dollars will be allocated for financing the establishment of SMEs Bank. At the same time, the budget loan was allocated to the Council for the Development of Cambodia for coordination with the ministries and institutions directly involved in the implementation of the Cambodian Industrial Development Policy 2015-2025.
* Continue to promote human resource development by improving the quality of education and vocational and technical training at both low, medium and high levels to supply sufficiently skilled skilled workers to meet the needs of the business.
The 2019 budget gives high priority to the social sector in order to promote human resource development, which is the most important resource for supporting and developing Cambodia's economy. In fact, the expenditure for the social sector in 2019 was 6,280,003.4 million riels, equivalent to 35.1% of the national budget current expenditure, which is 5.7% of GDP. And an increase of 9.1% compared to 2018 implementation.
* Continue to develop physical infrastructure, especially focusing on connectivity in the transport, energy and digital sectors, with electricity prices being discounted according to specific programs and tariffs for 2019 and 2020 to boost growth in the sector. Agriculture, industry and services.
In order to support economic growth, promote competitiveness and economic productivity, the 2019 budget has supported investment in essential infrastructure, both hardware and software. In fact, public investment expenditures with domestic financing in 2019 amounted to 3,515,793.3 million riels, an increase of 39.5% compared to the implementation in 2018, which is 3.20% of GDP.
* Continue to promote the development of the agricultural sector by focusing on increasing productivity, diversification, agricultural processing and trade.
* Continue to support the implementation of the financial sector development strategy 2016-2025.
Within the framework of market and financial institution development, the implementation of the financial sector development strategy 2016-2025 to support the management of financial stability, financing and revenue collection of the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
The securities market in Cambodia has evolved rapidly and has become an important part of the driving force behind national economic growth by providing long-term sources of capital for Cambodian businesses and promoting transparency and accountability. Accountability in the private sector in Cambodia, as well as the mobilization of the remaining local resources and increase investment options for the people of Cambodia.
* Continue to manage public debt effectively, efficiently, transparently and responsibly with the aim of maintaining long-term public debt sustainability and keeping debt risk levels low.
* Support the election of the Capital Council, Provincial Council, Municipal Council, District Council and Khan Council of the third mandate.
Expenditure of the National Election Committee in 2019 was 61,396.9 million Riels, equivalent to 0.3% of the current national budget expenditure, with special emphasis on supporting registration and audit. Name and election of Capital Council, Provincial Council, Municipal Council, District Council and Khan Council of the third mandate in 2019 to be conducted smoothly, correctly, transparently and fairly.
* Continue to reform governance and strengthen institutional capacity and cleanliness in public administration, especially strengthening the efficiency of operations to ensure efficiency, efficiency, accountability and transparency of public services to gain greater trust from the people.
