Senior Health Official Urges Stakeholders to Increase Child Care to Reduce Infant and Child Mortality in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Secretary of State for the Ministry of Health, Professor Eng Huot, urges health officials and stakeholders to pay more attention to child health care, while infant and child mortality rates in Cambodia remain a concern.
This statement was made by the senior official at the opening ceremony of the second pediatric conference organized by the National Children's Hospital at the Le Royal Hotel on October 22, 2020.
The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Health said that Cambodia has successfully reduced the maternal and child mortality rate significantly. But the issue remains a concern as the decline has not yet reached its target.
He added that the conference is very important for doctors, nurses, midwives and various specialists in the health profession to meet and share knowledge and experience in practice. Pediatric and infant care.
