(Tbong Khmum): Dr. Cheam Chansophoan, Governor of Tbong Khmum Province, and his wife, this morning, October 22, 2020, brought more than 10,000 fish fry into Trapeang Kampeng Lake in Khchay Village, Tambor Commune, Tambor District, Tbong Khmum Province.
The release ceremony was organized by the provincial administration in collaboration with the provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and Tambor district authorities, with the participation of the provincial board of governors, relevant departments and a large number of people.
Dr. Cheam Chansophoan said that it is best to have many natural lakes in the districts in Tbong Khmum province, and those lakes are important sources of benefits to the people, such as water and fish. Therefore, we must work together to prevent criminals from abusing or using illegal fishing gear such as electric shocks that harm all kinds of fish.
On that occasion, Dr. Governor called on all people to work together to preserve natural resources such as fish, not to use illegal fishing gear, which destroys and extinct fish in the future as an important source of food for Our descendants, the next generation.
At the same time, Dr. Cheam Chan Sophoan also called on all people to be very careful about the phenomenon of natural disasters that occur eventually and also to live hygienically to prevent various infectious diseases, especially Kovid. 19.
After releasing the young fish into Trapeang Kampeng Lake, Dr. Governor also went to inspect the raising of chickens, laying eggs and hatching young people in Trapeang Pring commune, Tambor district, to encourage farmers. Who started a career in his community, which was a major source of income for the family during the 1940 epidemic, as a result of migration to work away from home.
