Moteki reaffirmed his willingness to strengthen bilateral relations and cooperation with Cambodia under the new Japanese government. At the same time, Mr. Moteki expressed his condolences to the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia, who have been severely affected by the severe floods. He said Japan was ready to help Cambodia solve this problem.
Mr Moteki said Japan would support Cambodia in improving the urban environment and taking action against marine plastic waste, as well as building counter-terrorism capacity. Japan will also support Cambodia when Cambodia takes over the rotating chairmanship of ASEAN in 2022. Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon thanked Japan for its continued support for Cambodia's socio-economic development.
