Minister of Agriculture inspected the flood situation at the Agricultural Research and Development Institute of Cambodia and advised to restore the condition of rice crops when the water recedes
According to the institute's report, the effects of the floods from the upper reaches, especially from National Road 4 and the Prek Tnaot flood, have affected the institute's experimental fields of both light and medium rice. The flooding caused almost no damage to light rice and some damage to middle rice.
According to Dr. Ouk Makara, director of the institute, if the water level starts to decrease from today, next week the middle rice can be harvested.
In particular, in the case of administrative buildings and laboratories, leaders and professional officers at all levels worked together day and night to bring sandbags to prevent water from flowing into the building, and in some places to use water pumps to help. Save state property from sinking.
However, unfortunately, on the night of the first day, the effects of the flood destroyed 3 tons of rice seeds in the warehouse. In the meantime, the institute is continuing to take preventive measures by using sandbags to lift rice paddies around major buildings and pump out water.
After examining the situation of the disaster, Minister Veng Sakhon praised all the leaders, officials and staff who took the fatigue, mental and responsible responsibility to take preventive measures in time, despite the impact and Damage to rice seeds and some infrastructure.
After the flood, Minister Veng Sakhon instructed the institute to improve the infrastructure of the institute and to restore the condition of the rice crop as much as possible.
He said that this is an experience that should be remembered as a lesson for the next year. In addition, it is necessary to pay more attention to the maintenance of the property, especially the basic rice seeds in the warehouse of GEN Bank and the laboratory.
To alleviate the challenges on this occasion, Minister Veng Sakhon donated 900 liters of fuel and $ 500 to the Institute of Oil for use as needed, especially to continue pumping water from the flooded area.
The Director of the Institute, on behalf of all levels of civil servants, expressed his deep gratitude for the time, encouragement and care of Minister Veng Sakhon on the entire Institute, despite his busy schedule. .
On this occasion, the Director of the Institute donated 4 tons of fragrant rice and 20 tons of mixed rice to Minister Veng Sakhon to be distributed to farmers or agricultural communities affected by the flood to help restore production. Rice crops after the water recedes. Mr. Som Kdei and Ms. Chea Yuth Amara donated $ 2,000 to Samdech Techo Hun Sen to help flood victims
