Authorities crack down on imports of chicken and pork off the Cambodian-Thai border, which damaged more than 3 tons
(Banteay Meanchey): After careful attention and thorough research, the customs officer of the 5th Regional Smuggling Investigation Office in Banteay Meanchey Province led the officers under the cooperation of the National Gendarmerie and Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police. Crack down on illegal traders along the Cambodian-Thai border by smuggling substandard chicken and pig offal to be distributed in the Cambodian market.
After the crackdown, the exhibits were handed over to the competent authorities of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Production and Veterinary Office for incineration in accordance with legal procedures.
In addition, the director of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Veterinary Production Office would like to appeal to housewives to be careful of their health before buying chicken, duck, pork to eat, please check carefully because it seriously affects health.
