Ms. O Vandin praised the Preah Vihear provincial authorities for effectively preventing Kovid 19 and further promoting the practice of arbitrariness.
(Preah Vihear): Mrs. O Vandin, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Health, praised and thanked the Preah Vihear Provincial Authority as well as all relevant institutions in the province for their efforts to join the Royal Government and the Ministry of Health in The fight against Kovid 19 was especially successful, and two Kovid 19 patients were cured.
Ms. O Vandin made this statement on the occasion that she was represented by Prof. Dr. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, accompanied by Ms. Ly Ilen, Representative of the World Health Organization, led the working group to meet with Mr. Prak Sovann, Governor of Preah Vihear Province on the morning of the 22nd. This October 2020.
Ms. O Vandin stated that while Preah Vihear province has two 19 cases of Kovid, she is very worried, do not know how many more of these two? But obviously, through the close work between her and Dr. Kuong Lo, the director of the Preah Vihear Provincial Health Department, they communicate by phone all the time, finding ways to make this work more effective. "By working together, we can prevent it," she said.
Ms. O Vandin further stated that Preah Vihear is a tourist province with people passing in and out, so the possibility of bringing 19 Kovid virus is only we do not know when, so we must put strict measures to continue this measure. In the health check of those who come and go, especially at the border, as well as other tourist sites. Increased attention should be paid to the practice of meditation, both at home and in the district.
Mr. Prak Sovann said that as of October 21, 2020, Preah Vihear province had tested 19 samples for 519 people, including 507 negative results and 2 positive results, but had been cured. He said that a total of 813 foreign migrants were carefully monitored and placed in the center and at home for 14 days.
At the same time, the province has prepared to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 for 4 separate patients, including: Green Palace Hotel, Teachers' Guesthouse, Preah Vihear Chey Hotel and Ta Keung Safety Center. And medical staff as well as staff at Chattalysak Center.
