(Svay Rieng): The Anti-Technology Crime Department of the National Police in collaboration with the Svay Rieng Provincial Police investigated and arrested a suspect who posted a gun for sale on Facebook in Svay Rieng.
This operation was carried out under the direct command of General Dr. Neth Savoeun, General Commissioner of the National Police and led by Lt. Gen. Chea Pov, Director of the Department of Technology Crimes on October 20, 2020.
The suspect, 32-year-old An Sambath, was arrested at Tuol Srang village, Meam commune, Romeas Hek district, Svay Rieng province. He advertised and sold all kinds of guns on Facebook.
Lt. Gen. Riel Sophea, deputy director of the Anti-Technology Crime Department, who led the investigation and crackdown on the case, confirmed that the suspect had set up several Facebook accounts, all of which were fake accounts, and advertised the sale of modern pistols and shotguns. Animals and gas guns of all kinds, imported from neighboring countries to sell in Cambodia.
But of all the Facebook accounts, some are used to defraud buyers when they make a purchase and are required to pay the buyer, and most do not deliver the goods. The department's police force is currently preparing to send the suspect to court.
At the same time, Lt. Gen. Chea Pov, Director of the Department of Technology Crimes, vowed to continue to crack down on illegal trafficking through this technology and asked people who play on social media to report to the Department of Technology Crimes through Pak of the department directly when you see or suspect that any crime has occurred.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen made this statement on the occasion of continuing to visit and provide food to flood victims in Thmar Puok district and Poipet city on the morning of October 22, 2020.
The Prime Minister expressed his gratitude to His Majesty the King and His Majesty the Queen Mother for donating money and food to the flood victims and thanked them. All philanthropists who volunteer to participate in charitable activities with the government.
