Regarding this unintentional criticism, Samdech Techo replied that critics of philanthropists who contribute money to the Royal Government to help people affected by floods or other disasters are like insulting the King and Samdech Mother Nature, because both of them also contributed to this.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen considers that the opposition group that criticizes the donation of funds with the Royal Government to help people affected by the flood is jealous of this charity.
At the same time, the Head of the Royal Government also confirmed that in the past, the authorities at all levels as well as philanthropists have participated in a lot of activities to help and support the victims, some of which were distributed to the victims. Some people participate through national institutions, while others participate through the Royal Government or through the Prince himself.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed the hope that philanthropists will continue to join this spirit to solve problems for the people, while the Royal Government has been releasing funds and food to share with the victims.
