(Phnom Penh): Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that as a research institution, the Royal Academy will prepare all the statues of Jayavarman VII in the first phase according to the history of each image. Through the temples or his work to publicize.
This confirmation of the President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia was made this morning, October 22, 2020, on the occasion that he presided over the forum on "Identity of King Jayavarman VII". This is to suit the honor of the King and be kept in all provinces throughout Cambodia, while researchers have found the identity of King Jayavarman VII in other forms.
In that regard, Mr. Yong Pov, Secretary General of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, confirmed that a team of experts of the Royal Academy of Cambodia has studied and identified Jayavarman VII (the name of the emperor). The purpose of this research is to build a single statue of Jayavarman VII (in a different form than before) to be housed in the "Khmer Vito" building, which will soon be completed on the grounds of the Royal Academy.
Dr. Tha said: "The research team of the Royal Academy of Cambodia has conducted research to find the identity of the statue of Jayavarman VII in other forms other than sitting, meditating or saluting."
Mr. Yong Pov added that this study will result in the identification of a "statue of King Jayavarman VII", which is a national agreement, and the Royal Academy of Cambodia will establish a statue of King Jayavarman VII, as well as compile and publish. The form and rules of the statue in the spirit of the forum to show the "Emperor of the Angkorian era" to the next generation of Cambodians to remember the heroic and easy to build a statue of him.
Please be informed that King Jayavarman VII (the name of the emperor) led the country during the Mahanakorn period, which was a Khmer kingdom full of royal splendor and ruled Cambodia following the path of Mahayana Buddhism.
