(Phnom Penh): A Cambodian woman who claims to be a victim of abuse through marriage in China will return home on the evening of October 22, 2020 after the Ministry of Foreign Affairs through the Consulate General of Cambodia. In Shanghai, intervene. The intervention came after he posted a video on Facebook calling on Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen to come to the rescue.
The Royal Government of Cambodia, through the Cambodian Consulate General in Shanghai, China, has cooperated with the Chinese authorities to intervene to help this Cambodian woman named Sem Srey Pich, who lives in Zhejiang Province, China, intending to return to Cambodia because she could not live in harmony with Husband.
Neang Samreth Komar, Consul General of Cambodia in Shanghai, also told Fresh News that the woman had already boarded the plane and left for Cambodia, arriving at Phnom Penh International Airport this evening.
Ms. Neang Samreth Komar also confirmed that after arriving at the Consulate General of Cambodia, his officers stationed there took good care of him and were ready for his return to his hometown on This coming October 22nd.
He thanked all the parents and siblings who felt sorry for the sister who was the victim and helped share the information so that our Consulate General could receive the information quickly. Thank you for the good cooperation of the Chinese Immigration Police and the Cambodian Chaplain Coalition (helping to pay for airfare) and all the Consulate General staff who worked hard to fulfill their duties.
According to a video shared on Facebook, Srey Pich appealed to social media users who watched her video and asked her to share her voice of sorrow with Samdech Techo Hun Sen. He said he cheated when he arrived in China, adding that he did not have a family phone. Srey Pich lured her to borrow a phone from someone else to record the video and post it on social media.
