(Banteay Meanchey): On October 21, 2020, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, intercepted more than 400 kilometers from Phnom Penh to Banteay Meanchey province to inspect and distribute food to the affected people. Flooding.
On October 21, Samdech Techo Prime Minister held a get-together and distributed food at two destinations attended by up to 10,000 people. In addition to meeting with the people on the mainland, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also boarded a boat to visit and bring food to people living in homes not yet fled.
Samdech Techo, the head of the Royal Government, explained that the reason why Samdech had to go directly to Banteay Meanchey province was because Banteay Meanchey province was the most flooded province among the capital-provinces affected by the floods. In addition, the province also has many affected families, making the distribution of food by the provincial authorities is not fast, so Samdech had to come directly to speed up the distribution of food to the people.
Cambodia is a country that has suffered greatly from the flames of war and after the country was liberated from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot on January 7, 1979. Therefore, the hardships and sufferings of the floods in 2020 are not new for the people and for Cambodia as a whole. Cambodia has been through many hardships and disasters.
People who attended the meeting and received gifts from Samdech Techo Prime Minister, even though they were suffering because of the flood, were happy and warm to see Samdech Techo come down to the place where they were drowning. . These affected people said that the food donations that Samdech Techo brought to them were valuable and could help alleviate their shortage for a while before the water receded.
