Law enforcement forces launched an active anti-drug operation and achieved remarkable results, in which 30 major cases (3 processing sites) were suppressed by seizing more than 2 types of drugs. Ton and arrested 11 masterminds and 47 network.
Through the implementation of administrative and legal rules, the operation of crackdowns on entertainment venues has affected the country's drug trafficking and illicit markets. In fact, based on the results of the crackdown, drug use cases decreased by 3.28% compared to the same period in 2019.
In this meeting, Lt. Gen. Lek Vannak said that this is the result and the advantage of the law enforcement forces in the past operation is to get proud results with the continuous increase, especially drug seizures. And almost 3 tons of ingredients recently, but there are still some gaps related to technical skills, which requires the police to work harder to strengthen capacity.
General Mak Chito has set six goals for all anti-drug police to continue to promote the effective implementation of the Royal Government's anti-drug campaign plan, including:
1: Continue to promote the effective implementation of the Royal Government's anti-illegal drug campaign plan.
2. Continue to promote research and investigation into the remaining major cases in order to crack down on the root cause.
3: Continue to research, investigate and crack down on money laundering crimes as a result of drug offenses.
4: Continue to promote the implementation of measures to research, investigate, prevent and suppress the importation, smuggling, processing and trafficking in target by strengthening the monitoring and control of activities along the border, as well as the strict implementation of administrative and legal measures. Follow the spirit of the slogan of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior "3 Do 1 Report".
5. Strengthen cooperation in exchanging information with cooperation partners both inside and outside the region by striving to build and strengthen clear communication mechanisms.
