(Phnom Penh): A poor man was involved in an electric shock accident, causing injuries, almost death almost immediately after the accident, the victim was sent to rescue in Phnom Penh, but unfortunately due to the serious condition, doctors required surgery His hands out.
The victim is 29-year-old In Meng Hee, a car mechanic living in Thmey Village, Kampeng Commune, Prey Kabas District, Takeo Province.
The accident happened on September 12, 2020. Prior to the incident, the victim went to the garage of a car repair shop and was electrocuted on the ground. Hours later, he was rushed to Arunreah Polyclinic (near Hengly Market).
This dangerous situation is so serious that Mr. In Meng Hee's family has to spend a lot of money for medical treatment, as his family has sold all the tax land in his hometown, but still can not pay the full medical expenses.
Despite the huge sums of money, the victim's limbs were partially lost, and both legs were ready to be amputated, although his family had no money for the treatment.
