(Stung Treng): This morning, October 21, 2020, the leaders of Stung Treng Province visited a working group to visit and bring gifts from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Red Cross. Cambodia provides relief to 105 flood-affected families from Anlong Phe and Chamkar Leu communes in Thala Parivat district.
The distribution ceremony was held at Wat Chamkar Leu pagoda in the presence of Mr. Mom Saroeun, Provincial Governor, Mr. Chheang Lak, Chairman of the Provincial Council, together with Mr. and Mrs. Figure.
Mr. Mom Saroeun said that the gift given to the people now is the noble spirit of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, which both Samdech and the leaders of the Royal Government always pay attention From the well-being of people everywhere, regardless of race, religion or color.
The provincial governor confirmed that the flood situation occurred from October 10 to October 13, 2020, the water began to recede, affecting 13 villages in Thala Parivat district. And flooded 851 houses with 923 families or 3377 people.
The evacuation of 55 families, equal to 168 people, affected 327 hectares of rice, damaged 171 hectares, affected 30 hectares of mixed crops, damaged 22 hectares and affected the infrastructure of roads, sewers, schools, pagodas. Well.
It should also be noted that the donation from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to 105 families through Stung Treng Provincial Administration now includes: Each family received 25 kg of rice, soy sauce and 1 fishing rod. B: 1 can, 1 can of pure water, and 1 mosquito net.
