(Bangkok): Dozens of loyalists in the Thai monarchy rallied in Bangkok on Wednesday to show their love for the king and also warned anti-government protesters not to touch them. The King does not. This was released by CNA on Wednesday, October 21, 2020.
The rally was held at a time when the Thai government had declared a state of emergency, banning gatherings of more than five people. Organizers of the rally claimed that their rally was not under ban, but a Thai police spokesman told reporters that the ban should be applied equally to all.
