Prek Pnov District Governor Leads Officers to Inspect Flood Rainfall on Road 42 Near Boeung Krachap Bridge, Sangkat Ponsaing
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sok Sambath, Governor of Prek Pnov District, this morning, October 21, 2020, led Khan officials and Mr. Ponsaing Sangkat Chief to inspect the flooding of Road 42 near Boeung Krachap Bridge, Sangkat Ponsaing, Khan Prek Pnov, Phnom Penh.
Floods are affecting 19 capitals and provinces: Pursat, Pailin, Banteay Meanchey, Phnom Penh, Battambang, Svay Rieng, Oddar Meanchey, Siem Reap, Takeo, Kampong Speu, Mondulkiri, Sihanoukville, Koh Kong, Preah Vihear, Stung Treng, Kampong Cham, Kandal, Kampong Chhnang and Kampong Thom.
The introduction of the Supreme Leader of the Royal Government of Cambodia was made on the morning of October 21, 2020 on the occasion of distributing donations to 5,000 families (target 1) affected by the flood in Mongkul Borei district, Banteay Meanchey province.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructed the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Authority to coordinate with all philanthropists and politicians who wish to distribute gifts to the victims in their territory. Samdech stated that the more humanitarian donations available to help the affected people, the better.
Samdech Techo, the Prime Minister, said: "Please confirm again and again, it does not mean that when I finished distributing, there are philanthropists to distribute, we will not share. The more you share, the better. "Philanthropists, political parties are coming."
"And hopefully political parties, politicians do not discriminate against (victims). Please do not discriminate. "Whoever we are, we need to save the people." This is the additional confirmation of Samdech Techo.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen added that while traveling by car to distribute the gifts, Samdech listened to two songs, including: "Infinity of nature" and "Helping each other in times of need." Samdech considered that these songs inspired everyone to help each other to overcome difficulties without any political affiliation. Samdech also advised radio and television to broadcast these songs as much as possible.
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, who is always close to the people in all circumstances, said that when people face difficulties, it is customary for Samdech to run to the people, not to run to the people. Samdech Techo told about the history of the blue shirt that visited the people for many years until it turned pale to gray.
It should be noted that during the floods in Cambodia, many government officials, citizens, philanthropists and politicians burned their hands and feet to help as well as provide humanitarian assistance.
In that, Mr. Kem Sokha, former President of the National Rescue Party also distributed donations from people in Banteay Meanchey province. In addition, Mr. Kem Sokha also donated $ 5,000 to Samdech Techo Hun Sen to help people affected by the floods.
This statement by Samdech Techo Prime Minister was made during the distribution of donations to 5,000 families (target 1) affected by the flood in Mongkul Borei district, Banteay Meanchey province on the morning of October 21, 2020.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his gratitude to His Majesty the King and His Majesty the Queen, as well as to all the benefactors who participated in supporting the flood victims. The nobles of the King and Queen Mother, as well as these charitable spirits, showed their love for each other in times of need.
Samdech Techo, the head of the Royal Government, also thanked the people for giving their trust in Samdech as well as the Cambodian People's Party, and Samdech has nothing to give back to the people other than trying to keep the peace to ensure survival. Of people not to be in the flames of war like some countries.
At the same time, Samdech Techo also recalled a blue shirt that he had worn for more than 25 years while helping people in various localities, stating that when he wore this shirt, it means that he was Help farmers in rural areas.
Minister Vong Soth: So far, the program to provide cash assistance to poor and vulnerable families during the fight against Kovid 19 went smoothly
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, gave an overview of the financial support program for poor and vulnerable families during the fight against Kovid 19 went smoothly.
He said that even the current floods did not disrupt the payment process to the target population, and even more gratifying was the fact that the people who benefited the most took the money. Use it for the benefit of the family, while some people take the initiative to start their own business, which can be beneficial for their family life in the long run.
Mr. Vong Soth said this on the occasion of meeting and distributing gifts to 200 families who are the beneficiaries and flood victims in Pralay commune, Stong district, Kampong Thom province on the morning of October 21, 2020.
In addition, Mr. Vong Soth also always met to discuss the operation of this program with the operator, commune council officials and counters who pay people.
Mr. Vong Soth acknowledged that few (perhaps very few) beneficiaries have yet to use the funds provided by the Royal Government through the above programs in a good and beneficial manner. Mr. Vong Soth has no action other than appeals and explanations.
The Royal Government of Cambodia has officially announced that it will continue to provide cash assistance to poor and vulnerable families during the fight against Kovid 19 for another three months, starting on October 25 and ending on October 25. January 24, 2021.
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Chou Bun Eng, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior and Permanent Vice President of the National Committee for Combating Human Trafficking, on October 21, 2020, continued to call on all Cambodian women to consider taking a foreign husband to avoid losing. Cheating.
The call comes after a Cambodian woman who recently claimed to be a victim of abuse cheating through marriage in China has asked the Cambodian government to intervene. Under the immediate intervention of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, she will return home on October 22, 2020.
The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Interior warns that cheating brokers through marriage with foreign husbands has been around for a long time, but some women do not seem to have taken these things into account and are still taking risks. This risk is because they think that taking a foreign husband can be rewarding.
However, Ms. Chou Bun Eng, who works hard on human trafficking, urges Cambodian women not to be complacent and to be greedy with wealth due to marriage abroad. She says they should stay calm so as not to be deceived.
"When we cheat, we lose time, we lose wealth, we lose dignity, and sometimes they are saved. When they are not saved, we will face a crisis for life," she stressed.
A Cambodian woman who claims to be a victim of marital abuse in China will return home on October 22, 2020 after the Ministry of Foreign Affairs through the Cambodian Consulate General in Phnom Penh. Shanghai intervenes. The intervention came after he posted a video on Facebook calling on Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen to come to the rescue.
Ms. Neang Samreth Komar, Consul General of Cambodia in Shanghai, also told Fresh News that after arriving at the Consulate General of Cambodia last night, our officers took good care of him and were ready for his return. Return home on October 22.
He thanked all the parents and siblings who felt sorry for the sister who was the victim and helped share the information so that the Consulate General could receive the information quickly. Thank you for the good cooperation of the Chinese Immigration Police and the Cambodian Chaplain Coalition (helping to pay for airfare) and all the Consulate General staff who worked hard to fulfill their duties.
It should be noted that not a few Cambodian women are cheated by others through such marriages. Some are married to men who do not have enough water, and some are abused by their cruel husbands and use them like animals.
In this case, Ms. Chou Bun Eng considered that it was a good luck that the victim was able to find a way to intervene, but if she did not have access to social media, it would be unfortunate. She said the Royal Government of Cambodia is busy and working hard to help victims of abuse.
She said that Srey Pich's case, even seen on Facebook, is still trying to help him. The National Committee for Combating Human Trafficking told the Anti-Human Trafficking Team of the General Commission of the National Police and also informed the Ministry of Foreign Affairs to help him effectively.
Speaking from Banteay Meanchey province, Samdech met and distributed gifts to people affected by the floods, Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded of Sam Rainsy's shame about the three-finger campaign and announced that he joined the people Thailand in anti-government protests
Samdech continued, "What! "I want to unite with the struggle with the Thai people, the Thai story, the Thai story, the Khmer story, the Khmer story, just to clarify the need now, all forces must gather to help the people in times of emergency."
On October 18, 2020, Sam Rainsy, who is currently in exile, posted an inspirational post on Facebook, posting a photo of himself with three fingers and inciting his supporters to unite with protesters in Thailand. Demonstration against the Thai government.
In addition to mocking Sam Rainsy, who made uncertain politics, Samdech Techo Hun Sen told the rebel leader that he had already learned of plans to hold a demonstration in front of the Chinese Embassy on October 23, 2020. Samdech claimed that the demonstration was driven by opposition groups abroad and gathered people from the provinces, however, he warned to suppress the demonstration, similar to the story "Khanty Nhom".
3rd Deputy Chief Priest Muong Ra Donates Over 20,000 USD to Dangkor District Administration for Distribution to Flood Victims
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Preah Odom Vongsa, Honorary Doctor Dr. Muong Ra, Third Deputy Director of the Permanent Secretariat of the Buddhist Parliament of Cambodia, on the afternoon of October 21, 2020, handed over gifts to the administration of Dangkor district, Phnom Penh to distribute to the people. Citizens affected by the floods.
Gifts donated by Samdech Preah Odom Vongsa to Dr. Dangkor Khan Administration include: 20 tons of Angkor, 200 cases of noodles, 10 cases of milk, 10 cases of fish, 100 cases of soy sauce, 100 cases of fish sauce with a total budget of over 20,000 Dollars. In addition to donating more than $ 20,000, the third Deputy Prime Minister also donated 20 million riels to the authorities to continue to help flood victims.
On that occasion, Samdech Preah Odom Vongsa, Honorary Dr. Muong Ra, stated that the donation to support the administration of Dangkor district is to implement the strategy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia to help the people affected by The flood of Stung Prek Tno.
At the same time, Ms. Kim Nheb, Governor of Dangkor District, also expressed her happiness and gratitude to Samdech Sangkha and all the monks who have given a lot of gifts to the district administration at this time.
The district governor promised to bring all these gifts to distribute to all the people who are affected by the floods and floods, leaving no one to suffer from hunger.
After handing over the donations and budget to the district governor, Samdech Sang Neak also took a boat trip to check the flood situation of the people and the forces that are helping the people.
According to Ms. Kim Nheb's report, so far, the people living in Dangkor district affected by the Stung Prek Tnaot flood in 42 villages in 11 communes have 4,963 houses, equivalent to 5,587 families.
Ms. Koy Pisey Holds a Meeting with Local Officials in Prey Ampok Commune to Discuss and Solve Some Challenges
(Takeo): Ms. Koy Pisey, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, Deputy Director of the Permanent Secretariat of the National Authority for Border Affairs and Chairperson of Prey Ampok Commune, Kirivong District, Takeo Province, this morning, October 21, 2020. With the commune council to discuss the work and solve some of the challenges that arise in the local area, as well as to participate in the 7-day funeral of her former commune chief Prey Ampok.
The former chief of Prey Ampok commune, Mr. Neang Neang, who worked well for the local community and the people in the commune for many years, died of a disease.
During the ceremony, Ms. Koy Pisey thanked and commended the local commune leaders for their hard work in serving the people in the past and urged the officers to continue to improve this activity. More. She commended all the relevant officials in the commune for their active work in disseminating and informing almost 100 percent of eligible voters to register to vote.
Although Prey Ampok commune has not been affected by floods like some other localities, she urged commune leaders to continue to call on residents to be vigilant, clean and follow the instructions of local authorities. At the same time, she called on people to continue to implement health measures to prevent the spread of Kovid 19, because we can forget Kovid 19, but Kovid 19 never forgets us.
