It should be noted that since 1991-2019, Kayah has provided a grant of approximately 267.7 million US dollars to contribute to the Royal Government of Cambodia in socio-economic development, focusing on four priority areas, including: 1) Water management. And public health, 2) education, 3) rural development, and 4) transportation. In particular, for 2020, KOICA grants to Cambodia totaled 24.5 million US dollars.
