At the same time, Samdech Techo Prime Minister also called on banks and microfinance institutions not to confiscate the property, houses and land of people affected during the Kovid 19 and during the floods.
Once again, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also called on banks and microfinance institutions to seize the assets of those who believe in the instigators of the banking sector in Cambodia by calling on people to withdraw money. From the bank and not to return to the bank, etc., which Samdech supports the confiscation of property if you believe the propaganda of those groups.
The head of the Royal Government said that banking institutions and microfinance institutions doing business need to make a profit, but taking advantage of the hardships of the people is not happy. Samdech hopes that all banks and microfinance institutions will participate in implementing Samdech's call.
Samdech Techo also urged the National Bank of Cambodia and the Ministry of Economy and Finance to continue to advise microfinance institutions and banking institutions to understand the people who lost their income due to Kovid 19 and the floods. .
According to the report of the Committee for Disaster Management, floods are affecting 14,348 families, equivalent to more than 410,000 people, which is not so much that banks and microfinance institutions can not help. Solve that.
