Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications decides to cancel and suspend the licenses of 17 telecom operators
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications has decided to cancel and suspend the licenses of 17 telecom operators who are inactive, such as not having any business activities, no employees, not self-declaring income and other obligations under the terms of the license. And did not provide technical documents. This is according to the announcement of the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications on October 20, 2020, which was received by Fresh News.
The Ministry has instructed the operators whose licenses have been revoked to pay off debts owed by the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications, the Telecommunications Regulator of Cambodia, public-private debts, tax obligations and be liable to employees, customers and third parties in accordance with laws and regulations. Effective in the event of a dispute arising out of or in connection with the revocation of this license.
(Kampong Thom): The Royal Government team in Kampong Thom province told the people that even during the flood and after the flood, the Royal Government and authorities at all levels are still ready to intervene to help the people at all times. After the flood, the team will continue to address the impact on the people, especially the infrastructure system and cultivation.
This statement was made on the occasion of Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group on Kampong Thom Province, and Mr. Sok Loo, Governor of Kampong Thom Province, led the working group and provincial officials to distribute donations. Food and some money to 350 families from 5 communes in Prasat Sambo district on the afternoon of October 20, 2020.
On that occasion, Minister Thong Khon brought the greetings of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to the people that both Samdech always remember and care about. The well-being of the people in all circumstances: "Where there are people suffering, there is the face of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit."
Mr. Thong Khon confirmed that the Royal Government under the leadership of Samdech Techo, the Royal Government working group to visit the local level and the provincial-district authorities did not leave the people suffering, even during the flood and after the flood. Also ready to intervene to help people all the time.
He also called on people to save water for future use and keep it in the fields so that rice can grow well, especially to prepare rice seeds or seeds of other crops to grow next season.
The Minister further reminded the people to take care of their health by eating clean, drinking clean, living clean and hygienic. In addition, it is necessary to adhere to the implementation of safety rules and guidelines of the Ministry of Health in the fight against Kovid-19 well. People are healthy, the health of the nation is strong.
