(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the afternoon of October 20, 2020, ordered to search for the author of a letter of thanks to put in a rice package to cover the banana leaves for the troops who participated in the operation to save people from the flood. Offer special rewards. This was stated by Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, to Fresh News this afternoon.
It should be noted that yesterday, there was a case where people put a letter embedded in the rice package, thanking the army for participating in the rescue operation from the flood in Banteay Meanchey province. This letter belongs to the people in Kork Kathin commune in Thmar Puok district. Kork Kathin commune, as well as the model commune of Thmar Puok and Khok Romiet communes, were severely flooded on the night of October 16, 2020. As of October 19, 2020, the water has not receded.
On the night of October 16, the rescue force of nearly 400 people, which is the military force of the 5th Military Region from the 911 Special Brigade, the Military Force, the 51st Infantry Brigade, the Provincial Military Force, the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Gendarmerie and Police Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice-Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, and Mr. Ou Rathrey, Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, immediately acted to evacuate people and their equipment.
In the flood-hit commune in Thmar Puok district, despite the heavy flooding, they were not evacuated due to the high level of their houses. In particular, the low-income people were evacuated to relatives or neighbors.
In addition to evacuating to high-rise houses, the rescue force also helped to prepare people's belongings to be placed in high places and helped to move rice from the barn to the houses. To this day, rescue teams continue to deploy to help transport people from their homes to other areas, such as hospitals or markets.
This gesture of rescue full of courage and to keep the happiness of the victims as a whole made the victims respect, love and admire all the rescue forces. In return for the rescue force, the people in the back of each house also helped to prepare food and pack for the rescue force.
Among the emotional packages of the victims, a package of rice was found with a copy of the letter. The letter read: "I, Nhean Sambian and my wife, would like to thank all the soldiers who helped save the people of Kork Kathin commune throughout the village. I have no food, only fried eggs, thank you all soldiers.
Emergency rescue is the most important need for victims. Written in a short letter, but full of deep meaning for all rescue forces. It is an expression of gratitude and appreciation for the invaluable rescue force. Samdech Sangha Am Lim Heng Nimon Distributes Donations to 56 Flood Victims in Sangkat Prek Thmey, Khan Chbar Ampov
