Mr. Keo Remy's statement was made on October 20, 2020, when he chaired the third round of the Universal Periodic Review (UPR) Report and Recommendations Workshop. 2020, with the participation of Ms. You Sophea, Deputy Governor of Siem Reap and Mr. Koy Song, Member of the Siem Reap Provincial Board of Governors, as well as more than 100 government officials and the armed forces at the Empress Angkor Hotel in Siem Reap.
"The adoption of the UPR Recommendation demonstrates the Royal Government's commitment to the protection and promotion of human rights, and the Government needs to disseminate the UPR Recommendations at the national and sub-national levels," the Cambodian human rights chief said. "National, so that all relevant ministries, departments and institutions implement this recommendation to improve the field of human rights."
The purpose of this workshop is to disseminate the UPR report and the UPR recommendations that Cambodia accepts. In addition, Cambodia passed the UPR report on January 30, 2019, with 73 participating countries making 198 recommendations, with Cambodia accepting 173 recommendations and making 25 remarks.
Mr. Keo Remy, Chairman of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, stated that the UPR report is a report on the human condition of the member states of the United Nations. Every five years, Cambodia defended its first report in 2009, its second in 2014 and its third in 2019.
Mr. Keo Remy said that under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, the Royal Government pays attention to the protection as well as the promotion of human rights and has improved the human rights situation with recognition and evaluation. High for Cambodia. For example, the adoption of the 9 out of 11 conventions and conventions that Cambodia has adopted and is one of the leading countries in the ASEAN region.
Mr. Keo Remy said that the opening of the Office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights in 1992 and the presence of the United Nations Special Rapporteur on Cambodia to date have made Cambodia one of the countries in the world. Among other countries, openness to human rights issues, respect for conventions, conventions, laws and the rule of law, as well as all rights and freedoms of citizens.
