According to a report read by Lt. Gen. Tan Sok Vichea, director of the Secretariat of the Anti-Counterfeit Products Committee, the Secretariat summed up the committee's performance in the first nine months of 2020 to crack down on illegal drugs, medical products and drugs. A total of 134 cases of counterfeit products, equivalent to 594..65 tons.
Lt. Gen. Tan Sok Vichea said that among the crackdowns include:
* 1: Statistics by product type: 19 cases of medicine, 19 cases of 19 anti-Kovid medicine products, 35 cases of food and beverage products, 35 cases of cosmetic products, 29 cases of consumer products, 20 cases of consumer products and 19 cases of tobacco products.
* 2: Statistics by provinces: Phnom Penh 111 cases, Kandal 11 cases, Kampong Speu 2 cases, Takeo 1 case, Sihanoukville 2 cases, Battambang 1 case, Kampong Cham 1 case, Tbong Khmum 4 cases and Svay Rieng 1 case.
