On the morning of October 20, 2020, floods hit Poipet City due to the collapse of the O'Khaidon Dam by Tycoon Kok An, which caused even more flooding.
Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice-Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, immediately led a working group to evacuate people to find a safe place to stay temporarily. Mr. Ngor Mengchruon said that all the victims were safe, but the number of victims has not been determined.
Mr. Ngor Meng Chruon confirmed that "all intervention forces have successfully transported the victims to safety. "The construction of the dam is technical, but the amount of water is not known in advance, because natural disasters every year are not the same."
