This project, after construction, is very important in reducing floods across the Cambodian-Thai border in the border areas of Malai, Poipet, O'Chrov and Serey Sophorn, Banteay Meanchey province, especially to be able to supply enough water for family use and have Irrigation potential on rice cultivation area is about 34,600 hectares.
On the morning of October 20, 2020, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen traveled to Banteay Meanchey to visit and support about 20,000 families affected by the floods. . Samdech Techo stated that Banteay Meanchey is the province that suffered the most and the longest, which needs to be given priority to rescue and rehabilitate after the flood.
The Okay Don Dam is a dam designed to store water for extraction into clean water for the people of Poipet to use. Rainwater and runoff from Thailand must flow into the dam. According to reports, the dam can store up to millions of cubic meters of water.
The collapse of the O'Khaidon Dam caused the water in the dam to overflow into flooded rice fields and people's villages. The village of Sorya village, Nimmit commune, Poipet city was severely flooded.
Surya village, this virtual commune, was not flooded during the recent floods and floods from Thailand. But on the morning of October 20, 2020, the water flowing from the O'Khaidon Dam quickly flooded Sorya village.
Residents rushed to evacuate their children and animals to safety. As people's villages were being submerged, rescue forces from Lt. Gen. Sam Oun's 5th Army and Lt. Gen. Chap Pheakdey's Special Forces, police and police forces in Banteay Meanchey Province immediately launched an operation to evacuate residents. Well.
During the operation, Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, who is leading the rescue operation in Banteay Meanchey province, also visited the flooded area to inspect and manage the rescue operation.
As of noon on October 20, 2020, the dam has not been re-sealed and the flooding of villages has intensified. Ngor Meng Chrouh, deputy governor of Banteay Meanchey province, told Fresh News at the flooded site that no way to close the dam had yet been found due to the floodwaters. Authorities are mobilizing to help evacuate people to safety.
Please note that until October 20, 2020, Banteay Meanchey is one of the provinces that were flooded almost all provinces, especially in the city of Poipet, which is flooding. At the same time, many authorities are burning their hands and feet to save the people.
Lt. Gen. Sam Oun, Deputy Commander of the Army and Commander of the 5th Army Division, and Lt. Gen. Chap Pheakdey, Commander of the Special Forces Command (formerly 911 Parachute Brigade) are leading hundreds of military forces to rescue the victims. Flood attacks.
During the inspection of the water flow on National Road No. 5 after the collapse of the O'Kaidon Dam this morning, October 20, 2020, Lt. Gen. Chap Pheakdey and Lt. Gen. Sam Oun reaffirmed their strong and courageous determination to Carry out rescue operations because the army is the children of the people.
In a live interview with Fresh News, the two military leaders also claimed that both units, the Special Forces Command and the 5th Army Division, had been sent to the victims since the floods. First, since October 12, 2020. He said the rescue operation was not slowing down, no matter how difficult the situation.
Lt. Gen. Chap Pheakdey said that the force of the Special Forces Command involved in the operation was 100 people and 25 vehicles, along with many other rescue equipment. While Lt. Gen. Sam Oun confirmed that more than 100 troops from the 5th Military Command participated in the rescue to be sent to Poipet.
The commanders of the two units pointed out that all rescue forces were divided into two groups, one standing on the national road where the water flows and the other part going down by boat to rescue the people who were flooded in the village. And evacuate them to a safe place organized by the authorities.
However, in the course of this operation, both Lt. Gen. Chap Pheakdey and Lt. Gen. Sam Oun were equally committed to the fact that the army is highly committed to enforcing the order, and where there are difficulties, the army always saves the people. The people are the parents of the army, the backbone of the army, and the army must always protect the peace and survival of the people.
