(Phnom Penh): Mr. Peng Giren Kassmeyhan Peng Giren Tha Hee, Ambassador of the Kingdom of Brunei Darussalam to Cambodia, visited the "Samdech Mey Library" of the Documentation Institute of the Documentation Center of Cambodia this morning, October 20, 2020.
Brunei is one of the ASEAN countries with a monarchy, a monarch and a monarch. Brunei has always provided indirect support to the work of the Documentation Center of Cambodia in conducting research on the Cham people in Cambodia.
Brunei adheres to Islam. It should be recalled that since its inception, the Documentation Center of Cambodia has employed about 15% of the total Muslim staff.
The staff, who are of Cham Muslim descent, have studied, written and published books related to their community. The book "Memories of Cham Muslim Women on the Stories of the Khmer Rouge" is the work of Sopharina, Deputy Director of the Documentation Center of Cambodia.
DC-Cam is the first institution that has cared for and worked with the Khmer Muslim community since 1995 through oral history by visiting all mosques in Cambodia. . The Documentation Center of Cambodia provided documents to the Extraordinary Chambers in the Courts of Cambodia for the trial of senior leaders of the Khmer Rouge regime.
Youk Chhang, director of the Documentation Center of Cambodia, has been on a mission in Iraq to gather evidence of international crime in his specialty to participate in the trial of former Iraqi President Saddam Hussein.
During the two-hour visit, Mr. Youk Chhang described the exhibition of the relics of King Norodom Sihanouk and the Royal Family, the library room containing thousands of books, photographs, audio files, digital archives of the Documentation Center of Cambodia, An exhibition on the background and meaning of the Leaf Institute building design and the Leaf Institute building design by Zaha Hadid, a world-renowned female architect.
In addition, Ms. Sofarina presented research sites, research centers and libraries of the Khmer Rouge in the 10 provinces. The Documentation Center of Cambodia team and guests then discussed issues related to the challenges facing Cambodia's ethnic minorities and peacekeeping in the local community.
At the end of the visit, Ambassador Peng Giren Kashmir Han Peng Giren Tahi, Representative of the Honorary Delegation and the Embassy of the Kingdom of Brunei Darussalam in Cambodia, presented a memorandum on the Golden Book of "Samdech Mey Library" which reads as follows: :
"Thank you for this wonderful experience and visit. This is a wonderful experience for me to understand the history and the fact that the King Father is an important part of history.
