General Knowledge: Former Malaysian leader Mahathir reveals four habits that lead to longevity and agility despite old age
1: Proper eating habits The most important thing that we can maintain good health is to have good eating habits. We should eat to live, not to eat. Our bodies do not need much food, except for those who are young and growing. For them, food is required to ensure good physical growth. However, that amount still does not exceed what the body needs.
Flatulence is a disorder that is affecting more and more children and adolescents. Belly fat is not good for health and survival.
Young people, especially teenagers, want to keep their bodies clean, even if they eat a lot. But if the body shows a growing belly, they should know that they are eating more than their body needs.
Stomach problems usually start to appear when you are 40 years old. The tendency towards belly fat at this age is to eat as many delicious foods as possible. When food is delicious, it makes people eat more.
Our stomachs get bigger as we eat more. As a result, as the stomach gets bigger, more food is needed to relieve hunger. Eating too much will make us gain weight.
The body absorbs food and converts it into fat, which is distributed throughout the body. Tummy tuck is not a good thing for health. With such a large body, the heart has to work hard to provide blood and absorb nutrients for this overweight body. High blood pressure brings with it all the symptoms and diseases associated with high blood pressure.
Fat is distributed to the arteries and narrows them. Blood flow may be blocked, heart attack may occur, and sometimes it can be severe. Therefore, to avoid high blood pressure, you must eat less and not make yourself fat.
In addition to the heart, all other organs of the body, namely the liver, kidneys and pancreas, you should consider taking care of. Any of these organs can be damaged and shortened.
2: The habit of not being idle Personal hygiene is very important. Today, people brush their teeth regularly. Cleaning your mouth and brushing your teeth after eating is a good thing. At least brushing your teeth before going to bed is a good activity.
The nature of the human body is that all parts need to be used at all times to keep them healthy and functioning properly. If it is not used or taken care of, it will wither and lose its ability to function.
The best example is muscle. If they are used regularly, they will evolve and function well. We see this through muscle building exercises. Their muscles grow very well and they exercise regularly. On the other hand, those who do not exercise often lead to weakness, weakness and weakness.
People who like to rest almost all the time should observe themselves that they are weak and just get up every time they seem to have no strength at all. They could not walk very far, and they could not run much. This is because their muscle strength decreases because they never use it.
We see this among the elderly. They are often inactive and prefer to sit or relax. Soon they will be weak. Those who like to relax in bed are more likely to be weak. Their health is deteriorating. They can not resist common diseases.
Not only will they experience muscle weakness, but the bones will become weak because they are not used. These bones are fragile and can break easily if they come in contact with something.
To get rid of this problem, older people should get more exercise. They should do some walking and exercise as well. They will feel drowsy, but they have to resist the urge to sleep for hours, especially to avoid getting too much sleep every night. Sleeping during the day for a while does not affect anything, but sleeping for a long time will weaken the body.
What we do for the muscles of the body, it benefits the brain as well. If the brain is not used, it also loses the same function. Alzheimer's disease is more common in the elderly. Spelling may get worse.
It is very easy for people to forget the objects and faces of others. Dementia may worsen due to the tendency to age. When we tell them something, the word will not last long. In fact, immediately after the answer, the same question can be asked again. These are signs of aging.
To prevent mental retardation, it is necessary to engage in conversation, reading and writing, resolving disputes with others, and advocating. Those who do these things will maintain a lot of brain function even as they get older.
Reading storybooks is a wonderful activity. It improves memory and the ability to form sentences to speak. You will remember many words that can help you to read again and again easily.
3: The habit of reading the newspaper regularly when you speak or give a speech, memorizing words and other sentences can easily come from the mind. If someone does not read a book or who rarely reads when saying something, then the words to say do not come automatically. Technical terms in a subject will be difficult to remember when you want to speak or give a speech, for example, a scientific word or a word used in economics.
Reading the newspaper every day also stimulates the brain and also improves the ability to form words and sentences to speak.
It is common for older people to remember past and present incidents, but these memories can be enhanced if the person is in the habit of reading and speaking regularly.
4: The habit of standing and sitting upright. Other physical damage associated with old age is the curvature of the back. This curvature can be reduced or avoided by sitting or standing upright. It also helps prevent loss of height. Horseback riding can help reduce this problem because when riding a horse you sit with your body straight.
At all times, stand up straight like a military officer. At the same time, when walking, it is necessary to move in a straight back. Aligning your spine in this way strengthens your bones and prevents you from falling.
