He said that while the world was worried and fighting against Kovid-19 and Cambodia was facing floods, the prince paid the utmost attention to the vulnerable people at the local level because of the effects of Kovid-19. Has affected the economy and livelihood of the people in the daily business, especially the elderly, homeless, orphans, poor widows, many children, people living with HIV and the disabled.
Also, be on the lookout for new infections, such as bird flu and dengue fever, which are transmitted by mosquitoes, even young children or adults need to be protected from dengue fever and dengue fever. Cheek by cleaning around the house, get rid of tiger mosquitoes, wear long clothes and sleep under a mosquito net day or night.
Mr. Tea Seiha also thanked the people in Siem Reap City whose residential plots affected the development of 38 roads and participated in the demolition of houses for the benefit of all to improve. The beauty of the city, tourism, culture, nature, history and the improvement of people's lives in the future.
He also reminded all people to be careful of children and families when there is a flood, and to adhere to hygiene, clean the house, eat clean water, boiled water, etc. to avoid other diseases. Sleep under a mosquito net to clean the environment around the house to get rid of tiger mosquitoes, but if in doubt, please hurry to the nearest health center for consultation and treatment in time.
On the other hand, respect the new road traffic law to protect your life and the lives of your family, reduce traffic accidents and educate your children to stay away from drugs, and please hurry to grow crops after Water to increase daily life even more.
Donation to 116 families, each family received 30 kg of rice, 1 kit, 1 mat, 1 box of noodles, 1 box of fish, 4 bottles of soy sauce, 2 cans, 2 bars of soap, 1 plastic tent and 10 budget Ten thousand Riel. Mr. Ang Vong Vathana and Mr. Keut Rith, as well as leaders of the Ministry of Justice, marched to Wat Katom Phluk and Wat Sovanratanaram to collect the construction of Chan School.
