He added that the completion of the 2020 voter registration was completed on October 19, 2020, does not mean that the process of reviewing the voter list and the 2020 voter registration is completely closed, because there are still procedures. Many more to come.
"We have completed the commune registration, but this does not mean that the entire voter registration and 2020 registration process has been completely shut down, there are still many procedures to follow," said Hal Sarath. "
He added that further procedures include:
* Nationwide voter registration results summary * Resolution of related complaints * NEC review and decision on voter registration results and data to prepare the first voter list * Posting of initial voter list and voter list The person who will be removed from the voter list * The submission of the settlement of complaints related to the initial voter list * The decision and official validation of the 2020 voter list.
According to Hal Sarath, the deadline for official review and validation of the 2020 voter list is December 31, 2020, after the completion of all procedures and resolution of relevant complaints. As of October 18, 2020, the NEC has received a total of 103 complaints.
