Please be informed that for the 200 flood-affected families, each family received 1 box of noodles and 1 fishing rod and handed over 100 tents to the provincial authorities to be handed over to the flood victims. Newborns receive an additional $ 100. The Director General of the Rural Development Bank encourages farmers to replant safe vegetables after the flood, if there is a lack of capital, they can apply for an interest loan of only 0.42% per month!
(Banteay Meanchey): On the morning of October 19, 2020, under the coordination of Khmer Safe Vegetable Company, Mr. Kao Thach, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Rural Development Bank and Agriculture and his colleagues presided over the talk program with A total of 191 people from Banteay Meanchey, Oddar Meanchey and Battambang provinces grow safe vegetables.
The Director General expressed his regret that your crops were damaged by the floods last week.
He encouraged the community to replant and increase cultivation and expand cultivation after the water recedes to compensate for losses and supply the market in a timely manner.
Mr. Kao Thach shared economic news, local agricultural news and the experience of successful farming abroad to inform the community and encourage them to expand their cultivation.
The Director General encouraged and advised the community to grow safe vegetables with a clear plan and specific goals to supply the market in a sustainable and valuable way, and please avoid growing vegetables together, which is why every harvest is always Falling prices. At the same time, he asked the community to change their cultivation habits to be flexible and understand market information from agricultural products.
Mr. Kao Thach encouraged the farming community in the name of entrepreneurship to do business to improve their lives and health, not to farm for their own food, family and non-standard.
He asked the community to sign a contract to buy and sell safe vegetables with Sovath Khmer Vegetable Company to ensure that their community has a clear market and guaranteed contract price. However, the Director General requested that you improve the quality of cultivation and respect the quality and safety standards.
At the same time, Mr. Kao Thach disseminated the loan policy with a low interest rate of 0.42% per month to the vegetable growing community and encouraged the community to contact the Rural Development Bank and Agriculture in case of need for credit.
The Director General also thanked the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Administration for facilitating the location for the Rural Development and Agriculture Bank to host the program today. At the same time, he distributed 10 kilograms of rice per person and also donated some money during the current flood. More than 2,000 people registered to vote in 2020
