The report of the National Committee for Disaster Management on October 18, 2020 said that the floods affected 19 capitals and provinces, equivalent to 71 cities / districts / Khans. The affected capitals and provinces are: Phnom Penh, Pursat, Pailin, Banteay Meanchey, Phnom Penh, Battambang, Svay Rieng, Oddar Meanchey, Siem Reap, Takeo, Kampong Speu, Mondulkiri, Sihanoukville, Koh Kong, Preah Vihear, Stung Treng, Kampong Cham, Kandal, Kampong Chhnang and Kampong Thom.
The report also said that the floods affected more than 60,000 families and nearly 8,000 families, or nearly 30,000 people, were evacuated.
Banteay Meanchey, a province, is also being severely affected by the floods. Banteay Meanchey provincial governor Oum Rath said that six cities / districts were severely flooded, including Serey Sophorn, Poipet, Mongkul Borei, Thmor Puok, O'Chrov and Malai districts. Oum Rath said the floods had affected 15,000 families and displaced 2,700.
In response to the problems posed by the floods, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has ordered the authorities at both the national and sub-national levels to join forces to help the people. The main goal is to save the lives of the people from the floods, evacuate them to safety, and then prepare food and other necessities for the affected people.
In response to the order of Samdech Techo, the Commander-in-Chief of the Disaster Battlefield, national, sub-national, local authorities, both in Phnom Penh and in the provinces, were flooded with the help of the three types of armed forces. Acting diligently to rescue people affected by the floods.
In addition to rescuing the victims, the evacuees were provided with food and other supplies by the authorities. Not only people were evacuated to safety, people with high houses and not yet evacuated to safety were also distributed by the authorities at the back of the house.
All these activities made the affected people very satisfied and also helped them to be warm. Ms. Narin, a resident of Neang Ket village, Russey Krok commune, Mongkul Borei district, told Fresh News that since the floods, the authorities have been on a regular basis to evacuate people to safety and provide them with food.
Another flood victim in Neang Ket village, Duong Cha, also saw that the authorities were paying close attention to the well-being and hardships of the people during the floods.
Both Ms. Narin and Ms. Duong Cha said that although they were affected by the floods, she was warm when the authorities took care of them.
