(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) held a meeting with stakeholders on the morning of October 19, 2020 on the provisional results of the voter list review, transmission of provisional results. Examination of voter list and voter registration to the NEC Complaints related to voter registration and initial voter list preparation. This is according to the announcement of the NEC.
The meeting will be held at 10:00 AM on October 19, 2020 at the first floor conference hall of the NEC, National Assembly Street, Sangkat Tonle Bassac, Khan Chamkarmon, Phnom Penh.
The following is the announcement of the NEC: Today is the last day of the voter registration and verification process! Cambodians of all ages are invited to register to vote.
(Phnom Penh): October 19, 2020 is the last day of the process of reviewing the voter list and voter registration 2020, organized by the National Election Committee (NEC).
The NEC has announced that the process of reviewing the 2020 voter list and registration will take only 19 days.
To serve the 2020 voter list and voter registration review, the NEC has set up service offices in 1,646 commune halls across the country.
In order to register to vote, Cambodian citizens of either sex born on or before January 1, 2003 must have an ID card. If you do not have an ID card, go to the Commune / Sangkat Hall to get your ID card for voter registration.
Please be reminded that voter registration is very important for people to have the right to participate in the Commune / Sangkat Council Election in 2022 and the National Assembly Election in 2023. If not registered on the voter list prepared by the NEC, Cambodians of both sexes will not be eligible to vote.
The NEC calls on Cambodians of both sexes born before or before January 1, 2003 to go and register to vote and check the voter list.
Please note that the NEC regularly checks the voter list and voter registration every year to provide opportunities for citizens over the age of 18 to vote. According to the NEC, in the last voter list by 2019, there were 8,629,357 registered voters.
For 2020, according to population statistics and the estimated number of polling stations, the NEC plans to register 300,390 new voters.
Lt. Gen. Dy Vichea and Ms. Hun Mana Donate Food to Rescue Forces Operating in Banteay Meanchey Province
(Banteay Meanchey): Lt. Gen. Di Vichea, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police, and Ms. Hun Mana provided a total of 2,000 cases of food to the National Committee for Disaster Management to be distributed to rescue forces operating in Banteay Meanchey province.
