The food donation was handed over to the Special Forces Command of Lt. Gen. Chap Pheakdey, the Infantry Brigade and the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Military Operations Area. Each of these three units received 200 cases of noodles, 100 cases of caramel drinks and 7 cases of large fish.
On the occasion of receiving this food donation, Mr. Sok Sreng and Ms. Sroy Thida also contributed 20 million Riels to support the working group of the National Committee. In addition, Caritas Cambodia has provided 250 tents for Banteay Meanchey and 250 for Pursat.
Mr. Kim Sopharun and Mr. Kim Virak, Representative of Senior Minister Kun Kim, have already distributed this tent to the province and the army. After handing over and receiving, Mr. Kim Sopharun and Mr. Kim Virak organized and pitched tents for the victims to make them safe and avoid various diseases.
Senior Minister Kun Kim thanked Lt. Gen. Dy Vichea and Ms. Hun Mana for always paying attention to the plight of the victims and resolving them in a timely manner.
Senior Minister Kun Kim stated that Ms. Hun Mana is a Cambodian woman full of humanitarian heart. The Senior Minister praised Ms. Hun Mana's humanitarian gestures for Cambodian society. Especially in the current crisis caused by the floods, Ms. Hun Mana not only helped the people, but she also did her best to help the rescue forces.
On behalf of the receiving force, Senior Minister Kun Kim thanked General Dy Vichea and Ms. Hun Mana for always supporting the activities of the National Committee for Disaster Management and always helping the victims. HE Veng Sakhon and Lok Chumteav Donate $ 10,000 to Samdech Techo Hun Sen to Help Flood Victims
