Director General of Rural Development Bank urges millers to unite to achieve 1 million tonnes rice export target as Royal Government adds $ 30 million to rice sector
(Battambang): On the evening of October 18, 2020, under the coordination of Dr. Oknha Phu Puy, Mr. Kao Thach, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture, presided over a meeting with the mill owners. Coming from Banteay Meanchey and Battambang.
For the coming rice harvest season, Mr. Kao Thach would like to encourage and continue to encourage all mill owners to buy rice from farmers as much as possible at an affordable price, whether the quality of rice is good or not so good, especially rice. Which suffered flooding due to heavy rains.
He strongly hopes that all mill owners will work together in solidarity to improve farmers' livelihoods and boost the successful export of 1 million tonnes of rice. At the same time, the Director General informed the mill owners that with the trust from the Royal Government, the Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture has received an additional special fund of 30 million US dollars to provide loans to mill owners to purchase rice from Farmers in the upcoming harvest.
He encouraged millers to apply for a loan from the Rural Development and Agriculture Bank only when they meet the bank's qualifications.
The Director General requested all mill owners to prepare a standard and accountable list. Therefore, he asked the list company to present the main points and conditions to provide information to the mill owners as well.
At the same time, he encouraged millers to use the accounting software of the listed companies, which are established by Cambodian children and have sufficient credible credentials.
The Director General requested all mill owners to be united, not to compete with each other and work together to promote Cambodia's rice sector with prosperity and prosperity. Meanchey to help the poor and vulnerable
