Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen calls on people to be very careful about health and safety during floods
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, called on people affected by floods throughout the country to be very careful about health and safety during the floods.
This statement was made by Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen on the occasion of Samdech Techo PM's representative visiting and distributing gifts to 3,384 flood victims in Dangkor district, Phnom Penh this morning. This October.
Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen continued, "During the floods, we saw that there were 20 drowning deaths. From October 1-18, we all have It is with great sadness and condolences to the bereaved family. "Therefore, I urge our people, especially the guardians of all children, to be very careful in taking care of their children so that they do not drown."
Also, during floods or receding water, to avoid diseases such as diarrhea, poisoning and other diseases, drink clean water by boiling water or using water with chlorine. Wash your hands often with soap before and after eating and after using the toilet.
In particular, to clean the body by bathing, washing soap, washing hair and washing clothes to avoid skin diseases, blisters and itching, etc. by the flood.
