(Phnom Penh): In the first nine months of 2020, rangers cracked down on crime and confiscated 433 chainsaws, 9 cars, 106 bulldozers, 46 motorbikes, confiscated 303 cubic meters of wood, removed 1 trap, 677 traps and confiscated 10 recycled guns. This is according to Mr. Net Pheaktra, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Environment on October 18, 2020.
The spokesman for the Ministry of Environment added that in the first nine months of 2020, from January to September 2020, park officials and the protected area community patrolled 1,823 times during the patrol operation. 954 cases were cracked and 40 cases were built and sent to the court to educate and sign contracts, 420 cases were suspended and 41 cases were fined.
Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment Net Pheaktra stated: “In the past nine months, rangers have cracked down on crime and confiscated 433 chainsaws, nine cars, 106 bulldozers and 46 motorbikes and confiscated 303 meters of timber. "We removed 1,677 traps and confiscated and confiscated 103 recycled guns."
He stressed that this is the effort of park officials and the community of protected areas to protect and conserve natural resources in Prey Lang for generations to come.
At the same time, the Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment also said that despite the night and day crackdowns and crackdowns by park rangers and members of the protected area community, small-scale natural resource crimes such as logging, logging and encroachment Land ownership, poaching and trapping continue to occur in Prey Lang, which needs to be prevented and suppressed.
He said that the Royal Government of Cambodia and development partners are implementing action plans to improve the conservation of biodiversity and ecological status in the Prey Lang Wildlife Sanctuary, as well as to create sustainability and equity of economic opportunities, community livelihoods and Natural capital for reinvestment in the Prey Lang Wildlife Sanctuary and the protected areas around Prey Lang.
