Tehran: The Iranian Ministry of Foreign Affairs has announced that the United Nations (UN) arms embargo banning Tehran from buying and selling weapons has been lifted in accordance with the 2015 Iran nuclear deal. This is according to the release by the Chinese news agency Xinhua.
"As of Sunday, all restrictions on the transfer of weapons, including financial services to and from Iran, will be lifted," the Iranian Foreign Ministry said in a statement issued on Sunday. "Automatic." The ministry added that the Iranian side did not need to take any special action as the arms embargo was automatically lifted in the absence of further measures or delays by the UN Security Council.
