The six affected districts are: Serei Sophorn, Poipet, Mongkul Borei, O'Chrov, Thmor Puok and Malai. The three districts that have not been severely affected are: Phnom Srok, Svay Chek and Preah Net Preah districts. Legal Awareness: Termination of Contract
(Phnom Penh): Last week, the Legal Awareness Program brought up the topic of contract termination, but for this week, the Legal Awareness Program brings up the topic of contract annulment.
As we all know, the law gives the parties the freedom to agree on a contract, but any contract that goes against the law will be null and void. What are the reasons for the contract to be annulled?
Therefore, the legal awareness program of FRESH NEWS in collaboration with the Cambodian Bar Association for International Cooperation would like to raise the topic of "annulment of the contract" to the following students:
According to the provisions of the Civil Code, the reasons that lead to the annulment of the contract include: False will; Contradiction to enforced provisions; Contrary to public order and good customs and contrary to the form of law.
Contradiction to enforceable provisions: Refers to the meaning of a contract that constitutes any contradictory enforcement. Mandatory provisions refer to any provisions that the law requires to be strictly enforced, otherwise the law does not recognize the legal force of that action. For example, the law strictly prohibits the creation of a final mortgage contract.
Contrary to public order and good customs: refers to the meaning of a contract that is contrary to public order and good customs. The meaning or content agreed upon by the parties can be a drug trafficking contract and a sex contract or a pregnancy contract.
For the annulment of the contract is divided into 2 (two) types: absolute annulment and non-absolute annulment. Absolute annulment is like a contract that is contrary to the provisions of coercion or contrary to public order and completely good customs, such as in the case of a contracting party killing a person, meaning that all parts of the contract are annulled.
Non-absolute annulment refers to the meaning of a contract that is contrary to the provisions of coercion or contrary to public order and good customs, which leads to the annulment of the contract only to the contrary.
The person entitled to claim the annulment of the contract, according to Article 357 of the Civil Code, stipulates that if the meaning of the action is contrary to the provisions of coercion or contrary to public order and good customs, any person can claim the annulment of the contract. .
In the event that the act is considered null and void due to the action contrary to the form required by this code or any other law, any person can claim the nullity of the contract.
If the contract is annulled for any reason, the contract is considered invalid from the beginning (validity is not recognized from the beginning). In the event that the contract is annulled, the party providing the trustee may reclaim it through unreasonable progress or exercise the right to reclaim it on the basis of ownership rights.
However, in the case of a contract that is annulled for reasons contrary to public order and good customs and laws relating to public order, the parties may not make a claim for the return of the contract, as the contract of the contract may be a contract. Illegal, such as drug contracts, sex trafficking contracts.
In conclusion, the annulment of a contract is enshrined in the 2007 Civil Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia, which is a mechanism used to prove that a contract made has a meaning contrary to the provisions enforced by force or contrary to the form of law or contrary to law or order. Public and customary goodwill or false will is considered a powerless contract from the beginning, that is, no contract arises.
Therefore, in order for a contract to be effective or legally valid, the parties should study the legal aspects before proceeding with the creation of a contract to avoid the contract being created and subject to annulment.
