(Prey Veng): The Boeung Sneh Toul Poontali Conservation Area, a popular eco-tourism resort in Prey Veng province, is experiencing an increase in the number of tens of thousands of birds flying to lay their eggs throughout the flooded forest, while communities on conservation in the area That is a very small number can not patrol all the corners.
This has made the community leader concerned about the safety of the birds for fear of being snatched, eaten or sold.
He was concerned about the safety of the birds, as only five community conservationists could not move to the area where the eggs hatched, and the area was flooded. Give opportunists easy access to catch animals.
Mr. Pan Yun confirmed that in the area of Tuol Porn Tali, where tourists used to visit and watch the birds, it was completely flooded and there were not many tourists.
Please be informed that the Royal Government has decided to support the project to establish and preserve the Boeung Sneh Toul Poun Tali area, which is about 4,000 hectares in Ba Phnom district, Prey Veng province, a multi-use area that benefits the people in the area and the neighbors, especially to participate. Height of eco-tourism in the province.
