(Prey Veng): Mr. Sar Sokha, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and Deputy Chairman of the Working Group of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) in Prey Veng Province, on the afternoon of October 17, 2020, visited and talked with the families of martyrs 111 families living in Sithor Kandal district, Prey Veng province.
Speaking on that occasion, Mr. Sar Sokha reminded of the heroic example and great merits of all heroes and warriors, especially relatives of uncles, aunts, grandparents in Sithor Kandal district, who sacrificed bravely and sacrificed fresh meat. Fresh blood to exchange for peace for our beloved motherland.
"Even though the country is now completely peaceful, the CPP-led government has not forgotten the merits of the warriors and their families," he added. Mr. Sar Sokha also called on the families of veterans, victims and victims to continue to maintain the spirit of patriotism and together protect the peace that we have found so hard not to lose.
Finally, in relation to Kovid 19, Mr. Sar Sokha reminded the people to protect themselves and implement sanitary measures regularly according to the instructions of the Ministry of Health.
He brought gifts to the families of 111 martyrs and victims, each family received 20 kg of rice, 1 box of noodles, 1 stick of fish sauce, 1 stick of soy sauce, 1 kg of sugar, 1 kg of salt And a budget of 20,000 riels. Krousar Troop Village in Preah Vihear Province's Choam Ksan District Flooded by Heavy Rain, Military Forces Intervene to Help People
(Preah Vihear): Sangke Lech village at point 42 in Kantuot commune, Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province was affected by floods, flooding roads and houses of military families on the evening of October 16. And until October 17.
After receiving information about the flooding of the village and receiving orders from Lieutenant General Srey Duek, Deputy Commander of the Army and Commander of the 3rd Intervention Brigade, Major General Chou Tong An, Commander Deputy Intervention Division 3 gathered the pants to lead the engineering brigade, Intervention Division 3 intervened to help people all night.
Major General Zhu Tong An confirmed that the flood situation that flooded Sangke village at the 42nd point of flooding had flooded the houses of many military families and paved the red paved road for more than 100 meters. The water flowed at the same time, affecting some crops and poultry.
At the same time, Major General Chu Tong An advised the people to be careful to protect their property from being lost by the flood, especially to guide their young children not to visit the water for fear of danger.
Ratanakkiri Provincial Police is ready to intervene to rescue people during the floods
