Former pagoda chief arrested in Prey Nob district, Preah Sihanouk province after being found stealing, producing and storing child pornography
(Preah Sihanouk): A former pagoda chief in Ota Pong village, O'Oknha Heng commune, Prey Nob district, Preah Sihanouk province, was arrested by the police in connection with the theft and production of child pornography for children under 18 years old.
Lt. Gen. Chea Pov, Director of the Technology Crimes Department of the National Police General Commission, told Fresh News on the afternoon of October 17, 2020 that the operation took place on October 14, 2020 under the order Directly from General Dr. Neth Savoeun, General Commissioner of the National Police.
It should be noted that this operation was carried out by the competent force of the Department of Technology Crimes led by Lt. Gen. Chea Pov, Director of the Department, with the coordination of the Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh and Sihanoukville Provincial Prosecutor's Office in collaboration with the Sihanoukville Provincial Police. And the provincial Department of Cults and Religions.
The former pagoda chief, who was detained by police, was identified as 37-year-old Nonnimol, a resident of Ota Pang village, O'Ohnha Heng commune, Prey Nob district, Sihanoukville province. After questioning and listening to the suspects, the specialized force of the department prepared the case file and sent the suspects to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for legal proceedings.
