Please be informed that Kampong Thom is a potential province in agriculture with a total population of about 800,000 people, 80% of whom are farmers.
There are 10 operating banking institutions, 6 deposit microfinance institutions and 9 non-deposit microfinance institutions. The supply and demand for cash to facilitate economic activity in the province has increased significantly in the last two decades, especially the use of the riel has risen rapidly to a level similar to the use of the US dollar.
In fact, in the first 9 months of 2020, the demand for Riel from the branch of the National Bank of Cambodia in Kampong Thom province was 440 billion Riel (approximately 107 million USD) and the branch also received 511 billion Riel from customers. 125 million US dollars) compared to 132 million US dollars.
