(Phnom Penh): Cambodia has established the first SME competition program to attract the participation of start-ups and enterprises with many years of experience, companies that will invest and famous speakers in related fields to participate in promoting the sector. These SMEs to grow.
The arrangement will also boost investment funding for small and medium-sized enterprises to enable them to grow strongly as well as expand their business in one of the most developed countries. Fast economy in Asia.
Eligible conditions include:
First, this competition program is open for companies registered in Cambodia.
Second, small and medium enterprises with the following components are encouraged to apply. A small enterprise is an enterprise with a staff of 11-50 workers or a starting capital of between 50,000-250,000 USD. Medium-sized enterprises are enterprises with 51-100 employees or initial capital between 250,000-500,000 USD. A large enterprise is an enterprise with a staff of 100 or more or a capital of $ 500,000 or more.
Third: Applicants must be able to provide relevant information such as business plan concepts, management team and business model working group, fundraising plan, SWOT analysis, financial planning report from 3- 5 years and other projects.
Fourth, the application must not exceed the deadline and have sufficient information and documents, otherwise the candidate company will not be selected and participate in the next round.
Fifth, the bidding company must ensure that all information submitted is accurate, up-to-date and complete.
Sixth, the business should be something that can expand and have a reputation. Not in a restricted area, no legal issues, lawsuits and lawsuits, and being highly responsible for social and environmental impacts and / or having good CSR principles.
Seventh, the short presentation of the business should be in English and the presenter can speak this language.
The documents required to apply include:
1: The company's legal documents, such as the latest patent, business license, permit from the relevant ministry or authority, company statute, etc.
2: Certificate of Identity or Authorization on behalf of the Company in the process of participating in this competition (if the representative is not the owner or director of the company.
3: Identity documents of the representative.
4: Brief presentation of business.
5: The business plan should also specify: * Business concept * Management team * Business model Five-year business plan with the demonstration of market potential, source of revenue and sustainability * Demand and use of capital * Time of the business model Being in a position to benefit from the innovation of something that will replace an existing market.
6: Fill in the required information by applying online and be sure to complete it.
For the prize to be received:
* The final three winners will receive a Certificate of Qualification, as well as the right to receive up to US $ 1,000,000 in investment cycles of business cycle from PVCC.
* Twelve companies were shortlisted for the finals, all of which were required to speak on the objectives of their business plan and to demonstrate their ability to answer all relevant questions. Clear and appropriate for business plan. The Company reserves the right to select a replacement winner in the event that this requirement is not met.
* The funding cycle for the top three winners selected for investment will be at the discretion of PVCC after a detailed study of the company, after the competition, the event and according to the terms of The management is governed by an appropriate committee.
