Senior Minister Sun Chanthol inspects roads affected by floods
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, on October 16, 2020, led the Ministry's technical working group to inspect the flood situation affecting road infrastructure. In particular, National Road 2, National Road 3, Street 22, Street 41 and National Road 4, with the participation of representatives of construction companies, local authorities and stakeholders.
The senior minister said that 249 sections of national roads with a total length of 324.29 km were flooded. These roads include: National Road 2, National Road 3, National Road 4, National Road 5 and many other major national roads.
Speaking to reporters during a mission to inspect roads damaged by floods, the senior minister advised construction companies constructing National Road 3 to use stones and sandbags to stop the water from seeping through the road. National Road 3 in Kampong Toul is located in Kandal Province to prevent water from crossing the road, causing flooding to the backs of thousands of people's houses below the road.
At the same time, the Senior Minister also informed that the relevant professional working group of the Ministry will make an estimate of the extent of all road damage in the Kingdom of Cambodia to request the budget to repair when the water recedes. Immediately.
On that occasion, the Senior Minister appealed to the owners of heavy vehicles not to drive on the roads that are flooded and follow the instructions of the authorities to prevent our road infrastructure. The damage was even more severe and the people apologized for some roadblocks temporarily preventing heavy vehicles from operating during this difficult time.
