BANGKOK, Oct. 16 (Xinhua) - A large number of Thai police and security forces launched an operation on the evening of October 16, 2020 to crack down on a large number of Thai protesters protesting for the resignation of Thai Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra. From position.
Authorities and security teams have used all means to disgraced the protesters as protesters continued to demand their will.
Thousands rallied in Bangkok to express their anger and opposition as the Thai government announced emergency measures in Bangkok to ban rallies. Five or more to try to end the protests that have been going on for three months.
Around the issue, Thai police officers stressed that they would have arrested all protesters but did not explain how the police forces will arrest tens of thousands. The Thai Royal Palace declined to comment on the protesters' demands.
As of Wednesday, the Thai government had allowed protests but did not show any signs of responding to the protesters' demands. The government changed its stance after an incident in which protesters mocked the convoy of the King's car accompanied by Queen Suthida after returning from a rare visit to Europe.
