New President of the Bar Association, Lawyer Ly Chantola, sets out eight policies to promote the excellence and prestige of lawyers
(Phnom Penh): Immediately after being elected President of the Bar Association for the 13th mandate, Mr. Ly Chantola set out eight policies to strengthen the excellence and prestige of the Cambodian legal profession.
The eight policies set out to enhance the excellence and prestige of the legal profession include:
First, tighten the application for the legal profession through experience and the examination for becoming a lawyer based on quality and ability.
Second, strengthen and enhance the capacity of lawyers by increasing training courses, seminars, quoting and exchanging experiences, study visits both inside and outside the country.
Third, strengthen cooperation, values and understanding with national and international institutions, especially with the police, justice, prisons and the judiciary.
Sixth: Establish a campaign to value and honor lawyers who have made outstanding contributions to the Bar Association, the legal profession, and social justice.
Seventh, continue to implement and strengthen the welfare mechanism of all lawyers, especially the mechanism related to the fund to help lawyers who are old and seriously ill.
And 8: Increase the interaction between the Bar Association and all lawyers and provide better services to all lawyers.
