Maintenance of National Road 78C from O'Chum roundabout to Vern Sai district, Ratanakkiri province is almost 90% complete
(Rattanakiri): The Governor of Rattanakiri Province, Mr. Thong Savun, on October 16, 2020, led professional officers and units around the province to inspect and repair 28.52 km of National Road 78 (C) connecting at the district roundabout. O Chum to Vern Sai district.
Mr. Say Saman, Director of the Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport, said that last year, due to heavy rains, National Road 78 (C), which is a red gravel road, was severely damaged, making it difficult to The commute of the general population.
The director of the department said that with the care of Mr. Thong Savun, the Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport has repaired and maintained this road with red stone, 28.52 km long and 9 meters wide to facilitate Traffic to people's trade has become easier again, using the Ministry's budget dropped to the department of about 2,570 million riels.
At present, about 86 percent of the repairs have been completed and are scheduled to be completed soon, he said.
Mr. Thong Savun said that in the past, the provincial authorities have always taken care to promote the repair of all damaged roads in districts, municipalities, communes, sangkats, villages, in some places built with concrete, rubber and Others are repaired with red gravel according to the budget we have to meet the needs of the people.
In the morning of the same day, the governor of Ratanakkiri province led the director of the relevant departments to inspect the Sesan River, but the situation is not worrying, that is, there is no flood like in some capitals and provinces.
