The Ministry of Water Resources announces the presence of a protracted low pressure system on Cambodia that continues to increase its impact, causing rain to continue from October 17-21.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology on the evening of October 16, 2020 announced the evolution of the weather situation, with a low pressure system is prolonging on Cambodia and increasing its influence gradually.
This situation will cause more rain to continue, especially from October 17 to 21, 2020 in the northwestern provinces, geographical areas near the Dangrek mountain range, northeastern plateau and the Cardamom mountain range. Heavy rains continued. In the coastal areas, there will be more rain and on the sea surface there will be mixed rain, wind and high waves.
According to the weather situation, the Ministry of Water Resources calls on relevant institutions, local authorities at all levels and the public, especially the people in the above areas, to be informed and pay more attention to avoid any danger. That could happen eventually. Spokesman for the General Commission: On October 16, another 499 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 169 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to October 16, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected And fined a total of 191,757 vehicles, including 141,707 motorcycles and 50,050 vehicles of all types.
