Phnom Penh: The Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, Mr. Horn Sokhemrin, on October 15, 2020, decided to temporarily detain four Taiwanese Chinese nationals who brought more than 3 tons of drugs from Laos through Cambodia to Taiwan. More than $ 30 million after a formal interrogation. This was confirmed by Mr. Kuch Kimlong, spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Court to Fresh News.
Mr. Kuch Kimlong confirmed that the four Taiwanese Chinese nationals were detained at M1 Prison. The four Taiwanese nationals were indicted by Deputy Prosecutor Sit Vannak of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on charges of "illegal possession, transportation and trafficking of drugs" under Articles 40 and 48 of the Law. Drug control.
It should be noted that on the afternoon of October 14, 2020, the Anti-Drug Department collected evidence to build a case file and sent 4 suspects to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for legal action related to 2106 kg of drugs. And 215.89 grams and 600 kilograms of chemical compounds worth more than 30 million US dollars.
The case was sent after an operation to crack down on cross-border trafficking and illegal drug processing from Laos through Cambodia to Taiwan, China, on October 7, 2020. Cracked down in 3 targets in Sihanoukville and 4 targets in Phnom Penh.
