Royal Government helps a Cambodian woman in Zhejiang Province to return to Cambodia because she could not live in harmony with her husband
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Consulate General in Shanghai, China, has cooperated with the Chinese authorities to intervene to help a Cambodian woman named Sem Srey Pich, who lives in Zhejiang Province, China, intending to return to Cambodia because she could not live in harmony with her husband. This is according to the announcement of Mr. Koy Kuong, spokesman for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation on October 15, 2020, which was received by Fresh News.
According to Koy Kuong, the Royal Government of Cambodia, through the same Consulate General, has issued a permit to her, and the Chinese police have also agreed to issue her visa on October 21, 2020.
Currently, Sem Srey Pich is staying at a friend's house, a Cambodian woman, near the Zhejiang Provincial Police Station in Wenzhou to wait for a visa. At the request of the Consulate General of the Cambodian Hand in Hand, Phnom Penh agreed to help her get a plane ticket.
Kratie Provincial Leaders Celebrate the Remembrance of His Majesty the King
(Kratie): Mr. Hoeur Siyem, Chairman of Kratie Provincial Council and Mr. Vathorn, Provincial Governor, this morning, October 15, 2020, held a ceremony to pay tribute to the late King Father Norodom Sihanouk, His Majesty the King Father. National Independence, which is the body of Samdech Ov, Samdech Ta, Samdech Ta Tuot of the Khmer people, who passed away on October 15, 2012 to October 15, 2020, is the 8th anniversary.
According to provincial administration officials, the celebration was held to show the deep love and priceless loyalty of his people.
In this ceremony, there were members of the Provincial Council and the Board of Governors, as well as the participation of government officials from all institutions in the province and the Armed Forces of all kinds, representing the people throughout Kratie.
Attendance to pay tribute to His Majesty King Bhumibol Adulyadej, who left behind Cambodia's success in reclaiming independence from French colonial rule in 1951 and reclaiming the Khmer temple of Preah Vihear from Siamese aggression in 1962 Unification, reconciliation and many other great achievements. Senior official of the Ministry of Agriculture: Cambodia will be able to export fresh mangoes directly to China for the first time by the end of this year (Video inside)
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ngin Chhay, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Agriculture, Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, confirmed that Cambodia will start exporting fresh mangoes directly to China for the first time by the end of the year. This 2020.
Mr. Ngin Chhay confirmed that Cambodia is currently in the process of building a disinfection facility (fly eggs) that destroys mangoes using steam or hot water, with 6-7 companies starting construction.
The senior official of the Ministry of Agriculture added that after the construction and infrastructure, we will import equipment and start disinfection operations in mangoes.
Mr. Ngin Chhay pointed out that at present, Cambodia does not have an official export permit, but overall, China has announced that China can import mangoes from Cambodia when the final conditions (disinfection facilities) are Completed.
The Director General of the General Department of Agriculture claimed that once the Chinese side has checked and found that Cambodia has sufficient capacity, Cambodia will be able to export mangoes to China.
Please be reminded that the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of China signed an official protocol on the export of fresh mangoes to China in June 2020.
By signing the Cambodian Mango Export Protocol to China, Cambodia can export 500,000 tons of high quality mangoes to the Chinese market every year.
(Phnom Penh): Today is the 26th anniversary of the establishment of the 70th Brigade. What is the history of the 70th Brigade? What has this brigade done, especially at a time when Cambodia is suffering from the floods, how has the 70th Brigade been involved in rescuing the people? Please read the following summary:
* Committed to achieving the five-year direction of 2019-2024 of the brigade by continuing humanitarian activities, construction of infrastructure, improving the livelihood of the army, strengthening the quality and capacity of the army through training of soldiers to take turns and modernize equipment to Ready to implement all regulations of the Royal Government, the Ministry of National Defense, the Commander-in-Chief and the Army Command.
In 2019 and 2020, this is the year that Cambodia suffered major disasters such as the collapse of buildings in Sihanoukville and Kampot, as well as floods like now. The 70th Brigade also contributed to the rescue of the people through the 711 Disaster Search and Rescue Task Force. Not only that, Cambodia has started to have 19 cases of Kovid, which is a case of infection from other countries.
The 70th Brigade participated in the campaign to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 by spraying pesticides on various government and civilian units, especially under the command of Lt. Gen. Mao Sophan. Send rescue soldiers to train in other units.
From its inception, the 70th Brigade has overcome all obstacles to achieve the highest orders of the Prime Minister, as well as the Ministry of National Defense, the Commander-in-Chief and the Army Command, with many achievements, including :
* Strengthened the spirit of responsibility in national defense, defended sovereignty, territorial integrity by participating in the battle on the front lines in the direction of the 3rd Army, the 4th Army and the 4th Army
* Controlled the number of troops, assigned the command and combat forces and cooperated with the General Commissioner of the National Police, Gendarmerie, relevant authorities to maintain security, safety, stability and order in Phnom Penh by cracking down on several attempts to defeat the Royal Government.
* Paying attention to solving the policy when there are soldiers who have died or become disabled, resolving the cremation money, visiting sick soldiers, supporting veterans and military families in the spirit of contributing to the implementation of national policy for veterans
* The brigade has fire trucks, ambulances to intervene and transport the victims of traffic accidents, pregnant women along National Road 3, 4 and west of Phnom Penh to public hospitals in Phnom Penh without For a fee, the 711th Emergency Squadron of the 70th Brigade also mobilized rescue interventions across the country, such as building collapses and trapping people from caves.
