The NEC stated that: "The incitement of the youth to hate their national institutions and their own nation to the bone is enough for the Khmer nation, which has gone through the bitterness of extinction, which in the history of human society has no nation." Any like that. "Khmer used to have a noble and noble civilization, built a civilization to the top that foreigners admire everywhere, not built by people who hate their own race to the bone."
The NEC calls on all stakeholders, especially young people, to adopt an honest attitude (mindfulness, wisdom, principles of self-motivation and self-sacrifice), and to renounce chastity (a troubled and confused mind) because Who has a good future and success in life. The NEC continued that only by respecting the law can the country continue to maintain peace, security, stability, security and public order.
According to the NEC, the process of reviewing the voter list and voter registration in 2020 went smoothly. The NEC congratulates and welcomes the cooperation of all stakeholders.
The NEC further affirms that it is an institution enshrined in the Constitution and elected by the National Assembly, a body that represents the will of the Cambodian people throughout the country. The NEC is the competent organization to organize and administer the election of the Senate and the election of the National Assembly, as well as other elections as determined by law.
The NEC has consistently adhered to these legal principles, and only the last two general elections, 2017 and 2018, were considered by all parties, both national and international, to be acceptable. Any party that participated in the election and did not recognize those elections. Are these things that Cambodians, who can do, should not be proud of?
An election can be conducted smoothly and successfully, depending on the participation of all stakeholders, including political parties as one of the 11 main stakeholders of the election.
In order to strengthen the cooperation and raise the awareness of political parties about the rights and obligations as stated in the law and other legal documents in force, the NEC would like to introduce and remind the following:
1: Law on the Election of the National Assembly
Article 7: Each political party which has the right to stand for election shall have the right to appoint two of its own representatives, one full member and one reserve person among the names on the voter list, called political party agents to observe the election at the polling station and Each polling station.
Article 14: Each authorized political party agent has the right to be present at the polling station or the polling station in accordance with the NEC regulations and procedures.
Article 15: The agent of a political party has the right to object or protest any violation of this law or the rules and procedures of the election which he or she has witnessed.
Article 16: Objections or protests must be made to the chairman of the polling station commission or the head of the polling station at the time of the violation or after the violation.
Article 18: In observing the election process and counting the ballots, the agents of political parties must not:
1: Provide guidance or reprimand to election officials and vote counting officers 2: Interfere with or interfere with the election process and vote counting process 3: Raise objections or protests to anyone other than the chairman of the polling station commission or chairman Polling stations can not count 4: Violate the provisions of this law or the rules and procedures of the NEC.
Article 142: A fine of 5,000,000 Riels to 20,000,000 Riels, without consideration of other criminal penalties, shall be imposed on any person who, by any means of dishonesty: causes aggression or obstructs normal activities in Place for examination of voter list and voter registration during the examination of voter list and voter registration.
2: Code of Conduct for Political Parties, Candidates and Agents of Political Parties
The main goal of the NEC is to serve the general population without discrimination, that is, all citizens must be on the voter list until they reach voting age. The names on the list must be accurate and voting, and when voting is not intimidating, especially, everyone's vote must be counted correctly according to the will of the people. These principles are the most consistent respect for the will of the Cambodian people of the NEC.
