According to the Ministry of Water Resources, after monitoring and improving the actual weather conditions, on October 15, 2020, an active low pressure is located in the central Philippines.
The active low pressure is expected to move into the South China Sea and gradually develop into the 17th typhoon SAUDEL, making landfall in southern Vietnam on the 17th. October 2020 and reduced the influence to low pressure and low pressure when entering Cambodia.
At the same time, the low pressure system has been extending over Cambodia and this will make the weather in Cambodia from 17 to 19 October 1920 the following situation:
* First, the lowland provinces, including Siem Reap, Banteay Meanchey, Battambang, Pursat, Kampong Thom, Kampong Chhnang, Kampong Speu, Kandal and Phnom Penh, will receive more rain.
