Minister of Health: During the floods, the provision of health services closer to people's homes!
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Health, Professor Mam Bunheng, said that this year's natural disasters caused by floods have caused flooding of roads and houses of many people in each area of each province, including Phnom Penh. Risks of health problems occur all the time if not very careful.
"Therefore, during the floods, our health officials have been mobilizing in safe areas where people have been evacuated, and we have prepared medicines and medical equipment, especially vaccines and vaccines," he said. "Snake bites or other venomous animals."
This statement was made by the Minister of Health on the occasion of leading a working group to help Sen Sok district to provide relief to flood victims in Khan Dangkor, Phnom Penh this morning, October 15, 2020, which took place at the school. Dangkor district.
All the work so far is due to the guidance of the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, to unite and alleviate the difficulties of vulnerable people. Currently, due to the floods that have affected the health and economy of the family, the team from Sen Sok district came down to help Dangkor district because this district has suffered the most from the floods.
In order to minimize the impact on the health, lives of victims and health facilities from natural disasters, Minister Mam Bun Heng continued to call on all people to participate in the implementation of protection measures during the floods, such as:
Do not enter an old house or a dilapidated building as it may break and cause danger. Do not touch electrical appliances with wet hands or standing in water while traveling by boat or ferry at night, keep the lights on.
* Sleep under a mosquito net at all times to prevent dengue fever, malaria and other diseases.
* For pregnant women, follow up and check the pregnancy as determined by the health center or hospital. If the woman is close to giving birth, find a place to stay near the health center or hospital nearest to you.
Get your child vaccinated as prescribed by your doctor and feed them properly.
* Help the elderly in your family and the elderly in the neighborhood and provide support to family members or children with disabilities such as crutches, wheelchairs or some of the medications they are taking on a regular basis that are essential to their needs.
Be careful to avoid drowning, prevent small children from drowning, explain to children the dangers of drowning, take children to higher ground and have a caregiver use a jacket or plastic bag every time the child leaves the house. When traveling by boat, do not overcrowd. If someone drowns, call for help immediately.
* Clean your body by taking a bath, washing your hair with soap and water and washing your clothes to avoid eczema, scabies and scabies.
Ministry of Labor issues measures for factories, enterprises and workers to implement in a situation where Cambodia is suffering from floods
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training on October 15, 2020 issued a number of measures for factories, enterprises and workers to implement while Phnom Penh and some provinces in Cambodia are suffering from floods. This is according to the announcement of the Ministry of Labor, which was received by Fresh News.
In its statement, the Ministry of Labor stated that in order to avoid occupational risks and prevent any possible accidents caused by floods, the Ministry would like to advise the owners and directors of factories, enterprises and workers in areas that may be affected by floods. Rain as follows:
1: For factory owners and directors
* Regularly monitor meteorological forecasts and prepare flood safety guidelines and evacuation methods.
* Must cooperate and follow the instructions of the competent authorities and temporarily suspend production in case of severe flood can not be safe
* Check the electrical system and turn off the power immediately in case of water flowing into the production building and factory premises.
* Pay close attention to the place where chemicals are stored and keep the chemicals well closed to avoid leaks affecting the health of workers and double.
2: For workers
* Must follow the instructions and management of the employer regarding safety measures
* Cooperate with employers to prevent the influx of rainwater into production buildings and industrial premises.
The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training strongly hopes that the owners and directors of factories, enterprises and workers in the flood-affected areas will follow the guidelines.
