(Bangkok), police crack down to the Thai riot, has decided to use the force of protesters, from the outside of the premises, after the Bangkok's government, declared an emergency, including news dissemination Which causes fear. This is according to the release by CNA on the morning of Thursday, October 15, 2020.
Protests in Thailand have dragged on for more than three months, with thousands of protesters marching in Bangkok to demand the resignation of Prime Minister Prayuth Chan-o-cha and amendments to the current constitution. Some protesters even dared to demand the reform of the monarchy, which they considered to have given too much power to the king.
The decision to use force to disperse the protesters came shortly after a government emergency order came into force at 4:00 a.m. Thursday, with some protesters pushing and shoving with the army. Police force. Eventually, however, they were evicted from the area outside the prime minister's office as hundreds of police were patrolling the streets and cleaning workers began clearing the area.
According to the protesters, at least three leaders have been arrested, but the Thai government has not yet commented. The declaration of emergency aims to ban gatherings of five or more people, and any information that could cause fear or damage to national security is also banned.
