(Kampong Speu): Speaking at the Closing Ceremony of the Second Generation Military Training Course to Complete the Framework of the Military Academy under the Military Zone 2020, at the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces Techo Sen Phnom Thom, Preah Preav, Kampong Speu Province, on October 14, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Commander-in-Chief The Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) said that becoming a military officer was another step in a military career and an important task to fulfill.
On that occasion, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet congratulated on the successful completion of the second generation military training course for the 2020 Military Academy, which can be considered as the first model course for the Army due to its methodology and The selection process for the selection of participants is very detailed.
He said that this is a success that comes from the participation of all stakeholders, including the leadership of the Army, the Capacity Building Committee of the Army, the management of the military and all working groups, and those who benefit from this success is the Army. The mainland as well as the entire Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, especially the trainees.
The lieutenant general continued that this training course really responded to both the quantity and quality to the needs of training officers to become teachers in each profession, which is a resource that is lacking to meet the framework for military academies. Under the regional army, in accordance with the priority work plan of the army set out to solve the challenges ahead.
Trainees who complete the course will become military officers or perform professional duties in schools and units under the Army, which will in the future have the opportunity to continue training hundreds of thousands of other soldiers. What is important is that this training course gives trainees the ability to plan training, lead training, conduct leadership, practice, do lessons, know how to advance and have a clear pedagogy to teach both in the classroom and on the field.
"Becoming a military officer is another step in the military career and an important task to be fulfilled because it is to help the army and the motherland through hard work in the military," he said. Student resource training. "On the other hand, it is rewarding for oneself to take this opportunity to increase one's self-efficacy, create achievements, demonstrate one's abilities and promote one's potential as a basis for progress."
Mr. Hun Manet praised the military that as a leader, a father, a mentor, an adviser, has really played an important role in sharing knowledge and experience to the trainees, but the success and quality of training is Depending on the will and attention of the participants.
Investing four months in this course is to increase and refresh the capacity, because these skills and basic knowledge on military skills are already available to military trainees in this course. In the military academy in the past.
