Acting Head of State: Through the new diplomatic mission of Russia will help encourage more Russian investors to invest in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, Acting Head of State of Cambodia, expressed his hope that through the diplomatic mission of Anatoly BOROVIK, the newly appointed Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of the Russian Federation to Cambodia will help to expand relations and activities. Trade between the two countries to grow and encourage Russian investors to explore more investment opportunities in Cambodia.
Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey congratulated the Russian Federation on the achievement of the Kovid-19 vaccine, which is the hope of the people of the Russian Federation as well as the nations of the world.
The Russian Ambassador stated that through his diplomatic mission in Cambodia, he will make every effort to further strengthen the friendly relations and cooperation between the two countries to contribute to the promotion of Development of Cambodia.
He emphasized that this year marks the 25th anniversary of the Cooperation Agreement between the Russian Federation and the Kingdom of Cambodia, and next year the 65th anniversary of diplomatic relations between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Russian Federation.
Anatoly BOROVIK informed the Acting Head of State about the discovery of the Kovid-19 vaccine, which is not only a cure for the Russian people, but also a cure for humanity all over the world. Despite the outbreak of Kovid-19, he praised the development of relations and cooperation between the two countries, especially the relationship between the two countries' legislatures.
He informed the Acting Head of State that when Kovid-19 is over, the President of the Federal Council of the Federal Parliament of the Russian Federation will be able to visit the Kingdom of Cambodia at any convenient time.
The Ambassador recalled the Memorandum of Understanding between the Senate of Cambodia and the Federal Council of the Federal Parliament of the Russian Federation, which will be completed in March 2021. At the same time, he respectfully requested Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey to continue to implement this Memorandum of Understanding for the future.
In addition, the new Russian Ambassador hopes that in the near future, there will be an exchange of visits between the Chairperson of the Commission on International Affairs and the General Department of Protocol and International Relations of the two countries' upper houses, as well as training of officials of the General Secretariat of the Senate. Cambodia in the field of parliamentary diplomacy as well.
The Acting Head of State reminded that the relations between Cambodia and Russia (formerly the Soviet Union) established diplomatic relations on May 15, 1956. Until now, this diplomatic relationship has lasted 64 years, and next year will mark the 65th anniversary of diplomatic relations between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Russian Federation.
Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey stated that the Senate, National Assembly, Royal Government, Ministries and National Institutions of the Kingdom of Cambodia are always ready to work closely with the Ambassador and Embassy of the Russian Federation to contribute to the promotion of good relations and cooperation between the two countries. And both peoples.
Through the Ambassador, Samdech brought a courtesy call from His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, and Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk and other leaders of the Kingdom. Cambodia also provides top leaders at all levels of the Russian Federation.
However, the US government has not yet acknowledged any plans to sell arms to Taiwan, while China has warned it will take action if such a thing happens.
