The Kathina Ceremony has been practiced since more than 2,500 years ago, during the time when the Buddha, the Supreme Master Ching Hai, lived and granted alms to allow Buddhists to celebrate this ceremony to bring the three main elements of alms: Sbong Chivor and Sangkhadey to Ver. Give the monks who have been waiting for the rainy season for the whole quarter in Buddhism in various temples.
Buddhists from all walks of life throughout Cambodia, approving with pure generosity, began to celebrate the Kathina ceremony according to the Buddhist tradition with joy and pride for the full freedom of religion and belief, as well as in daily life in the Techo era. Full of peace, stability and rapid development in all fields.
