Cambodia is developing a roadmap to restore and promote tourism 2020-2025
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism has initiated a draft roadmap on a plan to rehabilitate and promote tourism during the Kovid-19 crisis and the five-year post-crisis period of 2020-2025.
This morning, October 14, 2020, the Ministry of Tourism met with the private sector in the tourism sector under the chairmanship of Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, before submitting to the National Commission for Tourism Development. Under the chairmanship of Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, Minister of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the National Commission for Tourism Development, and will continue to submit to the Royal Government in the near future.
Minister Thong Khon said that the road map has three stages:
The Minister of Tourism also requested the meeting with the participation of the public and private sectors to participate in some work, including:
First, to continue to promote economic and employment support measures, especially to promote the provision of budgets or funds of the Royal Government to help small and medium enterprises (SMEs) in the tourism sector and young entrepreneurs in the tourism sector with innovative ideas. Expanding human resource training in tourism and maximizing employment.
Second, continue to implement tourism safety measures in the first step and set out the next steps with high efficiency.
Third: Promote more Cambodian tourism to increase trust and credibility through various digital nursery promotions according to each priority market (besides current promotion), especially quality and professional promotion according to priority goals. And strengthen the role of tourism information centers and tourism departments in the capital-province to promote more.
Fourth, promote the movement of domestic and domestic tourism by creating new attractive and affordable tour packages.
Fifth, diversification of new tourism products in priority areas, including Phnom Penh and the surrounding areas of Siem Reap and the surrounding areas, the coastal area and the surrounding area, the Northeast and the surrounding area, in accordance with the concept of "clean and green".
Seventh, to establish a mechanism for leading and implementing with full authority and decision-making authority to effectively implement the strategic activities of the roadmap.
The Meeting agreed that the development of this roadmap will be an important mechanism necessary to respond to the current situation as well as the future, which is an important part of Cambodia's vision to be achieved, while the private sector also expressed support. Mostly with the action plan that the Ministry of Tourism has already mentioned in the draft roadmap.
According to Mr. Nep Samuth, the road map is scheduled to be submitted to the National Tourism Development Commission in November 2020 for review before being submitted to the Royal Government.
Senior Minister Kun Kim stated: "To date, we have been affected by the floods that affected about 19 provinces across the country, but out of 19 provinces, 4 or 5 provinces have been severely affected. Intervention is needed. Of the 19 provinces, nearly 40,000 families have been affected and more than 110,000 have been affected.
According to Senior Minister Kun Kim, "Over the past few days, the Joint Working Group has helped evacuate about 3,000 families with a population of more than 10,000." In addition, the floods affected about 40,000 houses in 19 capitals and provinces, more than 300 schools were flooded and 116,000 hectares of rice fields were planted. Ten thousand hectares as well.
More than 190 kilometers of national and provincial roads were also affected by the floods. This is the total result obtained from the 19 provincial secretariats.
According to Senior Minister Kun Kim, the four worst-affected provinces are Pursat, Battambang, Banteay Meanchey and Pailin, and most recently the floods have shifted to Phnom Penh and Kampong Speu.
It should be noted that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, this morning, October 14, 2020, released a charitable fund by providing $ 100,000 per capital-province affected by severe floods per capital-province. Through the National Committee for Disaster Management to address the issues at hand.
According to Senior Minister Kun Kim, the six capitals and provinces that will receive funding to solve the current problems are Battambang, Pursat, Pailin, Banteay Meanchey, Kampong Speu and Phnom Penh.
With the appeal, Samdech Techo Prime Minister also thanked the philanthropists who have contributed to help people who are suffering from floods through the Royal Government of Cambodia. Kampong Cham Provincial Governor Inspects and Accelerates Reconstruction of Drainage from Kampong Cham City
(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, on October 14, 2020, led the relevant officials of the relevant departments to inspect the progress of the construction of the drainage system from Kampong Cham City, which collapsed in the past at the park. Tonle Village 3, Sangkat Veal Vong, Kampong Cham City.
According to the administration of Kampong Cham Provincial Hall, due to the flood, the water level of the Mekong River has risen to 10.62 meters, which is 0.34 meters as of the morning of October 14, 2020. At the same time, the provincial governor led officials from the relevant departments to inspect in order to speed up the construction of the temporary drainage system from Kampong Cham City, which collapsed in the past at the riverside park.
However, according to technical officials, the construction of the drainage system from Kampong Cham has now achieved more than 20 percent. By pouring concrete around the waist of the new drainage system and pouring concrete on top of another floor with a length of 80 meters from the mouth of the old drainage well to the river and use a three-way drainage system, each of which is 0.8 meters in diameter And build two more floating drainage wells to prevent water blockage.
It should also be reminded that at midnight on September 13, 2020, the drainage point of the riverside park collapsed, and the case was concluded by experts to be caused by the drainage system. It is old and dilapidated, that is, this drainage system has been built since the French colonial era, and on the night of the incident, there was heavy rain.
