Lt. Gen. Seak Socheat sends condolences and considers Keo Maly's death as a great loss of resources for social development
(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. Seak Socheat, Deputy Chief of Joint Staff, Director of the Border Affairs Office (OCC) of the General Command, on October 14, 2020, sent a sad message of condolence over the death of Ms. Keo Maly, Advisor to the King. Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate of Cambodia, who passed away at 1:07 AM on October 14, 2020 in Bangkok, Thailand.
In this sad message of condolence, Lt. Gen. Seak Socheat said that Ms. Keo Maly is an dignitary who has contributed to the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the local people, especially the people in Kampong Thom province under the leadership of Dr. Nguon Nhel, the head of the Royal Government's working group, came to help this province.
Lt. Gen. Seak Socheat, please pray for the sacred objects in the world and the merits of the Buddha, the Dharma, the monks, to take care of the soul of Mrs. Keo Maly, who went to be happy in death forever.
According to the news of Keo Maly's death, she died of a disease at the age of 65. Her body will be transported from Bangkok, Thailand to Cambodia on the night of October 14, 2020.
