Kampong Thom MPs advise people to be careful during the flood season
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Kheng Nupheap, Member of Parliament for Kampong Thom constituency, advised the people to be very careful during the flood season.
Mr. Kheng Noupheap said this on the occasion of visiting the people to support the construction of the school in the area of Mr. Tanong in Veal Veng village and check the water level at the base of Ta Ok bridge, Chhouk commune, Prasat Sambo district on October 13. 2020.
"Be very careful, because in the coming days, the effects of the storm will continue to hit Cambodia, we may have more floods, especially to take good care of children, the elderly and the vulnerable," he said. "To avoid drowning, as well as protection from venomous bites or stings, if there is a flood, run to safety."
Mr. Kheng Nupheap also advised all participants to be very careful by participating in the implementation of measures to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 by properly following the educational messages of the Ministry of Health to jointly fight this deadly disease. Wash your hands often and regularly with soap, care for your health, hygiene and personal safety, and eat well-cooked food.
He added that the village-commune safety policy, authorities and local authorities must be widely disseminated so that people have a clear knowledge to avoid domestic violence and other abuses that the government is taking care of. Take care and try to explain to people to understand climate change.
During the visit, Mr. Kheng Noupheap also contributed some funds for the construction of Chhetan School and Veal Veng Primary School.
