(Phnom Penh): People with disabilities also need prosperity, a better life and all opportunities and rights and freedoms like people without disabilities. In recent years, society has undergone many positive changes, from promoting the rights of people with disabilities, providing equal opportunities and providing quality services to ensure a better quality of life for people with disabilities.
This was stated by Mr. Em Chanmakara, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation and Secretary General of the General Secretariat of the Disability Action Council in the opening ceremony of the National Strategic Plan on Disability 2019-2023 and infrastructure technical standards Physical comfort for people with disabilities on October 14, 2020 at the Ministry of Interior.
Mr. Em Chanmakara added that building a society that cares and values people with disabilities is not difficult if we believe that people with disabilities are capable people. There is a lot of evidence and experience that people with disabilities do many remarkable things that people without disabilities or physical disabilities cannot do.
In the past, some people with disabilities have had difficulty obtaining ID cards, birth certificates, marriage certificates, residency books, property titles, or due to the use of discriminatory language by some of our authorities.
In addition, Mr. Yun Chhunny, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior, said that the Royal Government of Cambodia has been investing in the field of disability for many years. Currently, the Royal Government is on the right path to restore and develop the motherland, especially peace, political stability and economic growth.
He said that the growth of the disability sector and the economic development of Cambodia is considered to be an encouraging political goal, which is an active push from the Cambodian government to investment companies, including providing priority opportunities for recruitment. Have a disability to work as well.
Mr. Em Chanmakara added that the Ministry of Interior has an important role to play in promoting the participation of persons with disabilities in public life, political life, the provision of justice and liberty, and the promotion of the protection, freedom and personal security of persons with disabilities in The goal is to empower people with disabilities by participating in all decision-making and political activities in society.
