(Kratie): Sambo District Police arrested a suspect in connection with the case of raping his own daughter and sent him to the Anti-Trafficking and Juvenile Office of the Kratie Provincial Police after receiving a complaint from the victim's mother.
According to the Sambo District Police report, on October 13, 2020, the Koh Khner Commune Administrative Police Station received a complaint from Chhun Toeun, 54, of Svay Chek Village, Koh Khner Commune, Sambo District, Kratie Province. Nai Chantha, 57, reportedly raped his 20-year-old daughter.
Immediately after receiving the complaint, our police force questioned the victim and took him to Sambo Health Center and arrested the suspect.
Mr. Noy Sithach, Deputy Inspector in charge of Criminal Affairs, further confirmed that after questioning the victim, he clarified that on July 2015, at 3:00 PM, while she was sitting alone at home, her father suddenly He came up, covered his mouth and threatened to kill me if I shouted.
At that time, Nai Chantha took off her clothes and raped the victim once, and she decided to stop studying until July 2019, when the victim left home to study hairdressing in Phnom Penh.
Later, she returned home on August 1, 2020, until October 8, 2020 at 2:00 pm, while the victim was charging the phone in the room, suddenly named Nai Chantha entered the room and arrested He shut his mouth and threatened to kill me if I shouted. He then took off his clothes and raped the victim again.
