This situation has caused physical damage, financial loss, affecting the economy, society and livelihood of the people, especially causing eventual damage to crops, livestock and aquaculture. Therefore, in order to help solve all the challenges that people have been facing and to improve their safety and disaster resilience, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries would like to make the following recommendations:
Second, the General Department of Agriculture must monitor and evaluate the impact of crop damage and prepare to release rice seeds and other crops from the stockpile of the Cambodian Food Reserve for interventions to restore the damage according to the actual situation.
Fourth, the Capital-Provincial Departments of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries must regularly monitor the flood situation, prepare for emergencies, assess the impact and damage gradually to obtain accurate figures by grasping the location and geographical conditions that can be Restore damage.
Fifth, all technical units under the Ministry must increase the campaign to promote short-term crop cultivation, animal husbandry and aquaculture work in the affected provinces in order to improve the living standards of the people. .
Sixth, the directors of programs and development projects must cooperate and accelerate the implementation of programs or projects to rehabilitate the impact in their target provinces.
And 7: To report the impact and challenges to the Ministry in a timely manner.
