(Pursat): Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management and Chief of Staff of Samdech Techo Hun Sen in the Battle of Disaster, highly appreciated the philanthropists who have joined the Royal Government in dealing with the floods.
The Senior Minister considered this assistance as a noble gesture to help the victims as well as help solve the difficulties of the Royal Government.
Senior Minister Kun Kim made the remarks while receiving assistance from Caritas on October 13, 2020.
Caritas is an organization that always helps the Royal Government of Cambodia in times of disaster. To deal with the floods that are hitting the northwestern province, the organization has provided 20 high-speed ferries, 500 tents, 500 nets and 500 blankets.
The Senior Minister praised Caritas Cambodia for always being a good partner with the National Committee for Disaster Management every time there is a disaster.
Notably, in addition to Caritas, many philanthropists have donated their food and funds to help flood victims.
Senior Minister Kun Kim said that the contribution of philanthropists is to alleviate the difficulties of the Royal Government and the people. This help also shows the gesture of support for the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
"The contribution of philanthropists is a noble gesture," he said. When our nation is in trouble, we must overcome these difficulties together. So it's a good idea to get involved from all walks of life. This gesture also shows support for the right leadership of Samdech Techo.
Along with high appreciation and appreciation, Senior Minister Kun Kim also thanked the benefactors who helped the people and the Royal Government.
The senior minister also continued to call on philanthropists to share to solve the difficulties of the people in the floods.
