During a courtesy call on Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong on the morning of October 13, 2020, Anatoly Borovic said he would report to Moscow on Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong's request for Russian assistance. Promote a free trade agreement (FTA) between Cambodia and the Russian Federation so that Cambodia can export agricultural products and other products to Russia duty free.
The Russian Ambassador said that he was very happy to have the Deputy Prime Minister as a close friend who strengthened and expanded the bilateral relations, relations and cooperation between Cambodia and Russia while Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong Acting as Cambodian Ambassador to Moscow.
As the Ambassador of the Russian Federation to Cambodia, he is a historical witness who sees the current development of Cambodia remarkably.
At the same time, he highly appreciated the role of the Deputy Prime Minister, who previously chaired the Intergovernmental Commission for Cambodia-Russia Trade, Economic, Scientific and Technical Cooperation (IGC) and was the founder of this commission. He pledged to further boost Cambodia-Russia trade and investment, albeit at a low level.
In fact, 2021 is the 65th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between Cambodia and the Russian Federation, Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong believes that this anniversary should be well organized in line with friendly relations and close cooperation between our two countries. Two.
In addition, the Deputy Prime Minister said that today, Cambodia and Russia have an intergovernmental commission for trade, economic, scientific and technical cooperation between Cambodia and Russia (IGC), so should cooperate between our two countries. To be even bigger, including trade and investment.
In this regard, the Deputy Prime Minister suggested that the Commission meet online to promote trade and investment, while Kovid-19 could not have a face-to-face meeting. In addition, the Deputy Prime Minister also informed the Ambassador that currently Cambodia is not open to foreign tourists, but Cambodia allows foreign businessmen to come to Cambodia to promote economic cooperation, trade and investment.
On the other hand, the Russian Federation in 2020 will chair the Shanghai Cooperation Organization (SCO), which has seven member countries in Asia and the Russian Federation. The Deputy Prime Minister requested the Government of the Russian Federation to help make Cambodia an observer country and a future member.
As for Cambodia's debt owed by Russia after Cambodia was liberated from the Khmer Rouge genocidal regime, Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong said that there have been long and frequent discussions between the Cambodian Ministry of Economy and Finance and relevant institutions. Russia, but not yet achieved.
The Deputy Prime Minister stated that the fact that this debt is to help the hunger of the Cambodian people after the fall of the Khmer Rouge regime and the reconstruction of Cambodia, unlike the debt of another country that led the war to Cambodia until the Khmer Rouge regime. The Deputy Prime Minister also called for a settlement based on the long-standing friendship and mutual understanding between our two governments and peoples.
Finally, the Russian Ambassador would like to commend Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, for direct and effective control and prevention of Kovid-19 in Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's message stated that "I am always very proud of the noble virtues of our compatriots, who always show kindness and solidarity to help each other in times of emergency.
