(Siem Reap): Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, on October 13, 2020, led a delegation of the Ministry of Education, National Scouts of Cambodia to ride a bicycle to celebrate World Peace Day 2020 in Siem Reap.
Leading a delegation of the Ministry of Education of the Cambodian National Scouts to ride a bicycle to celebrate the World Peace Day 2020 in the program to promote peace messengers under the theme "Building peace together" with the participation of 150 leaders of the Cambodian National Scouts.
The purpose of this ceremony was to inspire and inspire the people in the community to better understand the value and importance of peace that the leaders of the Royal Government, especially Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia and the teachers of the Cambodian National Scouts. Life is the capital to bring peace to the people of Cambodia.
Minister Hang Chuon Naron, President of the Cambodian National Scouts, stated that peace only guarantees the stability and progress of democracy and freedom, and that the success of the development process and the strength of democracy and, in turn, ensures the stability of peace.
"If we lose peace, we will lose everything," he said. The road ahead will face many more obstacles, but no obstacles can hinder our nation's journey, as long as we maintain national unity and solidarity, we are determined to protect the peace we have achieved so hard and remain strong. Always dynasty.
The Cambodian National Scout Movement was re-established on April 27, 2006 and became a full member of the World Scout Movement on July 1, 2008. Currently, the Cambodian National Scout Movement is widely recognized both nationally and internationally. The Cambodian National Scout Movement is structured from national to grassroots and has grown to include more than 150,000 children and youth from all walks of life across the country.
This significant increase in membership is reflected in outreach programs and the expansion of youth scout membership, community outreach and community outreach, leadership development, and scout training for all Scout leaders. Special Class, Unified Chief, who is the Rector, Director-Director of public and private educational institutions throughout the country.
