The back of Stung Prek Tnaot delta dam is still facing flooding in Stung Prek Tnaot in the western part of Phnom Penh and Kandal province, the Minister of Water Resources continues to intervene to prevent
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of October 13, 2020, Mr. Lim Kean Hor, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, together with the Ministry's technical working group, inspected and ordered the intervention work along the back of the Stung Prek Tnaot Delta Dam. Currently facing the flooding of Stung Prek Tnaot in the western part of Phnom Penh and Kandal province.
Please note that the water level at the dam on January 7 this morning, the water level was 8.80 meters, compared to yesterday, an increase of 0.45 meters, an increase of 7 meters above the alert level, making the water level in the river close. Equivalent to the back of a dam in some lowlands.
The Ministry of Water Resources has confirmed that "the technical team of the Ministry has been working to repair the dragon tunnel that appeared continuously using earth-moving machinery to lift and compress the dam, as well as sandbags to raise the back of the dam."
In addition, with the participation of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, the Minister donated 3,000 sacks to Ms. Kim Nhim, Governor of Dangkor District, to continue to the three Sangkats to prevent the flow of water on the dam to the bottom causing flooding. Citizens.
In the near future, the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology will start implementing the irrigation and flood protection projects of Stung Prek Tnaot, Phnom Penh, Kandal and Takeo provinces with financial assistance from the People's Republic of China.
