(Banteay Meanchey): About 205 families in Say Samorn village, Chamnom commune, Mongkul Borei district, Banteay Meanchey province were completely flooded.
The village is about 10 kilometers from the provincial town, and the floods make it impossible for villagers to travel anywhere. Currently, people are being evacuated to a pagoda.
The suffering of the people is also the suffering of the authorities and the national leadership. Therefore, Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice President of the National Committee for Disaster Management under the direct command of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Commander-in-Chief on the Battlefield. The disaster traveled directly to the flood-hit area on October 13, 2020.
The visit to the flooded area was also accompanied by Mr. Ou Rathrey, Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police Commissioner, Brigadier General Sith Loh and Commander of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Gendarmerie, Brigadier General Born Bin and other relevant officials. .
Due to difficult road conditions and flooding, it took nearly two hours to reach the flooded area by tractor and ferry.
As soon as Senior Minister Kun Kim and the provincial leaders arrived, the people there applauded the presence of the Senior Minister and the provincial leaders. Senior Minister Kun Kim met with village chiefs, commune chiefs and residents about their impact.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Kun Kim brought greetings and greetings from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross. The Senior Minister also informed the people about the issuance of Samdech Techo's order to the authorities at both the national and provincial levels to help the people from the flood.
The Senior Minister emphasized, "Both Samdechs are constantly monitoring the situation of the floods." Both princes ordered us to come down and meet with you to solve your problems. Samdech Lok has ordered to help you not to leave you.
In front of the flood victims, Senior Minister Kun Kim praised the provincial governor, U Rathrey, and the provincial forces for helping the flood victims. In Banteay Meanchey province, floods in eight districts and 33 communes affected nearly 3,000 families, killing five people and affecting nearly 6,000 hectares of seedlings and crops, he said.
The provincial governor said that the worst flooding areas were in Serei Sophorn and Mongkul Borei districts. The provincial governor said more than 300 families had been evacuated.
According to the provincial governor, the affected people have been provided with food and temporary supplies by the province, and armed forces and officials have been deployed to rescue people from the floods.
The provincial governor also expressed concern about the rising flooding in areas bordering Thailand as Thai Sa Kaeo provincial authorities announced the opening of a dam in the province. The opening of the dam will lead to flooding in the border area.
It should be noted that in order to share the hardships of Banteay Meanchey province, Mr. Oknha Leng Pros, President of Leng Navatra Company, Brother Oknha Leng Navatra donated $ 1,500 to the province to buy food for the victims after donating $ 5,000 yesterday. To help the victims in Pursat and Battambang provinces, as well as the forces.
