The Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement (CCFTA) was officially signed on October 12, 2020 via video by Cambodian Minister of Commerce Pan Sosak and Minister of Foreign Affairs Zhong Shan. Chinese Trade under the Testimony of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Wang Yi, State Councilor and Minister of Foreign Affairs of the People's Republic of China at the Peace Palace.
The Ministry of Commerce states that the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement will provide many benefits to Cambodia, such as:
Larger and better market access for all kinds of fish, meat, agricultural products, vegetables, fruits, processed and handicraft products and more while Cambodia can produce and comply with sanitary and phytosanitary rules. No hygiene.
* Access to the market for trade in services that Cambodia can export in the case of adequate training, skills and qualifications, especially when Cambodia can strengthen itself in the service sector in the future. In addition, Cambodia will benefit from tax collection, employment, training, knowledge, skills from service providers and foreign service providers, which are important factors to strengthen the domestic production sector.
Clarify the procedures related to the rules of origin, customs procedures and trade facilitation, sanitation and phytosanitary and trade facilitation.
Organizing and creating an investment and political environment to attract foreign investment.
The trade agreement will enter into force 30 days after the date on which the two sides exchanged notices of termination of their internal procedures, including the approval of the two parliaments and The signature shall be ratified by the King or may enter into force on a different date as agreed by both parties. Military forces in Banteay Meanchey province are busy rescuing people from the floods
