Preah Chao Athikar Wat Preah Indra Tep handed over 41 pieces of statues to the Apsara Authority to keep, some statues built since the Bayon period
(Siem Reap): 41 pieces of statues and stone carvings were handed over to the APSARA Authority by the Chief Bishop of Wat Preah Ind Tep, while some of the statues were built in the Bayon style during the reign of King Jayavarman VII. Come on.
Regarding the preservation of this artifact, according to Chief Inspector Sem Sammean, the priest stated that originally, these 41 pieces of sculptures were scattered in the compound of Wat Preah Ind Tep and some at the back of Khoeun Preah Ang Tep. Therefore, in order to be safe, he also collected and stored in the southern part of the pagoda to prevent loss and damage by various means.
After receiving the information from the Angkor Heritage Protection Team, the inventory team of the Department of Temple Preservation in Angkor Park and Preventive Archeology and APSARA Authority went to receive the above statues and kept them at the office of the Department of APSARA Authority for work. Take a photo and describe it as a document for future repairs.
