Rainfall in Stung Treng province's Thala Parivat district has gradually receded
(Stung Treng): The flood that flooded last weekend in Thala Parivat district, Stung Treng province, which affected 5 communes and 13 villages, gradually receded on the evening of October 12, 2020.
The floods caused the flooding of 851 houses and evacuated 55 families to safety. A total of 923 families and 3,377 people were affected by the floods.
The floods affected a total of 327 hectares of people's rice fields and damaged a total of 171 hectares, while other mixed crops accounted for a total of 30 hectares and damaged a total of 22 hectares, as well as flooding schools, roads and sewers. The pagoda, too.
On the morning of October 12, 2020, Mr. Mom Saroeun, Governor of Stung Treng Province and provincial leaders continued to inspect the flood situation in Doung and Kes villages, Kaing Cham commune, Thala Borivat district, which is flooded.
In addition, Mr. Mom Saroeun also instructed the local authorities to take care of the people affected by the floods and be ready with emergency equipment or materials in case of increased flood to help. Save the local people in time.
It should be noted that as of the evening of the same day, the flood in Thala Parivat district has gradually decreased in four communes, but for Kaing Cham commune, the water is still flooded.
