In the first 9 months of this year, the General Department of Taxation collected 2225 million USD in tax revenue, an increase of nearly 4%
Mr. Kong Vibol, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the General Department of Taxation, emphasized that the effects of the Kovid 19 epidemic had shown negative signs and effects on tax revenue, especially tax categories and key sectors in the first quarter. 3 This.
He also instructed all units to continue to work hard to strengthen the effective implementation of laws and regulations and to be gentle but firm. To ensure the effective management of tax revenue collection and to achieve the plan set by the General. The Department of Taxation will continue to strictly and effectively implement the Royal Government's in-depth reform policy and set out the following measures:
* Continue to strengthen cooperation with relevant ministries and institutions, especially the General Department of Customs and Excise in order to strengthen the effective exchange of information to collect taxes in all aspects.
* Continue to disseminate to taxpayers and train tax officials at all levels on the tax on capital gains, which will start collecting from January 2021 onwards.
* Continue to strengthen the provision of property tax payment services that have been postponed to pay tax for 2020 until October 31, 2020 and promote taxpayers to hurry to pay property tax in 2020 to avoid waiting too long. After the deadline to pay, leading to a long wait.
* Continue to strengthen the provision of services, new registration / updating of real estate, payment of stamp duty on real estate transfer in Phnom Penh and in the provinces in collaboration with property owners and relevant institutions to ensure efficiency. Maximum.
* Continue to strengthen and provide comprehensive training in the field of online filing management system (E-Filing) by continuing to work with the private sector to address challenges as well as strengthen the capacity of all relevant tax officials in order to ensure Maximum efficiency in implementing the use of online submission management system (E-Filing).
* Promote and accelerate the implementation of business registration in the same nursery, which is a new innovation of the Royal Government to increase efficiency, facilitate and accelerate business registration in the Kingdom of Cambodia using information technology.
* Continue to review and pay more attention to the request for temporary suspension of business activities to prevent tax evasion of some corrupt enterprises.
* Accelerate the procedure for resolving taxpayers' complaints in order to improve the efficiency of providing services to taxpayers.
Strengthen and mainstream the culture of paying taxes and disseminate fiscal obligations to taxpayers and enterprises through seminars or other training sessions for taxpayers and relevant tax officials.
* Continue to pay attention to and implement the new regulations of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, such as Instruction No. 15301, dated 22 June 2020 on the implementation of VAT on the sale of long-term financial assets and Instruction No. 11581 AMD dated 05 May 2020 on the implementation of VAT on the issuance of business assets.
