General knowledge: Why did Gaddafi choose his own bodyguards, all women?
(Libya): Most leaders in the world always choose male bodyguards, except for former Libyan dictator Gaddafi, who chooses his own bodyguards, all women. What are the reasons behind this?
Speaking to reporters, Salam confirmed that she had joined Gaddafi's bodyguards in 1984 and had been captured by rebel forces in opposition to Gaddafi in 2011 during fighting in the northwestern part of the city. Tripoli, the capital of Libya.
"Gaddafi usually has three personal bodyguards everywhere, but if Gaddafi goes abroad, there will always be four more female bodyguards," she said. "The woman who was chosen to be Gaddafi's bodyguard is very happy," Salam said.
Answer with the question, "What are the special features of Gaddafi's bodyguards?" Ms. Salam stated that all bodyguards were recruited from a well-trained army and that they had to stand tall because they had to stand behind Gaddafi.
Mohammad al-Gaddafi has ruled Libya since 1969 through a coup. He occupied the Middle East for more than four decades before being assassinated by the opposition in 2011, backed by the United States.
Although Gaddafi's position in Libya has improved, he is considered by the world to be one of the most authoritarian dictators in modern times.
