(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance has opened a training course on "State Asset Management Procedures and Non-Tax Revenue Management" to target trainees who are Deputy Governors of Capital-Provinces, level officials in charge of management. State property and non-tax revenue of the capital-provincial administration and the director / deputy director of the Department of Economy and Finance throughout the country, a total of more than 100 people.
The purpose of this training is to strengthen the capacity and increase the awareness of civil servants to contribute to the promotion of transparency, accountability, efficiency and effectiveness of the management of state assets and non-tax revenue in accordance with technical principles and compliance. According to the Law on the Public Financial System and within the framework of the Royal Government's Public Financial Management Reform Program.
Dr. Hean Sahip, Secretary of State and Chairman of the Capacity Building Working Group of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, emphasized that the reform of public financial management was officially announced by the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen in 2004 with the goal of Transform the Cambodian budget system from an input-based and centralized budget to a performance-based and decentralized budget.
