Chicken owner lays wire to prevent thieves from electrocuting a young man near a chicken coop in Ba Phnom district, Prey Veng province
(Prey Veng): There was a surprise when a young man was electrocuted near a chicken coop of a family in Ba Phnom district, Prey Veng province, suspected of stealing chickens.
This case happened on October 11, 2020 at around 22:00 at the chicken coop of the owner, Meas Touch, male, 56 years old, in Tong Neak village, Sdao Kong commune, Ba Phnom district, Prey Veng province.
The victim who was electrocuted to death was named Yim Sam Ath, male, 25 years old, residing in Thmey Village, Sdao Kong Commune, Ba Phnom District, Prey Veng Province.
Baphnom district authorities said that after receiving the information, Mr. Mam Sarom, Baphnom district police inspector, led the district specialized force to examine the body and found a burn wound on the left palm. After examination, the authorities concluded that the body died due to electric shock.
After examining the body, the authorities handed over the body to the family for a traditional ceremony. The owner of the house was detained at the Ba Phnom District Police Inspectorate to build a case to be sent to court in accordance with the law. Cambodian Red Cross receives hearings and donations of food and supplies from philanthropists
