(Phnom Penh): Some Chinese investors and tourists in Cambodia have congratulated and expressed positive views on the signing of a free trade agreement between Cambodia and China.
The Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement was signed on October 12, 2020, during Wang Yi, State Councilor and Minister of Foreign Affairs of the People's Republic of China, on an official visit to Cambodia.
Here are some Chinese views on the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement:
Suker: The signing of the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement is of great benefit to the Cambodian people and the Chinese people who do business and invest in Cambodia, and this is also a good opportunity. I would like to express my deep gratitude to Chinese President Xi Jinping and Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen for setting up such a great forum.
Hu Jajun: I can eat Cambodian bananas in China and it tastes really good. I hope to bring more Cambodian products to my family and friends in China.
Sen Ying: I hope that after Kovid-19 disappears, I can bring my Chinese friends to visit Cambodia. The scenery here is very beautiful and the people here are very friendly.
Kao Seang: China and Cambodia have built a "common destiny community", especially the signing of the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement. I am confident that the signing of this agreement will push bilateral economic and trade cooperation between the two countries to a new level in the near future and will bring good news for the people of our two countries. From Cambodia and China.
