Acting Head of State issues Royal Decree terminating Lt. Gen. Tat Nimol from Deputy Chairman of the Legal Council of the Ministry of Interior
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, Acting Head of State, has issued a Royal Decree terminating the position of Lt. Gen. Tat Nimol, No. 71910, from the Deputy Chairman of the Legal Council of the Ministry of Interior with the same rank as the Director General.
Although the founder of Cambodia-China relations, His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, died in the land of friendly China on October 15, 2012, the Cambodian-Chinese relationship, which is said to be close The flood did not continue, according to the wisdom of Samdech Sihanouk.
The Beijing government began working closely with the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen in 1997. Especially after the first visit of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister, nicknamed the Cambodian Strongman to China in 1999.
Starting from this visit, the Royal Government of Cambodia of Samdech Techo Hun Sen has become an important cooperation partner of China. Senior Cambodian-Chinese leaders have been in frequent contact with each other. In December 2010, Samdech Techo Hun Sen paid a visit to China, and the two countries strengthened their strategic partnership and cooperation in all fields.
Communication, coordination and cooperation in international and regional affairs between the two countries are getting closer day by day. Based on the high-level political consensus, the two sides have mutual understanding, respect and mutual support, jointly safeguard the situation of China-ASEAN relations, as well as regional peace and stability.
As an indisputable justification, relations between one country and another are focused primarily on political and economic interests. The relationship between Cambodia and China, too, through this close relationship has borne much fruit for both nations and peoples.
What has Cambodia achieved in terms of relations with China for more than 60 years?
* Infrastructure: Infrastructure is a priority of the Royal Government of Cambodia. Road and bridge infrastructure is Cambodia's main artery in connecting the country, boosting the economy and facilitating people's travel.
Since 1998, when Cambodia has achieved full peace, the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has been launching its strategy and policy of building interconnected infrastructure from Phnom Penh to the provinces. Currently, the quality of roads is being improved and the roads are being widened in response to economic growth and increased traffic on the roads.
Separately, 8 major bridges have been completed, with a total length of 7,434 meters, using a budget of approximately 233 million US dollars, and bridges under construction, such as the Cambodia-China Friendship Bridge, Stung Trang-Krouch Chhmar and the bridge across the Bassac River (Sitbo) of the cable project. The third ring road has a total length of 2,127 meters, using a budget of 113 million US dollars.
Minister Sun Chanthol stated that the total number of projects funded by cooperation and grants of Chinese friends that have been completed and are under construction is about 2.741 million US dollars.
Responding to some criticism that the Royal Government is a Chinese satellite. Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the inauguration of Prince Manor Entertainment Center last week raised the question of which country would not be able to implement these infrastructure projects without China.
* Rural development: Cambodia is a country recovering from the flames of war as a developing country, rural development work to help improve the lives and livelihoods of the people is also essential. China has also made significant contributions to Cambodia's rural development.
The Ministry of Rural Development has received two grants from the Chinese government worth about $ 83 million. Through this assistance, the Ministry of Rural Development will develop rural infrastructure, including rural roads, canals, ponds, wells, education, vocational training, sanitation and clean water.
Irrigation: Cambodia is a country largely dependent on agriculture. Irrigation plays an indispensable role for the agricultural sector to thrive. The Royal Government has made efforts to build irrigation systems such as dams and canals to draw water for irrigating farmers' crops.
* Education: Education is another priority of the Royal Government of Cambodia. To achieve the development plan to promote the country to become a high middle-income country by 2030 and a developed country by 2050, increasing human resources with high potential is not to be overlooked.
China has also contributed to the development of many Cambodian students by providing scholarships and opportunities for Cambodian students to improve their knowledge in well-known Chinese schools. The report shows that from 1998 to 2019, more than 3,000 Cambodian students graduated and are continuing their studies in China.
Graduates in some countries have worked as civil servants and others have applied their skills to work in the private sector.
Through good relations between Cambodia and China, China has become a top trading partner and foreign investment for Cambodia. In fact, in 2018, the bilateral trade volume between Cambodia and China totaled about $ 6.5 billion, an increase of 15 percent compared to 2017, which was worth only $ 5.6 billion.
In 2019, the total trade volume between the two countries reached 8.2 billion US dollars, an increase of about 27 percent over 2018. Cambodia and China have ambitions to increase trade between the two countries to 10 billion US dollars by 2023.
Another important fruit and key to boosting trade between Cambodia and China is the Free Trade Agreement (FTA), which will be officially signed during the visit of Wang Yi, State Councilor and Chinese Foreign Minister. Monday, October 12, 2020. The free trade agreement will pave the way for Cambodia to export about 95 percent of its goods to China duty-free out of more than 340 items.
The free trade agreement will boost Cambodia's exports to China by an additional 25 percent.
China is also the largest investor in Cambodia in many sectors, such as industry, agriculture and construction. To date, Chinese direct investment in Cambodia has reached more than 10 billion US dollars.
* Health sector: In order to improve the health and well-being of the people, the Royal Government has also considered strengthening the health sector. China has also made significant contributions to the health sector, such as medical equipment, ambulances and training of Cambodian health officials.
Minister of Health Mam Bunheng has said that as of the beginning of 2019, China has provided assistance to the health sector, such as 40 mobile ambulances, 200 ambulances and 200 ecological machines.
In addition to these grants, China has also provided assistance for the construction of a large hospital building in Tbong Khmum province at a cost of more than 45 million US dollars and the Preah Kosamak Hospital building at a cost of approximately 82 million US dollars. The construction of these two hospitals is a necessary response to provide health services to the people of Cambodia.
In addition to the achievements outlined above, Cambodia and China have always supported each other's international policies, both regionally and internationally.
By: Van Saray Chinese Foreign Minister Pledges to Provide 19 Kovid Vaccines to Cambodia (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): In a meeting with Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong, Co-Chair of the Cambodia-China Intergovernmental Coordinating Committee on Strategic Partnership Yesterday, Wang Yi, State Councilor and Minister of Foreign Affairs of the People's Republic of China, promised to provide Cambodia with 19 Kovid vaccines.
The meeting took place at the Sofitel Hotel, where Wang Yi stayed during a two-day visit to Cambodia.
During the meeting between the two sides, Mr. Hor Namhong asked the Chinese side to consider the possibility of encouraging Chinese investors to transfer more factories from China to Cambodia in accordance with the national agricultural development policy. The Deputy Prime Minister also raised the issue of Kovid 19 vaccine that can be used officially and asked the Chinese side to provide this vaccine as a gift to Cambodia.
