The FTA is not only an agreement on the exemption of tariff barriers, but also covers many other areas, such as investment services, trade facilitation, and the elimination of non-tariff barriers.
Because this free trade agreement is a huge market opening between countries like this, only on October 12, 2020, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Wang, State Councilor and Minister of Foreign Affairs. Of the People's Republic of China presided over the signing ceremony at the Peace Palace in Cambodia. After closing a joint study between the two parties last July.
The free trade agreement between Cambodia and China is now claimed by political expert Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, who has previously claimed that it will help Cambodia grow economically faster and turn Cambodia into It is also the second largest country in Singapore.
The FTA was also seen by economist Dr. Ky Sereywat, President of the Chinese Studies Center of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, as another venture of the Royal Government of Cambodia to establish a new trade pole outside Europe. And America. Which can make Cambodia escape the economic pressure of the Western powers as well.
The economist also added that the agreement will give Cambodia six major opportunities for Cambodia's sustainable development.
The goods that the Chinese side tariffs on Cambodia are various types of machinery and vehicles. The reason why the Chinese side levies tariffs on all these goods is because the Chinese side does not want its imports to affect domestic products. In addition, the taxation of these goods is not a problem for the Cambodian side, because Cambodia is not a country that produces all these materials. This was further confirmed by Mr. Sok Sopheak, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce.
According to Mr. Sok Sopheak, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce, most of Cambodia's goods exempt from China are chemical minerals for industrial use, as well as imported plastics for assembly and export.
