He added that Japan is currently providing construction assistance for emergency bridge reconstruction projects in flood-prone areas, with seven bridges being built in Prey Veng and Kratie provinces at a cost of about $ 35 million. The 366-kilometer National Road 5 is also under construction, with a concessional loan from the Japanese government of about $ 500 million.
