National Bank of Cambodia Celebrates 41st Anniversary of National Bank Reconstruction
(Phnom Penh): The National Bank of Cambodia celebrates the 41st anniversary of the re-establishment of the National Bank. On that occasion, Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, said that the decision to establish the Central Bank and the national currency quickly is the right decision of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
According to Chea Chanto, it has been 41 years since the Central Bank was re-established after the liberation on January 7, 1979, after the nation and people of Cambodia were liberated from the genocidal regime. Pol Pot.
He added that at that time, the capital of the National Bank of Cambodia increased continuously from 5 billion riels in 1992 to 100 billion riels in 2000.
Mr. Chea Chanto also pointed out that since 2000, the banking system has developed rapidly and steadily after the successful completion of the banking sector reform. In addition, the banking system has been continuously modernized and has made a significant contribution to maintaining macroeconomic stability, supporting economic growth, improving the economic and social environment and reducing poverty.
Overall, he said, over the past two decades, the inflation rate has been kept low at around 2.5 percent, with better exchange rate stability at around 4,050 riel per US dollar. Banking assets grew rapidly from just $ 0.5 billion in 1998 to $ 56 billion today, an increase of 112 times.
