Legal Awareness: Contract Termination
1: Termination of contract according to law
The statute of limitations (period determined by law) of the termination of the right to terminate the contract on the grounds of non-performance of obligations and the right to demand the restoration of the original status or return shall be for a period of 5 years after the non-compliance. Implementing this obligation means that after this period of 5 years, the party entitled to dissolve will no longer have the right to exercise its rights.
The right to dissolve in the contract in this case is the right of the parties, if the contract states the "conditions for termination of the contract", the parties to the contract must respect and comply with the contract.
If any party intends to terminate the contract, that party must show its willingness to terminate the contract, with the effect of the termination of the contract, the party shall be exempt from the obligations in the contract, except in the case of compensation (if the termination of this contract To the detriment of the interests of either party, the offender must compensate the injured party of the contract).
On the other hand, if the party receives part or all of the other debit, the receiving party must make a donation to the other party (return) at the time of termination of the contract, but if the party has a case of payment, that party must pay. In cash, including interest, from the date of receipt of the principal. On the other hand, if the case is an object, the party must return it to the other party as an object, including the proceeds from that object.
3: Termination of contract by agreement of the parties
The right to terminate the contract by agreement This case is the easiest because, although there is no limit to the right to dissolve, one party has the right to dissolve if the other party agrees to the contract. At this point, however, the law protects the interests of third parties by not allowing the termination of the contract to cause harm to the interests of third parties.
Floods continue to rise in Pursat city as Battambang city begins to flood
(Phnom Penh): Floods caused by rain have not subsided in the northwest until October 11, 2020. The floods continue to pose a threat to Pursat and Battambang provinces.
Mr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Pursat Province, said that in the morning of October 11, 2020, the water level of Pursat River was about 5.5 meters higher than the emergency level of about 0.5 meters. The provincial governor added that due to the high water level of Pursat River, the lowlands around Pursat city and Kandeang district were almost completely submerged.
This morning, the provincial governor is also inspecting the flood situation and putting out some measures to avoid danger to the people.
Please note that the low pressure has been raining continuously for 5-6 days. Several days of torrential rain caused flash floods in the northwestern provinces of the country. Pursat and Battambang provinces were the worst affected by the floods.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen during a meeting of the Council of Ministers on Friday, October 9, 2020, reminded all relevant authorities to carry out evacuation operations for flood victims and solve various problems.
