(Koh Kong): Coastal City Development Group EK, one of the largest tourism development companies in Cambodia, has launched a new project in the Darasakor area, the Boeung Darachan Tourism and Culture Borey Project, to serve additional needs. For national tourists in the context of the current Kovid-19 crisis and to prepare for the presence of international tourists after the Kovid crisis is over in the near future.
The new project was officially inaugurated on October 9, 2020 under the chairmanship of Mr. Pak Sokhom, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, on behalf of Minister Thong Khon, together with Mr. Hab Touch, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, on behalf of Ms. Phuong Sakona and Ms. Mithona Phuthong, Governor. Koh Kong province, as well as the participation of company leaders and many other Cambodian government officials.
On that occasion, Mr. Pak Sokhom praised Costa City Development Group EK for its efforts to develop support facilities and new tourism products in Darasakor area, Koh Kong province and brought economic and social development. Notably. In fact, the Boeung Darachan Borey Tourism and Culture Borey project is one of the other development projects of the Stardream project.
He said that through the launch of this project will attract more investment to visit and relax from many investors and tourists. Not only that, this development project will create more job opportunities and income for Cambodians and local people as well.
