At the request of the community, Minister Veng Sakhon Tha will help repair the 160-meter-long dam to hold water for common use.
Separately, Siem Reap has 62 community forests covering 34,690 hectares of forest. Currently, most communities rely on the collection of non-timber forest products such as mushrooms, wild fruits, wild bees, processed bamboo, processed bamboo, used and sold, which can earn an average of 8-12 million riels per year per community.
This afternoon, the distribution and planting of bamboo seedlings is symbolic of the Forestry Administration's 11,000 bamboo planting activities for 11 forest communities in seven provinces: Kampong Chhnang, Kampong Speu, Kampong Thom, Pursat, Siem Reap, Preah Vihear and Oddar Meanchey. . Ratanakkiri Provincial Police Commissioner Donates More Than 30 Million Riels and $ 3,300 to Wat Kiri Ratanaram
