It should be noted that Kathina is a traditional Buddhist festival that Cambodians start after the rainy season. Kathin festival is always paraded in all temples from the 1st day of the lunar month to the 15th day of the lunar month, no pagoda is missed. And if the temple does not have any Kathin, the temple must also be prepared as a pagoda Kathin.
The Kathin procession to each temple is celebrated with great rejoicing, and the initiators always prepare the Kathina equipment, such as the trident, the sangha, the land, and other gifts such as the bottom of the bowl, the knife, the needle, the needle, the guard bag and the umbrella. They marched to the designated temple. NEC: On the 9th, nearly 20,000 people went to register to vote
