This will cause the weather in Cambodia to continue to rain for several days in moderate to heavy levels, making the northwestern and northern provinces in the area adjacent to the Dangrek and Cardamom Mountains can continue to flood. More rain. During the same period, there may be rain, wind, and high waves in the coastal areas and on the sea surface.
In light of the above-mentioned weather conditions, the relevant ministries, institutions, local authorities at all levels and the public, especially the people in the above areas, please be informed and pay more attention to avoid any danger. Other things that can happen eventually.
The following is a press release from the Ministry of Water Resources: The Mine Authority issued guidelines to strengthen mine prevention and control measures to prevent mine and explosive remnants of war during and after the floods.
According to the observations and weather forecasts presented by the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, the effects of the low pressure system on Cambodia have resulted in continuous rains throughout the country, leaving some provinces suffering. The effects of rainfall caused floods in Battambang, Pursat and Pailin provinces.
During and after the floods, some landmines and unexploded ordnance (UXO) were found to have been washed away by landslides from anti-personnel mines, anti-tank mines and various explosive remnants of war. Lives of people eventually, especially those living in areas affected by landmines and explosive remnants of war.
In order to prevent the dangers of landmines and explosive remnants of war during and after the floods, the Mine Authority recommends to all Provincial Mine Action Committees, all operators to reduce mine and explosive hazard hazard education and related organizations. Participate in the implementation of some of the following measures:
* First, continue to monitor the safety of places and low-lying areas where people live and pass through to avoid the dangers of landmines and explosive remnants of war.
* Second: Disseminate to the people, students, boys and girls to be very careful about the dangers of landmines and explosive remnants of war and when found, please report to local authorities, village chiefs, commune chiefs or demining operators. Who was there immediately to take those seeds and destroy them.
* Third: Prepare content to disseminate and produce educational materials to provide education agencies to reduce the risk of landmines and explosive remnants of war, mine networks, community volunteers, teachers, as a means for direct education to the people and students in Flood-affected areas.
* Fourth: Respond in a timely manner to the collection and destruction of landmines and explosive remnants of war reported by the people.
* Fifth: Immediate signage in areas suspected of mines and hazards due to mines and explosive remnants of war that can flow through water and sediment to prevent people from entering or passing through.
* 6: Continue to educate people about the dangers of landmines and explosive remnants of war on a regular basis to people who are temporarily staying in safe places as well as other areas to prevent people from being affected by landmines. And explosive remnants of war during and after the floods.
