(Battambang): Mr. Lim Kean Hor, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, said that climate change on our planet is not caused by Cambodia, a small country, the main root is from greenhouse gas emissions. Heavy industrial plants in large countries and destruction of natural resources.
Minister Lim Kean Hor made this statement in response to allegations by unscrupulous groups and attacks from some quarters that blamed Cambodia for causing climate change due to deforestation.
During a visit to inspect the flood situation in the northwestern province on October 10, 2020, the Minister said, "Those who are causing global climate change are caused by countries with heavy industries. "The big ones who have a lot of money, they have been investing for a long time."
The Minister of Water Resources stated that unlike what is being accused of Cambodia, because it is clear that Cambodia does not yet have a heavy industry, but in other large countries there are many. On the other hand, blaming Cambodia for deforestation is not right, although Cambodia does cut down the forest, it is far smaller than other countries.
He also said that the presence of many forests on earth contributes to the balance of carbon dioxide and oxygen. On the other hand, if there is a lot of forest, it also helps prevent landslides and erosion during floods.
He recalled at a recent meeting on climate change in Paris, France, calling on countries around the world to take action to prevent the effects of the weather.
According to Minister Lim Kean Hor, the Royal Government of Cambodia is very thoughtful in participating in preventing climate change. For example, when there is rain, storm or low pressure passing through Cambodia, the Royal Government has issued a press release to the people beforehand, especially the measures to be ready to intervene and have a direct inspection, that is, not to let the people suffer due to lack of action. From the authorities and the Royal Government.
