(Battambang): Mr. Men Pheakdey, Director of the Data Management and Macro Analysis Department of the National Bank of Cambodia, said that the reorganization of loans during the period affected by Kovid 19 virus is very important and beneficial. For customers.
Mr. Men Pheakdey made the remarks at a dissemination workshop on the Cambodian microfinance sector held in Maung Russey district, Battambang province on October 9, 2020.
Mr. Men Pheakdey said that seeing the benefits of refinancing loans to customers during the Kovid 19 period, on March 27, 2020, the National Bank of Cambodia issued a circular on restructuring loans. In order to alleviate the burden on borrowers who are facing major income declines and difficulties in repayment. With this also to support economic activity during the Kovid.
He explained that another benefit that customers get is to provide customers with a number of benefits such as deferred and reduced interest rates, reduced principal amount, extended credit (repayment time). And additions or exchanges of borrowers and guarantors.
Kea Boran, Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Microfinance Association of Cambodia, said that in the difficult circumstances caused by Kovid 19, the association has been actively working with its members and stakeholders, especially the National Bank of Cambodia, to help clients. Affected by this.
He added that as of September 27, 2020, more than 276,000 clients of microfinance institutions in Cambodia have applied for credit restructuring. Of these, nearly 260,000 clients requested more than 94% of the total applicants for credit restructuring, with a total loan size of $ 1.260 million.
On that occasion, Mr. Men Pheakdey requested that local authorities and all stakeholders need to have a clear understanding of the work and other issues related to the microfinance sector to serve as a basis for supporting and assisting its citizens. To prevent them from getting into debt and being exploited by traders or informal lenders.
