Senior official of the Ministry of Tourism: Tourism safety rules must be implemented in the context of Kovid-19
(Battambang): Mr. Song Tong Hap, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, stated that all places where visitors come and go must instruct the owners of those places to follow the tourism safety rules to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease into the community. The government has waived the one-year tourism license fee in 2021 as an incentive for tourism business owners.
Mr. Song Tong Hap made this statement during a meeting to monitor and evaluate the implementation of tourism safety rules at Battambang Provincial Hall on October 9, 2020.
Mr. Yim Sieb, Deputy Governor of Battambang Province, said that on behalf of the Provincial Administration, the Provincial Department of Tourism must pay attention to the strict implementation of Circular No. 004, dated June 4, 2020 on the implementation of the rules. Tourism safety during the prevention of the spread of Kovid-19 disease and must be regularly disseminated to all tourism businesses in their jurisdiction to follow the tourism safety rules.
He reminded that tourism safety rules are mandatory and additional conditions in applying for a new or renewable tourism license for each type of tourism business.
Mr. Song Tong Hap said that in Battambang province, about 55 restaurant owners, restaurants, guesthouses, hotels, resorts, tourism services (including 3 tourist communities) have received a large number of tourism safety labels from the Battambang Provincial Department of Tourism.
He said that the Label Tourism Safety Rules were designed to clarify the implementation of tourism operations in response to the tourism safety rules in the context of Kovid-19, which the Ministry announced on June 5, 2020, including There are: accommodation services, tourism, restaurant-canteen tourism services, water transport services, land transport services, tourist resorts and tourism communities.
Please be reminded that the receipt of Label Tourism Safety Rules now is to confirm the implementation of tour operators in accordance with the conditions of the Ministry of Tourism set in the Tourism Safety Rules and will continue to be implemented 100% in December. 2020 as well.
