General knowledge: Which countries allow legal sex services?
(Foreign): Currently, sex work is considered an illegal business for most countries in the world, including Cambodia, but there are still some countries that allow people to do business legally. . So which countries still allow the operation of legal sex services?
New Zealand In 2003, the New Zealand government allowed people to run legal sex businesses. This business owner can get legal business rights under the Public Health Law and the Labor Law, which means that this business owner can get the same benefits and get the same rights as the employees in the labor sector. Other.
* Australia In this federal state, the operation of sex work depends on the state, with some states allowing legal business and others not.
In Bangladesh, in Southeast Asia, the government has made it legal for women to engage in sex work, with all forms of sex work being legal, but not for men.
In addition to these four countries, there are a number of other countries that have easy access to sex work, even without a valid permit, including Japan, Thailand, Singapore, South Korea, China, Vietnam, Belgium, Brazil, Canada, Colombia, Ecuador, France, Germany, Greece, Indonesia. The Netherlands and so on.
