(Phnom Penh): Samdech Preah Moha Sometheathipady Non Nget, Samdech Preah Sang, Director of the Kingdom of Cambodia, on the morning of Friday, October 9, 2020, presided over Decision on the appointment of 5 teachers in Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province as his personal adviser, held at Wat Botum Vatey, Phnom Penh.
Pursuant to the decision of the Board of Priests of the Kingdom of Cambodia, Preah Krou Chea Preah Anukon Srok Rolea Bier, Preah Krou Chea Samuh, Preah Koun Srok Rolea Bier and Preah Krou Chea Krou Chief Inspector of a total of 5 pagodas as personal advisers to Samdech Preah Moha Sometheathipady Non Nget Samdech Chief Monk of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The decision on the appointment of Samdech Preah Moha Sometheathipady Non Nget is as follows:
* First: Preah Mettisathavong Kosal, Honorary King and Dhammanuvat, Preah Anukon Srok Rolea Bier, has been appointed as a personal advisor to Samdech Preah Moha Sometheathipadei Non Nget, Samdech Preah Sang, Director General of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
* Second: Rev. Serey Panhanan Ouch Sophal, Preah Samuh, Deputy Chief of Rolea Bier District, Preah Chao Athikar Wat Chiv Rainsy (Wat Damnak Key), Cheung Kreav Commune, Rolea Bier District, Kampong Chhnang Province, has been appointed as a personal advisor Kingdom of Cambodia.
* Third: Rev. Serey Mongkul Moni Moch Sauly, Chief Inspector of Wat Samdech Non Nget Sen Chey Satharam, also known as Wat Kralanh Chas, located in Srang Tear Village, Prasnup Commune, Rolea Bier District, Kampong Chhnang Province, has been appointed as a personal advisor to Samdech Preah Moha Sometheathipady Non Nget. Of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
* Fourth: Preah Vihear Visoth Vongsachar Neang Phearun, Chief Bishop of Wat Banlang, Pong Ror Commune, Rolea Bier District, Kampong Chhnang Province, has been appointed as a personal advisor to Samdech Preah Moha Sometheathipatei Non Nget, Samdech Preah Sang, President of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
* Fifth: Priest Serey Thom Vongsa Sengda, Chief Bishop of Wat Thom Rattanasophea-Trea, Sre Thmei Commune, Rolea Bier District, Kampong Chhnang Province, has been appointed as a personal advisor to Samdech Preah Moha Sometheathipadei Non Nget, Samdech Preah Sang, President of the Kingdom of Cambodia. The National Police Commissioner and the Governor of Phnom Penh told all Borey owners to install security cameras and have their own water tank for timely intervention
(Phnom Penh): The National Police Commissioner General, General Dr. Neth Savoeun and Mr. Khuong Sreng, the Governor of Phnom Penh, told all Borey owners to be equipped with security cameras and to have at least one private fire truck to easily intervene in time. A fire broke out in its location.
In a meeting on strengthening security in Boreys and condominiums in Phnom Penh on the afternoon of October 8, 2020, General Dr. Neth Savoeun and Mr. Khuong Sreng confirmed that the owners of Borey and condominiums must be equipped with security cameras And have this security system to ensure warmth to the people who are staying.
Mr. Khuong Sreng said that when a crime occurs, the owner of the location must cooperate and provide data from security cameras to the authorities to have a basis for identifying the target, and all data attached to the Phnom Penh Police will be kept confidential. No part of this site may be reproduced without our written permission.
In addition, Mr. Khuong Sreng requested that the owners of major cities in Phnom Penh to have fire trucks, the capital administration will ask the Royal Government to exempt. He said that in the past, some Boreys have set a good example, such as Borey Peng Huoth and Borey in Koh Pich, always sent out water trucks to intervene when there is a fire, so hopefully the owners of big cities will buy fire trucks. To prevent and prevent fires together.
Violence against women is a major obstacle to women's participation in national development and a serious burden on the national economy and society. The Royal Government loses money on health services, loss of productivity, safe havens for women and children, social services to rehabilitate women victims, legal services and some other necessary support services.
Therefore, the National Action Plan on the Prevention of Violence against Women 2019-2023 is an important tool for reducing violence against women.
Mr. Phay Siphan, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Chairman of the Royal Government Spokesperson Unit, said that the draft National Action Plan on the Prevention of Violence against Women 2019-2023 was developed in accordance with the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4, Plan National Development Strategy 2019-2023 and Cambodia's Sustainable Development Goals in Goal 5 on "Achieving Gender Equality and Empowering Women and Children".
The draft National Action Plan for the Prevention of Violence against Women 2019-2023 sets out four strategies, including: prevention, legal protection and multidisciplinary services, law and policy, and monitoring and evaluation. .
