According to Mr. Phay Siphan, the three-year rolling public investment program 2021-2023 is designed based on the total expenditure requirements for the implementation of the National Strategic Development Plan 2019-2023 to be in line with the actual situation of fluctuations in prices and inflation. Based on the amount of co-financing that development partners have promised.
Mr. Phay Siphan said that the 3-year rolling public investment program 2021-2023 has about 629 projects to be implemented. Of these, 203 projects are ongoing projects that require a capital of 8,397 million US dollars and 426 projects are projects for the implementation of the PFRC, which requires a capital of 4,399 million US dollars.
The draft law concludes that the three-year rolling public investment program is an important policy tool to achieve overall and sectoral macroeconomic growth goals in the National Strategic Development Plan 2019-2023.
The conclusion also reminded the authorities from all ministries and institutions to continue to pay high attention to ensure the quality of information on public investment projects that ministries and institutions must provide to the Ministry of Planning for the effective preparation of this three-year rolling public investment program. High.
