(Phnom Penh): The Technical Director General of the Ministry of Health, Prof. Hok Kim Cheng, has supported the National Eye Health Program and all national and international partner organizations to continue to work together to reduce the rate of blindness in Cambodia.
This statement was made by Professor Hok Kim Cheng on the occasion of presiding over the dissemination of the World Health Report on Vision and Celebration of the World Eye Health Day 2020 under the theme "Eye Health Gives Hope" on 08 This October 2020 at the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital.
Professor Hok Kim Cheng said that the achievements of the National Eye Health Program in 2019, the national research on blindness and vision loss found that in Cambodia, the rate of blindness has decreased to 0. 37% and the main cause of blindness is cataract 80.4%.
"Therefore, we would like to encourage the national eye health program, national-international partner organizations and humanitarian organizations in the past to continue to put together more strategies, including disseminating to the people to understand and access medical services," he said. In hospitals, especially the poor, to receive free medical services through the Equity Fund of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
"The National Eye Health Program is an important staff and has been incorporated into the Ministry of Health's strategic plan for non-communicable diseases," he said. "People in rural areas as well as everywhere have access to this eye health care service."
Meanwhile, Professor Ngy Meng, Director of the National Eye Health Program and Director of the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital, said, "As of 2019, the National Eye Health Program of the Ministry of Health has provided care and examination services to more than 300,000 people. "More than 80,000 people underwent cataract surgery."
Please be informed that cataracts are opacity caused by aging and other diseases, making it impossible for light rays to pass through the optic nerve, which reduces vision and is the main cause. Of blindness in Cambodia. Drug use destroys itself, family and society! Nationwide drug crackdown for October 8: 27 cases cracked, 56 arrested
