Driving, be careful! A family died in a car accident with a Camry in Sambo district, Kratie province
This incident happened on the evening of October 7, 2020 along National Road 7, Kratie, Stung Treng, at the point of Ta Kot Bridge in Sangkom Village, Sandan Commune, Sambo District, Kratie Province.
According to the Sambo district police report, the driver of the car, Phal Den, a 27-year-old man living in the land concession village of Kakod, Sambok commune, Chit Borei district, Kratie province, escaped after the incident.
The victims were a 26-year-old motorcyclist, Sam Roeun Phalla, and his wife, 19-year-old Chan Doeun, and their 1-year-old son. All three of them live in Dar village, Da commune, Chet Borey district, Kratie province.
At present, the bodies of the three parents and children have been handed over to their families for the traditional ceremony, while the car and motorcycle exhibits have been taken by the specialized police and kept at the Sambo District Police Inspectorate.
