(Banteay Meanchey): At least six political parties attended a meeting to promote political parties and stakeholders for the review of the voter list and voter registration 2020 in Banteay Meanchey province, which took place on the morning of October 8, 2020 at In the meeting hall of the Provincial Election Committee.
The six political parties are: FUNCINPEC, the Khmer United National Party, the Cambodian People's Party, the Khmer Anti-Poverty Party, the Alliance for Democracy, and the Khmer Patriotic Party.
Mr. Yang Sak, Director of Banteay Meanchey Provincial Election Secretariat, said in the meeting that in order to disseminate to political parties and stakeholders on cooperation in security, safety and order for the examination of the voter list and voter registration in 2020.
Mr. Yang Sak added that in Banteay Meanchey province, there were 87,330 names and district voter lists throughout the province, 24,243 people with type 3 ID cards, and 39,040 people without type 3 ID cards. A total of 24,047 names have not been found.
He added that Banteay Meanchey province has 65 communes. In the 2020 voter registration, type 1 and type 2 ID cards have expired and only type 3 ID cards can be used to register. Citizens who can register to vote in 2020 from the age of 18 in the commune where they live.
Mr. Ly Sary, Deputy Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, said that the review of the voter list and voter registration 2020 aims to ensure that the voter list is complete, accurate and up to date.
(Phnom Penh): The head of the Anti-Corruption Unit (ACU), Senior Minister Om Yentieng, said that as of June 2020, 140 cases of money laundering in Cambodia and 22 cases have been sent to court, which is a small point. Most.
He said this on the morning of October 8, 2020, on the occasion of the Anti-Corruption Unit, in cooperation with the Ministry of Justice, organized a workshop on "Management, Management and Seizure of Crimes" at the Anti-Corruption Unit.
Mr. Om Yentieng stated: "As of June 2020, 140 cases of money laundering have been investigated and 22 cases have been sent to court with the detention and freezing of some assets in "There are five cases that have already been tried, which may have a final verdict / judgment in the near future to implement the seizure."
He said that in the context of anti-corruption and anti-money laundering, Cambodia has international obligations to fulfill. In terms of anti-corruption, Cambodia has received the second round of evaluation of the implementation of the United Nations Convention against Corruption (UNCAC), and the visit of Cambodia by UN experts and two countries: Esvani and Thailand on November 30, 31 and October 1, 2019.
He added that this was a challenge for Cambodia's efforts to get off the gray list (last defense in January / February 2021). In practice, Cambodia has done little / never carried out confiscations, and the management of seized and frozen assets is still poor, causing a lot of national budget losses.
