However, on the evening of October 7, the workers, who were the drivers, changed their minds and refused to leave the car to collect garbage as agreed. General knowledge: Before the great era like today, how did the ancient people count the years?
Of course, due to the lack of a global communication system, the ancients did not yet agree on an era for counting the universal years, that is, they used different timepieces in different regions. The number of hours, days, months, years and seasons is not the same.
As for the Khmer Empire and the territories under the ancient Khmer Empire, there was no AD and Mahamat era yet. Khmer people have three major eras for daily use, including the Chul era and the Buddhist era.
