Samdech Techo Hun Sen: Climate change is an interconnected issue that must be addressed in a comprehensive and balanced policy, both social, economic and environmental aspects (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia Climate change is an interconnected issue that needs to be addressed through a comprehensive and balanced policy on social, economic and environmental aspects.
This was stated by Samdech Techo at the Leadership Event of the Climate Vulnerability Forum (CVF) held on video on the night of October 7, 2020. The invitation to attend the forum was made at the invitation of Ms. Sek Hasina, Prime Minister of the People's Republic of Bangladesh and Chair of the Climate Vulnerability Forum.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen considers climate change to be another worrying issue that will have serious and unpredictable consequences for society, economy and security in the region and the world. In recent years, a series of disasters around the world have become more severe and intense than we have ever experienced.
"At the global level, I see climate change as a cellular issue that needs to be addressed through a comprehensive and balanced policy in terms of social, economic and environmental aspects," he said.
He said that in the current context, advancing and adhering to the regionalism and multilateral framework is an important principle for addressing the challenges that are emerging in all areas, especially Born from climate change.
He added that despite Cambodia's limited resources and capabilities, Cambodia has a high level of commitment and political will to contribute to global efforts to address climate change based on key principles of the United Nations Framework Convention. On climate change, especially the principle of shared responsibility, but with different obligations based on their respective capabilities.
