At 8 pm tonight, Samdech Techo Hun Sen will attend a forum to discuss vulnerabilities caused by climate change
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will attend the Leadership Event of the Climate Vulnerability Forum (CVF) at 8 pm on October 7, 2020. .
Samdech Techo Hun Sen will deliver a special speech at this forum. In this live intervention, the Prime Minister will highlight the serious impact of climate change on socio-economic development and security in the region as well as the world.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen will also make recommendations in practice on a comprehensive and effective response to the negative effects of climate change on the environment, economy and society.
As an important global forum for cooperation between developing countries vulnerable to climate change, the Leadership Forum of the Climate Vulnerability Forum will be attended by the Secretary-General of the United Nations and the Head of State. And the government, as well as key partners.
This leadership event underscores the urgency of action and the need for all countries to update on national contributions to the implementation of the Paris Agreement.
The forum will also highlight the importance of strengthening climate resilience efforts, as well as responding to the Kovid-19 epidemic and post-crisis recovery, to maintain the momentum of resilience. And reduce damage and displacement caused by natural disasters.
