Samdech Techo Hun Sen's message on World Tourism Day 2020 is posted on UNWTO website
(Spain): The World Tourism Organization (UNWTO) has expressed its full support for the message of the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of the celebration of World Tourism Day 2020 and posted the content of this message on its website. Its official.
The posting of the message of the Prime Minister of Cambodia on the UNWTO website took place from October 6, 2020, as Cambodia considered this gesture to reflect the attention of the top leaders of the member countries of the tourism organization. The world plays an important role in tourism in the economic recovery from the Kovid-19 crisis.
The World Tourism Organization also highlighted Cambodia's efforts to pay attention to the implementation of tourism safety and hygiene measures, especially the role of the Cambodian Ministry of Tourism.
According to the World Tourism Organization, under the leadership of the ASEAN Tourism Cooperation in the 2020 term and chair of the World Tourism Forum 2021, the Ministry of Tourism of Cambodia has organized a number of common interests, including:
2. Lead the development of ASEAN safety and hygiene rules.
3: Lead the preparation of a plan to restore ASEAN tourism after the Kovid-19 crisis, with Cambodia has been mapping the road for the restoration of tourism as well.
World Tourism Day is often celebrated by members of the World Tourism Organization (UNWTO) on or after September 27 to promote the future outlook of tourism in specific directions to contribute to the achievement. The world agenda.
For 2020, World Tourism Day is being held under the theme "Tourism and Rural Development", with a particular focus on ways to restart tourism and transform tourism potential as a catalyst for greater resilience and responsibility. Better for the future.
The Ministry of Tourism celebrated World Tourism Day in Siem Reap on October 3, 2020. At the event, community tourism officials and people's representatives expressed support for the development of rural tourism to strengthen the local economy and celebrate peace, which is the foundation of tourism development, bring prosperity and opportunities. New to every citizen.
The whole ceremony committed to implement the recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen through congratulatory messages and supported the following rules:
Second, the Capital-Provincial Department of Tourism must cooperate with local authorities, communities, relevant institutions to develop more rural tourism development plans in response to new global tourism trends as well as increasing domestic tourism.
Third, the ongoing tourism community must pay attention to create more new products by trying to research and compile the attractiveness of natural resources, culture, traditions and customs in their area to turn those potentials into unique tourism products in the region. .
Fourth, all development partners who are participating in the development of rural tourism in Cambodia must cooperate with local authorities, tourism communities and stakeholders under the guidance of the Capital-Provincial Department of Tourism to implement the recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen effectively.
Fifth, the Department of Tourism must cooperate with relevant parties to organize and train human resources at the local level to be more active to ensure job sustainability and satisfactory service delivery.
