TOKYO (Reuters) - China on Wednesday issued a statement calling on the United States to abandon the Cold War-style mindset, and the city even accused US Secretary of State Mike Pompeo of defamation and creating an atmosphere. Malicious politics on Beijing. This is according to the release by CNA on Wednesday afternoon, October 7, 2020.
In a statement, the Chinese embassy in Japan said: "Pompeo has once again fabricated and lied about China and created a confrontational and malicious political environment against China." "We urge the United States to abandon the Cold War mentality, including discrimination, and stop making unreasonable accusations against China, taking relations with China in a constructive manner."
China's reaction comes after US Secretary of State Mike Pompeo, during a visit to Japan on Tuesday, called on Australia, Japan and India to work together to counter growing influence. China in the region. A hotel in Sihanoukville put a statue of Jayavarman VII on the fence and the authorities immediately took action.
(Sihanoukville): It is shocking for a hotel in Sihanoukville to take the head of Jayavarman VII, the King of Cambodia, as a shrine to the end of a stone fence near the entrance. The hotel has caused a great deal of criticism from the public.
The official said that after learning about this information, the Governor of Kouch Chamroeun Province ordered the professional officers of the Department of Culture and Fine Arts, the Department of Tourism and the relevant law enforcement forces to facilitate the hotel owner to remove the statue of King Jayavarman VII from the fence. To keep or display tourists appropriately inside the hotel to maintain the traditional cultural values of Cambodia.
