Please read the following press release: Senior Minister Sun Chanthol: In the last three months, the Ministry has fined nearly 3 billion riels for expired vehicles.
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, said that in the last three months, the Ministry of Public Works has fined vehicles that exceed the validity of technical inspections called "Cheak". A total of nearly 3 billion riel, and as of now, there are still about 360,000 vehicles that have expired and have not been inspected.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol further stated that so far, the Ministry has received a large number of vehicles for technical inspection, and there are still about 360,000 vehicles that have expired and have not yet been inspected. Technical specifications are still up, so all vehicle owners are required to check the car in time to avoid causing traffic accidents and avoid fines.
According to Mr. Chuon Vorn, Director General of the General Department of Land Transport, for the past three months since the implementation of the law on fines for vehicles that have expired, more than 80,000 vehicles have been taken. Inspected the specifications and found nearly 20,000 vehicles that were expired and fined.
GMAC donates 40,000 units to the Ministry of Education to help prevent the transmission of 19 Kovid virus during the reopening of educational institutions
Mr. Van So Eang, President of the Garment Manufacturers Association, stated that seeing the reopening of the educational institutions, the association believes that the relationship between the public and private sectors is a partnership, and therefore the 40,000 mass support is a contribution. The prevention and fight against the spread of Kovid 19, especially to students in schools and higher education throughout Cambodia.
"The private sector has always paid attention to the education sector, which is one of the government's top priorities in human resource training, so this 40,000-dollar subsidy is a social responsibility," said Van Sou Ieng. "Private sector to contribute back to society."
Dr. Hang Chuon Naron thanked the Garment Manufacturers Association of Cambodia for its contribution to the prevention and control of the spread of Kovid 19 in the education sector under the guidance of the Prime Minister Techo Hun Sen. Sen to fight against the spread of Kovid virus in Cambodia.
Dr. Hang Chuon Naron said, "On behalf of the leadership and staff of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, I would like to thank the Garment Manufacturers Association of Cambodia for their cooperation and support to the Ministry to distribute to the public educational institutions. "Staff, teachers and students use it to prevent the spread of Kovid 19."
Please be informed that tomorrow, the 8th, the association will also donate 40,000 masks to the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training to help prevent the transmission of 19 Kovid virus in Cambodia during the reopening of training centers and institutes. Technical and professional in Cambodia.
Of that, 20,000 masks will be donated to the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and another 20,000 masks to the General Department of Technical and Vocational Education and Training of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training.
The Association would like to point out that the above mass is manufactured by a factory that is properly registered with the US Food and Drug Administration, and that this mass production is also recognized by EU standards.
The association hopes that this support will help prevent the transmission of Kovid 19 virus in accordance with the guidelines of the Ministry of Health, as well as prevent transmission into communities in Cambodia.
Despite Tram's efforts, the Kovid-19 vaccine is unlikely to be achieved before election day.
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - The US Food and Drug Administration (FDA) instructed vaccine developer COVID-19 on Tuesday that it wants to collect safety data at least two months before the vaccine is approved. Vaccination approval is likely to be delayed until after the presidential election. This is according to the release by CNA on Wednesday afternoon, October 7, 2020.
A senior US official says the White House has agreed to the principle, thwarting Trump's hopes of getting a vaccine before the election. "The new FDA guidelines will make it harder for us to get the vaccine approved before election day," Trump said in a Twitter post.
The FDA has issued a new guideline stating that participants in the COVID-19 vaccine trial should be subject to a two-month follow-up period to ensure that the vaccine is effective. And safety. The changes are the latest effort by the FDA to ban political gambling over vaccines and ensure public safety.
According to a statement from the Ministry of Health, obtained by Fresh News on October 7, 2020, Cambodia is still at risk of contracting Kovid-19 virus at all times. To help prevent the spread of Kovid-19 virus into the community, strengthen the 14-day vaccination or isolation of individuals who need to be vaccinated for 14 days at home and in the community.
In addition, proper participation is required under the guidance of the Ministry of Health from individuals and is strictly controlled by local authorities throughout the country after receiving the first negative Kovid-19 test. The person is allowed to go for a four-day detention or detention at their respective homes.
Failure to properly follow the guidelines of the Ministry of Health, such as the movement of an individual from one place to another, or to come in contact with others during catastrophic or isolated activities, may result in transmission. The Kovid-19 virus transmits the virus from one person to another and can also lead to community transmission if the person is infected with the Kovid-19 virus.
The Ministry of Health has once again appealed to the public, relevant ministries, sub-national authorities, local authorities and all of you to join in preventing the transmission of Kovid-19 virus into the Cambodian community. Follow the instructions of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and the Ministry of Health by implementing the following key guidelines:
* Sub-national authorities shall assign commune / sangkat and village officials and organize village working groups to strengthen the implementation of the Chatsalysak housing rules by monitoring the practices of the Chatsalysak and protecting the safety and security of those who have The desire to run away can run away.
* In the event of a fugitive, the law applicable to the fugitive shall apply.
 * Inspect the situation at the residence of the caregiver at home, sent from the provincial health examination center and from the health center or referral hospital and arrange for further work based on the results of the most thorough monitoring.
For individuals doing home remodeling, please complete the following measures within 14 days:
1: Stay in a separate room for 14 days and the room must be well ventilated 2: Wear a mask and keep at least one and a half meters away from other family members and others 3: Cut Reduce the use of shared space such as bathroom, kitchen, etc.
4: Monitor your personal health: Check your body temperature twice a day. If you have a fever, cough, sore throat, runny nose, difficulty breathing, headache, muscle aches or diarrhea, please report to 115 or to a doctor near you. Health center or public hospital, etc.
5: Wash your hands often, especially before and after preparing food after going to the toilet and when you see dirty hands.
6: Cover mouth and nose when coughing or sneezing with a paper towel or bend the elbows and wash your hands immediately. 7: Dispose of waste in a sealed bin. Other uses on a regular basis
9: Do not travel by public transport, taxi together with others and do not go to public places.
