(Phnom Penh): General Him Yan and Lt. Gen. In Bora, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, this morning, October 7, 2020, chaired a meeting on the implementation of the monthly action plan for the prevention and suppression of theft in Phnom Penh. September 2020 and continue the direction.
The meeting was held at the meeting hall of the Criminal Police Department with the participation of Lt. Gen. Neng Chuor, Director of the Criminal Police Department, Deputy Director of the Department, Deputy Commissioner for Criminal Planning, Director of the Office under the Criminal Police Department and Phnom Penh Municipal Police, Inspector All 14 districts, as well as many other relevant officials.
A report read by Major General Suy Sokunthea, deputy director of the Criminal Police Department, shows that there were a total of 39 crimes, a decrease of one case compared to August 2020. About the operation, with the efforts of all forces, all units cooperated in cracking down on a total of 38 cases, arresting 49 suspects, accounting for 97%.
In order to continue to implement the action plan to prevent and suppress theft in order to contribute to the reduction of criminal offenses, the Steering Committee for the Implementation of the Action Plan has set out some important directions and professional measures for further implementation, including :
* First, strengthen the command mechanism to lead cooperation at all levels to increase the effectiveness of crime prevention, especially to encourage the forces responsible for implementing the crime prevention plan.
* Second: Strengthen and promote the management of the subject and the procedure to build a case to have strong evidence to prosecute at a high level (crime) in accordance with the Penal Code.
* Third: Review the case of the shocked person who was released and take action again to report to the management for further action.
