"Hun Sen Tbeng" Primary School was re-established during the 1980s and has trained hundreds of thousands of children. In the school year 2019-2020, the school has 336 students, 186 females.
At present, "Hun Sen Tbeng" Primary School has two school buildings, which were built in 1997. After more than 20 years of educating students, the school building, which is the legacy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has also fallen into disrepair.
Apart from the dilapidated school building, during the rainy season, when it rains heavily, it rains in the school because the campus is lower than the surrounding houses. The floodwaters in the school caused the students to stop studying and also made it difficult for the students to cut water into the school.
After receiving information about the dilapidated building of the building, threatening the safety of the students and the flooding, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, decided to build a new school building for the students there.
In addition to this decision, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also instructed Tycoon Try Pheap, Samdech's personal advisor and chairman of the "B6" Party Committee, to inspect and manage the construction of this school immediately. On October 6, 2020, Mr. Oknha Try Pheap, Deputy Chairman of Kandal Stung Local Strengthening Committee, led the team to inspect the site, select the location and assign the construction technician to measure the construction site.
Tycoon Try Pheap instructed the team to repair the old school building so that the students could study temporarily and to speed up the construction of the new school building so that the students could get to school as soon as possible. The tycoon claimed that he would speed up the construction of the new school building soon.
Mr. Oknha Try Pheap, who was born and raised in Tbeng commune, also expressed his pleasure by working under the guidance of Samdech Techo Hun Sen in building this school for the benefit of the people in His homeland.
Both teachers and students who used to be worried about the dilapidated school condition and the difficulty of walking through the water to the school were overjoyed. They smiled and said that the new school is the desire of both teachers and students to be able to serve not only the students of this generation but also the students of the next generation.
It should be noted that on the occasion of inspecting and managing the construction of this school, Mr. Oknha Dr. Try Pheap met with teachers and students and brought with them the donations and books of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Katiprittbandit. Bun Rany Hun Sen distributed to teachers and students as well.
