Mr. Hem Hoeun, a 61-year-old male resident of the above village and a foreman in the above plantation, described that his plantation owner has planted 15 hectares of pumpkins and the pumpkins have started to ripen, with 25 harvests per hectare. Tons and hired workers to harvest and sell to traders at a lower price than last year, with the first pumpkin weighing 5-12 kg, traders buy 1 kg for only 700 riel.
