The Ministry of Health has issued a proclamation to facilitate Muslims to organize funerals and worship at mosques and all religious ceremonies in stages, except for pilgrimage gatherings.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health on October 6, 2020, issued a proclamation to facilitate Muslims to organize funerals and worship at mosques and all religious ceremonies in stages, except for gatherings. Pilgrimage.
The ministry said that all religious ceremonies and gatherings of Muslims must adhere to the rules of health, such as wearing a mask, measuring their hands, washing their hands regularly with soap and alcohol, or that there should be at least 1.5 gaps between individuals. Disinfection meters regularly clean the temples and keep the appropriate social spacing of each church site.
The Islamic leadership must also monitor the implementation of all religious ceremonies and gatherings as thoroughly as possible. In case of any problem related to suspected Kovid-19 disease, each church committee should immediately report to the nearest local authority or health center.
