(Phnom Penh): Ambassador Pablo Kang, Representative of the Australian Embassy in the Kingdom of Cambodia, led his delegation to visit the "Samdech Mey Library" of the Documentation Institute of the Documentation Center of Cambodia this morning, October 6, 2020. .
After a warm welcome to the distinguished delegates, Mr. Youk Chhang, Director of the Documentation Center of Cambodia and his team gave a detailed presentation on the two main exhibitions of the "Samdech Mey Library", the exhibition on the relics of His Majesty the King. Norodom Sihanouk and the exhibition on the design of the Sleuk Reut Institute building. Ms. Sofarina introduced the guests to the Khmer Rouge Research Centers and Libraries in the six provinces.
Mr. Youk Chhang also presented to the delegation the Samdech Mey Library, which contains more than 1.7 million documents and archives in various forms, collected by the Documentation Center of Cambodia team for more than 25 years, as well as the new archives. In addition, the generous donation of Ambassador Dr. Holly E. Gelres arrived at the Documentation Center of Cambodia in late 2019.
Ambassador Dr. Holio A. Gelredes is an Australian native to Chile. He was his personal secretary from 1981 to 1991 and was a former biographer of the Royal Palace from 1993. The Ambassador has published a number of research works related to the Royal Family of Cambodia, as well as continuing his further research on the above topics.
Youk Chhang expressed his deep gratitude for Ambassador's generous donation, saying: "This donation is not only a gift of great knowledge, but also a donation for The future of education and research in Cambodia.
He said that today's libraries, schools and research documentation centers are "seed nurseries for the future of Cambodia."
Through visits and discussions on various topics surrounding the work of the Documentation Center of Cambodia, the delegates expressed their deep appreciation and satisfaction.
