(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) on October 6, 2020 issued a press release stating that it has three mechanisms during the voter list review and registration process. 2020.
According to a press release obtained by Fresh News, the NEC has set up a working mechanism with three stakeholders to monitor and review the progress of the 2020 voter list and voter registration review. Below:
1. Mechanism of regular meetings with stakeholders at both the national and provincial levels in order to identify challenges and jointly find solutions.
2. Communication mechanism through administrative letter In case the relevant party finds that there are gaps or any irregularities, the relevant party can use this second mechanism to raise those issues in writing to c. The NEC asks for clarification or take appropriate remedial action.
3: In case of violation of the provisions of the Law on the Election of the National Assembly (NCC), Chapter 10 and / or regulations and procedures for the examination of the voter list and voter registration. Stakeholders can use the third mechanism, which is the mechanism for receiving and resolving complaints according to the hierarchy and according to the form, duration and procedure set by the NEC.
