Among the eight draft laws passed by the National Assembly, they are important in society, strengthening social, economic, trade, domestic and international trade, as well as enhancing cooperation with friendly countries in the fields of trade, law and environment. .
Such as the draft law on the management, use and disposal of state property. The draft law aims to strengthen the legal framework, institutional structure and enhance the institutional capacity to manage state assets, good governance, increase efficiency, transparency, efficiency and accountability.
Please be informed that the eight draft laws that the National Assembly discussed and approved today include:
1. Discussion and approval of the draft law on the management, use and disposal of state property.
Discussion and approval of the draft law on the ratification of the Treaty on Mutual Legal Assistance in Criminal Field between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Republic of Korea.
Discussion and approval of the draft law on the approval of the extradition treaty between the Royal Government of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Government of the French Republic.
Discussion and approval of the draft law on the ratification of the Treaty on Mutual Legal Aid in the criminal field between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Russian Federation.
Discussion and approval of the draft law on the ratification of the Minamata Convention on Mercury.
7. Discussion and approval of the draft law on the approval of the amendment of the Montreal Protocol on Ozone Depleting Substances.
Discussion and approval of the draft law on the approval of the ASEAN-Hong Kong Free Trade Agreement of the People's Republic of China.
