The third wall structure of Banteay Srei temple was repaired to avoid danger
(Siem Reap): The third wall structure of Banteay Srei temple, which was damaged and dilapidated, has been repaired and resisted by conservation experts to avoid risk. The third wall, which has now been repaired and supported, has five locations and a total length of 40 meters.
The main purpose of the repair is to reduce the serious damage to the wall structure as well as rescue other related structures that are in danger in a timely manner.
Mr. Saray Kim Huol, Archaeologist and Head of Banteay Srei Conservation Project, said that the reason for the deterioration of the structure of the walls and temples is due to natural factors combined with the longevity of the construction, that is, part of the structure was destroyed by The collapse of the trees suppresses the roots of large trees, causing the foundations to collapse and crack differently from the original form.
In 2005, Switzerland and the Apsara Authority collaborated to excavate and save the temple to preserve its ancient beauty and design it as the first hospital venue in Angkor Park.
In 2016, the APSARA Authority repaired and strengthened the structure of the gates and laterite walls by preserving the original form of the building and re-considering the use of traditional techniques, including materials and history of construction.
However, Banteay Srei still has many structures that have not been repaired and require further conservation and repair.
Kampot Provincial Governor Reminds Relevant Departments and Authorities to Increase Attention and Accelerate Investment Program Building
(Kampot): Mr. Chiao Tay, Governor of Kampot Province, reminded the relevant departments and authorities to pay more attention to accelerate the construction of investment programs on a clear basis in accordance with the instructions of the Ministry and specialized departments to implement the program. Timely and able to meet the needs of the people, reduce the poverty rate as desired by the Royal Government.
This reminder as the provincial governor participated in the consultation forum on the construction of the three-year rolling investment program (2021-2023) on October 6, 2020 at the Kampot Provincial Hall with the participation of about 186 stakeholders .
The provincial governor said that usually, whatever you do, you need to have a plan, vision, direction and time, especially the synthesis of inputs to be successful. However, the development of Kampot is the same, investment planning is very important in case of interruption or not on time, it is not only a loss, development is slow, people also have more needs and challenges. To affect the leadership of the Royal Government.
He also asked the municipal, district, commune and sangkat departments to pay more attention to and accelerate the development of their investment programs. Mr. Pan Sosak defended the draft law on the ratification of the ASEAN-Hong Kong Free Trade Agreement.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce and Minister of Economy of ASEAN for Cambodia, led a delegation to defend the draft law on the ratification of the ASEAN-Hong Kong Free Trade Agreement (AHKFTA) at the 1st Plenary Session of the National Assembly. 5 The 6th legislature on the afternoon of October 6, 2020.
During the 5th Plenary Session of the 6th National Assembly, Minister Pan Sosak also informed about the main contents of the agreement and the benefits that Cambodia will receive when this agreement enters into force.
After careful scrutiny, the 5th Plenary Session of the 6th Legislature fully approved the draft law on the approval of the ASEAN-Hong Kong Free Trade Agreement with 111 votes.
Minister Pan Sosak, on behalf of the Royal Government, expressed his deep gratitude to Samdech Chakrei, Chairman of the Meeting and members of the National Assembly for approving the draft law. The Minister expressed strong hope that this law will bring significant benefits to society as a whole and promote better economic growth of Cambodia.
The agreement will also make a significant contribution to facilitating cross-border trade and investment, as well as reducing barriers to market access, to facilitate the facilitation of small and medium enterprises between ASEAN and Hong Kong of the People's Republic of China.
