Senior officials of the Ministry of Agriculture instructed the Tbong Khmum Provincial Department of Agriculture to continue to support farmers in planting and raising livestock.
(Tbong Khmum): Mr. Nut Chan Sokha, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, instructed the Tbong Khmum Provincial Department of Agriculture to continue to support farmers in agriculture, production and veterinary work, forestry, fisheries, community work and animal husbandry to facilitate livelihoods. Citizens of the 19th Kovid period.
He said this on the morning of October 6, 2020 during a meeting on the management of civil servants of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries in Tbong Khmum.
Mr. Nuth Chan Sokha continued that today's talk shows the attention of the Ministry's leadership in strengthening the management to promote the development of agriculture, forestry and fisheries to contribute to maintaining economic growth. National as well as increase the income of farming families in line with the rectangular strategy of the Royal Government of Cambodia, which is turning Cambodia into a high middle income country by 2030.
He praised and appreciated the achievements of the department in the past and present, despite some challenges, and advised the department to continue its efforts to implement the guidelines. The ministry has set out in the past.
In particular, responding to the challenges of Tbong Khmum Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries will continue to implement the strategic plan for the development of agriculture, forestry and fisheries and mobilize the participation of all parties to accelerate the development momentum to maintain national economic growth and Farmer family income.
Mr. Heng Piseth, Director of Tbong Khmum Provincial Department of Agriculture, gave a brief report on the situation of civil servants, management of civil servants and agriculture, forestry and fisheries in the province. He thanked the leadership of the Ministry of Agriculture for always paying attention to local officials, especially present now.
