(Phnom Penh): Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, urged Cambodian students to receive scholarships from the Government of Australia and New Zealand to study hard and use all their knowledge to develop Cambodia further.
Mr. Vong Soth added that studying abroad is very important for every student and this is also a rare opportunity, so all Cambodian students must cover their knowledge, strive to strengthen their abilities and must take Success to the motherland.
The Minister of Social Affairs also said that all Cambodian students must also show the prestige of Cambodia to other countries during their studies there. What is special is that all Cambodian students take good care of their health during the spread of Kovid 19.
Mr. Vong Soth's remarks came as he allowed Cambodian students receiving scholarships from the Government of Australia and New Zealand to meet and pay a courtesy call on October 6, 2020 at the Ministry of Social Affairs.
During the courtesy call, representatives of Cambodian students who received scholarships from the Australian and New Zealand governments also thanked Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, for allowing Cambodian students to pay their respects.
On behalf of the Cambodian students, they are also committed to using the knowledge they have acquired and gained from their studies to develop themselves and the country to grow further.
It should be noted that a total of 27 Cambodian students received scholarships from the Government of Australia and New Zealand, including 11 women who passed the scholarship exam to Australia and 9 New Zealand who will be sent to study at January 2021 is coming. Among them, there are 16 civil servants from ministries and institutions and 11 employees of private companies and NGOs.
The scholarship has been offered to Cambodia since 1994 as part of the Australian Government Development Assistance Program and aims to support Cambodia's growing economic growth while promoting people-to-people contacts. People of both countries
To date, more than 800 Cambodian students have received this scholarship to pursue postgraduate studies in Australia in various fields to bring this knowledge back to develop Cambodia and maintain cooperative relations. Operations between Cambodia and Australia.
Similar to the Australian Government Scholarship, the New Zealand Government Scholarship aims to promote sustainable development by providing postgraduate study opportunities in New Zealand in a variety of disciplines for Cambodian students to apply this knowledge. Participate in the development of the country after graduation.
The New Zealand government has been providing scholarship opportunities to Cambodian students since 2005, with about 35 students receiving scholarships each year to pursue postgraduate studies at universities in New Zealand.
Students who receive this scholarship must return to Cambodia immediately after graduation and must pledge to use their knowledge to develop themselves and the country and not be allowed to leave Cambodia to live or continue. Absolute study abroad during 2 years.
(World): The use and production of fossil fuels is increasing day by day according to the economic activity and consumption needs of each country. Do you know which countries use the most fuel and which countries produce the most energy?
But the country that consumes the most fuel is the United States, which has an average consumption of 20.54 million barrels per day. This is according to data from the US-based International Energy Data Analysis and Management Unit (EIA).
After the United States, China consumes an average of 14 million barrels per day, while Japan consumes an average of nearly 40,000 barrels per day.
