Preah Vihear Provincial Governor Introduces Four Measures to Monitor the Implementation of Tourism Safety Rules in the Province
(Preah Vihear): In the meeting of the working group to promote, guide and monitor the implementation of tourism safety measures in Preah Vihear province this morning, October 6, 2020, Mr. Prak Sovann, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, set out four measures to be implemented.
The four measures to be followed include:
* Agree on the stated directions and request the Secretariat of the Working Group to cooperate with the relevant departments and units of the local authorities to continue to disseminate the tourism safety rules and to monitor the implementation of the tour operators in accordance with the guidelines.
In the future, we must ensure that Kovid-19 does not spread in the community by respecting the implementation of safety and hygiene rules, which are the basis for building the trust and confidence of national and international tourists. Indispensable factor of the resumption of tourism in the province and in the country as a whole.
* In addition to preventing the spread of Kovid 19 under the mechanism of the Provincial Tourism Development Commission, the Department of Tourism should continue to pay more attention to cooperate with relevant departments and units to strengthen the management of tourism destinations. Existing tourism communities, tourist destinations and the development of new tourist destinations by connecting rural areas to attract more tourists.
* The Department of Tourism must cooperate with the Department of Environment, the Department of Agriculture and other relevant authorities to set up a mechanism to manage tourism destinations in Phnom Tbeng properly and ensure the effectiveness and sustainability of the environment.
Mr. Prak Sovann said that under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, in cooperation with the World Health Organization and other stakeholders, Cambodia has effectively prevented the spread of Kovid 19. High, with no outbreaks in the community, only a small number of imported cases, and doctors have treated many, especially 19 cases of Kovid's death in Cambodia.
He added that in addition to preventing Kovid 19 virus from infecting communities, the Royal Government has put in place measures to rescue businesses, services, staff and poor people affected by Kovid 19 virus.
At the same time, the Governor of Preah Vihear expressed his gratitude for the efforts of the leaders of the departments, units, governors, districts, commune chiefs, commune chiefs, the three armed forces and all stakeholders, especially doctors who have worked hard to treat patients. Both 19 Kovids in Preah Vihear province were cured.
For the most important and necessary purpose of participating in the prevention of the spread of Kovid 19, in addition to the many measures taken by the provincial administration, the provincial administration has set up another working group to promote, guide and monitor implementation. Tourism safety rules in accordance with the guidelines of the Ministry of Tourism and the Ministry of Health. Today, 3,478 people went to register to vote in Svay Rieng province
Mr. Toch Poliva, Deputy Governor of Svay Rieng Province, said that the participation of all stakeholders in helping to disseminate and encourage people to come and check the voter list and register to vote in 2020 is really invaluable.
In fact, in just five days, the voter registration team of Svay Rieng province provided new voter registration services to 3,478 people of all ages, equivalent to 64.48%, compared to the five annual voter registration plans for 2020. , 394.
Mr. Touch Poliva thanked for the efforts and good cooperation of the authorities at all levels and all election officials in Svay Rieng.
It should be noted that the National Election Committee (NEC) on October 6, 2020 issued a press release on the provisional results of the 5th day of the review of the voter list and voter registration 2020, stating that 18,342 people went to register to vote.
(Kampong Cham): Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham Province, urged the Joint Provincial Committee to continue to expedite the resolution of the remaining Prek Dambok market traders in Prek Dambok commune, Srey Santhor district as soon as possible in the second phase.
This was said by the Provincial Governor on the afternoon of October 5, 2020 at Kampong Cham Provincial Hall after a meeting to review the dispute resolution work of Prek Dambok Market traders with the participation of the Deputy Governor and members of the Joint Committee. The province settled disputes between Prek Dambok market traders and other relevant officials.
Mr. Heng Vanny, Deputy Governor of Kampong Cham Province and Chairman of the Provincial Joint Committee for Dispute Resolution at Prek Dambok Market, stated that the Joint Committee has resolved 13 times with a total of 115 traders with 138 stalls / beds. 93 stalls and 45 beds.
At the same time, the working group of the Provincial Joint Commission also raised 14 suggestions and challenges to request the decision-making principles from the provincial governor.
After listening to the report and the request of the Chairman of the Provincial Joint Commission, Mr. Un Chanda decided and agreed on the request for the coordination principle of the Provincial Joint Commission by dividing the number of stalls to be removed to divide the width of the stalls / beds. By keeping the layout of the stalls / beds and sidewalks the same and not allowing further expansion other than the review and approval of the Joint Provincial Commission.
As for the owners of 7 stalls out of the 25 stalls that have been confiscated in the past, they have come to the provincial administration to claim the stalls, and the provincial governor has handed over the matter to the district authorities to continue to deal with the stall owners. Stalls confiscated by the province. The provincial governor instructed the provincial joint committee to continue to resolve the remaining issues in the second phase as soon as possible.
It should be reminded that on September 3, 2020, Mr. Un Chanda and Mr. Lou Kimchhon, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of Sihanoukville Autonomous Port and the Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group visited Srey Santhor District, led a public forum with Prek Dambok Market traders. To solve this problem.
At that time, the provincial authorities decided to confiscate the remaining 25 stalls and hand them over to the chairman of the market management committee and set up a joint provincial committee headed by Mr. Heng Vanny, the deputy governor to mediate and resolve the dispute.
