Health Minister Shares Kovid-19 Fighting Experience in Cambodia at the 71st Meeting of the World Health Organization (WHO) in the Western Pacific
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Health of Cambodia, Prof. Mam Bun Heng, highlighted four key experiences on the topic of "Fighting Kovid-19 in the Kingdom of Cambodia" at the 71st Meeting of the Health Organization. The world of the Western Pacific via video.
The ceremony took place at the Ministry of Health on October 6, 2020 with the permission of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Minister Mam Bunheng shared four important experiences with the following contents:
So far, Cambodia has successfully managed and responded to Kovid-19 with the National Commission for the Fight against Kovid-19 under the wise and wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. The Inter-Ministerial and Sub-National Committees for Combating Kovid-19 have played an important role in responding, directing and coordinating the implementation of measures throughout the Royal Government and society as a whole.
Third, community participation is very important. Through this global epidemic, Cambodia has mobilized entire social resources, both public and private. Cambodia has made a special effort with the participation of religious leaders.
Fourth, national and international unity is a necessity. Close cooperation and partnership around the world in this circumstance is more important than ever.
The Minister of Health also stressed that Cambodia fully supports the leadership and coordination of the World Health Organization in the global response to Kovid-19 and expressed his deep gratitude to the World Health Organization. Special thanks to Dr. Takeshi Kasai, Regional Director of the Western Pacific and all Member States for their contribution to the fight against Kovid-19.
