The National Assembly continues to discuss and approve some important draft laws for the field of economy, trade and international cooperation (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The National Assembly of Cambodia on October 6, 2020 continued the 5th session of the 6th legislature. To discuss and approve some important draft laws that serve the economic, trade and international cooperation in the country.
The first plenary session was chaired by Dr. Nguon Nhel, First Vice President of the National Assembly, as Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, was busy accompanying the King and Queen Mother on a medical visit to Beijing, China. Then Samdech came back to chair the meeting.
For the draft law that the National Assembly will continue to discuss and approve in today's session are:
Discussion and approval of the draft law on the ratification of the Treaty on Mutual Legal Aid in the criminal field between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Republic of Korea.
Discussion and approval of the draft law on the ratification of the Treaty on Mutual Legal Aid in the criminal field between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Russian Federation.
The above draft laws are all important in the society, such as promoting economic growth, trade and international cooperation. For example, the draft law on the management, use and management of state assets aims to strengthen the legal framework, institutional structure and enhance the institutional capacity to manage state assets.
It should be noted that in the 5th session of its 6th legislature yesterday, the National Assembly approved the draft law on the regulation of commercial gambling, which will contribute to the absorption of revenue from the gambling sector through investment permits. In the field of commercial games and some other games that are under the rules.
This draft law has 12 chapters and 97 articles that apply to the Integrated Trade and Gambling Center in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
Kathen Donation Ceremony of King Kong Sam Ol at Wat Champouvorn
(Phnom Penh): On the occasion that Buddhists from all over Cambodia have united in building the Kathina according to his generosity to give to the monks after waiting for the rainy season for a quarter in every temple during A period of 1 month from the 1st day of the lunar month until the 15th day of the lunar month, the year of Chuot Tosak 2564.
Separately, Samdech Chao Feang Kong Sam Ol, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of the Royal Palace and Mrs. Thay Va Kong Sam Ol, Director of Panha Maternity Hospital, initiated the construction of a large charity with great generosity to Buddhism to provide monks at the pagoda. Chumpouvorn is located in Sangkat Choam Chao, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
The ceremony took place with the invitation of monks Chamroeun Preah Berit to give sermons on non-monks, which arose from the pure generosity in the construction of the Kathina and to perform other good deeds in accordance with the Buddhist tradition.
It should be reminded that Samdech Chao Fea Veang, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of the Royal Palace and she always initiated the construction of the Kathina every year to provide monks at Wat Chumpouvorn and in various temples.
Not only that, the Prince and Queen are the great Buddhists of Cambodia who have sacrificed a lot of personal resources in a clear and sincere respect for Buddhism. Many important monks at Wat Champouvorn and other monasteries to contribute to the promotion of Buddhism in Cambodia to grow forever.
It should be reminded that the construction of the Kathina is a big festival with a history dating back to the time when our teacher Samma Samput lived, and in that prehistoric era, there was a millionaire Anabandit who initiated the construction of the Kathina first to give the Samma Samput.
The ceremony held a procession in honor of Preah Ratanatray, then the Prince and Queen, as well as government officials, philanthropists and Buddhists celebrated the Preah Ratanatray Samathan Sil. In this order, the monks were invited to perform their duties in the ceremony of offering the Kathina, the Swayaya Buddha, Chey Mongkul, the Triangle, the Tey Leang, and the Bovana Chaktachchai to all the monks.
At the same time, they donated the equipment of the Kathina and the suffix on the trumpet, which is the generosity of the King and Queen, and the family of Mr. Kuy Sophal and Mrs. and the leaders of the civil servants of the Ministry of the Royal Palace Philanthropists and Buddhists at the foot of Wat Ver donate to monks for the benefit of supporting the lives of monks and building achievements in this pagoda.
