Unfortunately, this natural waterfall area is overlooked by most tourists in Mondulkiri. If you visit once, you will really fall in love with the natural beauty of the cold waterfall, along with the delicious and delicious food of the indigenous people of Pnong.
"Leng Ang Leng Khin" waterfall is about 4 km from National Road 76, traveling through the entrance of the red road on the left hand side. When traveling from Phnom Penh, pass the road of Orang district about 100 meters, surrounded by cool forest, a quiet place for relaxation and bathing, located in Puzam village, Sen Monorom commune, Orang district, 26 kilometers from Sen Monorom city.
About 200 meters from the waterfall resort, walk the same size as the body without any sign. "Leng Ang Leng Khin" resort seems to show a smile waiting for guests to come and relax the silence there. Under the roar of the waterfall, "Leng Ang Leng Khin" waterfall sprayed cold water to irrigate the surrounding plants, keeping the light green and providing dew to the guests walking down the slope to the bottom.
"It is estimated that the Kovid-19 outbreak receives more than 7,000 or 8,000 multi-national tourists a year through the Kovid-19 waterfall outbreak," he told reporters. The visit of these tourists has greatly contributed to the development of their community.
Ms. Sreung Sen, an indigenous Pnong chef, expressed her happiness since the establishment of the community, making them earn money by cooking for tourists who come to visit the "Leng Ang Leng Khin" waterfall area. In particular, give them extra income to develop their community.
It should be informed that throughout Mondulkiri province, there are up to 36 resources and natural tourist attractions, including waterfall resorts, indigenous cultural resorts, mountains, landscapes, villages, ethnic groups, seas, forests, tourism communities, sanctuaries. Wildlife and cold weather. Deputy PM Hor Namhong Chairs a Meeting of Cambodia-China Intergovernmental Coordinating Committee
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong this morning, October 6, 2020, chaired a meeting of members of the Cambodia-China Intergovernmental Coordinating Committee on the implementation of an urgent job list in a number of key areas.
The meeting was held at the Office of the Council of Ministers with the participation of representatives of relevant ministries and institutions.
The meeting also discussed and mentioned the following important areas:
The signing of the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement, which has already achieved the full text of the agreement, is still under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and the top leaders of China.
* Development of infrastructure projects for Street 71C, Street 31, Street 33 and Street 41
* In particular, to import more Cambodian agricultural products to China soon, especially 400,000 tons of rice and many other agricultural products such as: banana, mango, cassava flour, durian, cashew nuts, rubber, sugarcane, Pailin, pepper. Coconut, dragon fruit and saliva, etc.
* Development of modernization of Cambodian agriculture
* About the development of wastewater system in Sihanoukville as soon as possible
* On cooperation between the Ministry of Interior, especially security issues, human resource training issues, sub-national administrative cooperation issues, and direct communication issues between other institutions.
The Chinese representative stressed that global solidarity and international cooperation are the most powerful weapons in the fight against and overcome COVID-19. Among the countries that support the statement, more than half are facing sanctions from the United States, the European Union (EU), including Cuba, North Korea, Iran, Russia, Syria and Venezuela.
