(Phnom Penh): A young man, a former activist of the former opposition party, was arrested and educated and released after he broke into the headquarters of the former National Rescue Party in Chak Angre Leu, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh and recorded a video As well as cutting pictures and posting insulting content to the leaders on Facebook.
Through the contract that the young man made in front of the authorities, the young man admitted his mistake and publicly apologized.
In addition to confessing and apologizing with the promise to stop committing illegal acts, the young man also called on the people as well as all the authorities to pardon him, with the promise: "Promise that if the next day "The authorities need to come to clarify again, I will come at the time of the summons of the authorities without any evasion."
