Turn some locations in some protected areas with tourism potential into eco-tourism areas to increase local economy and strengthen the conservation of natural resources and biodiversity
Secretary of State Net Pheaktra said that this policy has now become a reality and has been implemented and fruitful as the relevant ministries and institutions have been promoting and developing ecotourism in protected areas in Cambodia. Some locations in nature reserves are full of tourism potential.
According to the Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment, in Keo Seima Wildlife Sanctuary, there are 10 attractive natural waterfalls such as Leng Ang Leng Khin Waterfall, and now the Ministry of Environment and NGOs Wildlife Conservation WCS, a partner in the protection and conservation of the Keo Seima Wildlife Sanctuary, has been providing both spiritual and technical support to communities to create ecotourism communities.
Andong Kraloeng eco-tourism community in Sen Monorom commune, Oreang district, in the project to conserve white-tailed monkeys and yellow-cheeked vultures, has been attracting tourists, especially foreign tourists, to visit rare animals in the world. In 2019, Andong Kraloeng eco-tourism community received more than 450 tourists, earning more than 17,000 US dollars. Mr. Pheaktra said that the revenue went to the community.
Ministry of Water Resources: From October 7-9, Cambodia will have more rain and wind, people living in low-lying towns near waterways and fishermen should be very careful
The capitals of the southern provinces bordering Vietnam and the coastal provinces are likely to receive heavy rainfall, making lowlands near waterways, mountainous areas and the Cardamom Mountains in those provinces. High risk of flooding At the same time, in coastal areas and on the sea surface, there may be heavy rain, strong winds and high waves.
