The Minister of Water Resources led a technical team to inspect the water situation at the 7 Makara Reservoir Dam and along the river delta that may face harassment from the Stung Prek Tnaot flood.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Lim Kean Hor, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, on the afternoon of October 5, 2020, led a technical team to inspect the water situation at the 7 Makara Reservoir and along the river delta, which may face harassment. From the flood of Stung Prek Tnaot in the western part of Phnom Penh and Kandal province.
To date, the water situation is still under alert. The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has prepared 14 heavy machinery, 1,000 large sandbags, 20,000 small sandbags, rock nets and a 24-hour team to continue to intervene at the dam. Delta to prevent the risk of flooding, which can cause flooding to people's homes in the area.
On October 5, 2020, the Ministry of Water Resources issued a statement on the weather situation in Cambodia, stating that after monitoring the progress of the weather conditions, it was observed that the low pressure system continued to extend across Cambodia. By connecting to a low pressure in the South China Sea.
At the same time, the Ministry of Water Resources called on people living in low-lying towns near the waterway and all fishermen and seafarers to pay more attention to avoid any danger. That could happen eventually.
