(Phnom Penh): Oknha Lim Heng, Vice President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, emphasized that the signing of the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement is not only beneficial for Cambodian and Chinese companies, US companies or Japanese companies. And other countries also benefit from this agreement.
In a weekly guest interview, Tycoon Lim Heng stated, "The first beneficiaries of the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement are our local Cambodian companies, whether Cambodian or foreign-invested. "Once the agreement is finalized, it will benefit from duty-free production and export in China."
In addition, the Vice President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce stated, "Not only that, companies from the United States, China, Japan, Korea and other companies in the ASEAN region will be able to invest in Cambodia. To be able to produce and export to China to be duty free as well.
At the same time, Tycoon Lim Heng also said that we should be proud that our country is small and the economy is small, why we got a free trade agreement with China is not normal, so it is good relations between The leaders of the two countries who favor Cambodia, which is the luck of the Cambodian people.
Cambodia and China recently concluded negotiations on a free trade agreement and are expected to sign the agreement soon between the two countries' leaders. If nothing changes, the free trade agreement will enter into force in January 2021.
China is the largest source of foreign direct investment as well as tourists to Cambodia and also Cambodia's most important trading partner.
In fact, in 2018, the bilateral trade volume between Cambodia and China totaled about $ 6.5 billion, an increase of 15 percent compared to 2017, which was worth only $ 5.6 billion.
In 2019, the total trade volume between the two countries reached 8.2 billion US dollars, an increase of about 27 percent over 2018.
