The wife of 4-star General Lay Kimhong obeys Samdech Techo's win-win solution to end land dispute with 5 families in Poipet
As a result of the mediation to end the dispute, Ms. Lay Kim Hong agreed to accept $ 130,000 and agreed to give all the land to the five families, including all the potato crops that are being grown. (Approximately $ 7,500) to the five families who agreed to take back all the land.
Seeing the effectiveness of the win-win solution for Samdech Techo, Ms. Lai Kimhong decided to apply to Samdech Techo on September 4, 2020 to ask for justice for him. On that occasion, Mr. Duong Dara, Samdech Techo's personal assistant, went to Battambang province to meet and coordinate with Ms. Lai Kimhong and General Bun Seng many times about the above dispute.
On the morning of October 5, Mr. Duong Dara also invited all parties concerned, including lawyers from both sides, to meet for the last time to mediate and resolve the dispute at the Peace Palace, as a result, all parties agreed to Hands end the dispute based on the win-win principle of Samdech Techo under the mediation of Mr. Duong Dara.
Of course, no matter how long the conflict lasts for many years, no matter how much each party has the influence of great merit and wealth, but if the solution is based on the principle of win-win with virtue to solve it, that will Get good results, as in the case above.
Mr. Duong Dara, Samdech Techo's personal assistant, thanked Ms. Lai Kimhong and 5 families such as Mr. Chinchon, Mr. Suon Bora, Ms. Sam Than, Mr. Chea Sarath, and Mr. Chuon Chivin for choosing to resolve the external land dispute. The judiciary that wins results wins with a smile on everyone's face.
Mr. Duong Dara also expressed his deepest gratitude to Samdech Techo Prime Minister, who always has love, compassion and high attention to the people everywhere, because the well-being of the people is the personal well-being of Samdech.
Mr. Duong Dara called on the officials and the rich to choose a win-win solution to end all disputes, big and small throughout the country, to contribute to our leaders for the harmonization of our society as a whole. .
