Foreign Ministry Delegation Visits "Samdech Mey Library"
(Phnom Penh): Twelve female delegates representing the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia visited the "Samdech Mey Library" of the Documentary Institute of the Documentation Center of Cambodia on the afternoon of October 5, 2020. This visit is the initiative of Princess Norodom Arunrasmey.
Youk Chhang, Director of the Documentation Center of Cambodia and his team warmly welcomed the distinguished delegation. The visit begins with a detailed description of the exhibition of the relics of His Majesty the King Father of Cambodia, His Majesty the Queen Mother of Cambodia and the Royal Family, provided by Ambassador Dr. Holio A. Gelres, the former biographer of the King, accompanied by music composed by the King.
Mr. Youk Chhang presented to the delegation the library of thousands of books and hundreds of thousands of documents, original documents, photo and video archives, audio-visual archives and digital archives of the Documentation Center of Cambodia. All. Mr. Youk Chhang also described in detail the background and meaning of the design of the Sleuk Reut Institute building.
Ms. So Farina, Deputy Director of the Documentation Center of Cambodia, presented the six "Khmer Rouge Documentary Libraries and Research Centers" in the provinces, along with her book on Cham Muslim women.
At the end of the visit, the DPRK delegation and the working group of the Documentation Center of Cambodia discussed issues related to the preservation and documentation of the tragedies that women faced during the Khmer Rouge regime and its consequences, as well as the role of women in development. After the fall of January 7, 1979, the Khmer Rouge regime left most survivors, women and children, accounting for 65% of the population of the then 5 million people.
Women have also become a major force in rebuilding and rebuilding the nation after decades of genocide, genocide and conflict. With the Royal Government urging and focusing on gender equality and empowerment, many Cambodian women have evolved from traditional roles that determine that women should remain housekeepers and participate in key government positions. Business, education and many other fields.
Ms. Srounarya shared her interest, understanding that the layout of the library is very good because the building is an ancient building, but the exhibits of the building are highly creative, especially the contemporary photo exhibition space (including ancient And modern). The other is related to the preparation of documents, although the space is not very spacious, but the arrangement is artistic.
This proves that Cambodian women are the symbol of the soul of the Cambodian nation. Samdech Mey Library was established to dedicate to Cambodian women in the past, present and future.
The water of Pursat river has started to recede!
(Pursat): The water level in Pursat city has started to recede and the flooding will be less as of the evening of October 5, 2020.
It should be noted that on the evening of October 4, 2020, the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology of Pursat Province issued a notification on the water level of Pursat River, the water level has risen to the level of emergency for the second time after being affected by the low pressure system. From the South China Sea, flash floods occur after the Cardamom Mountains, Areas, Prey Khlong and Stung Thom are high on the Pursat River.
In that announcement, it is said that in order to be prepared to prevent natural disasters and floods along the river in Pursat province, the authorities of municipalities, districts, communes, sangkats at all levels and people throughout Pursat province, especially people living along the river. Pursat and related rivers, please pay close attention to avoid any accidents that may occur and be prepared to find a safe place for evacuation of vulnerable people.
