Spokesman for the General Commission: On October 5, another 830 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 158 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to October 5, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected And fined a total of 184840 vehicles, including 136731 motorcycles and 48109 vehicles of all types.
Notable offenses for motorcycles are mostly helmet offense, sign offense, no license plate, drunken driving and cell phone use. In particular, the offenses for cars are mostly speeding, overcrowding, driving licenses, no seat belts, drunkenness and using mobile phones.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 158 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine vehicles for offenses has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
It should be noted that for October 5, 2020, there were 13 traffic accidents throughout Cambodia, including 3 deaths, 21 injuries (15 serious injuries). During the 158 days, there were 1318 traffic accidents in Cambodia, in which 653 people were killed and 2058 were injured (1,231 were seriously injured).
