Cambodia cannot escape the threat of Kovid-19 as well, although so far Cambodians and foreigners living in Cambodia have not been harmed. Loss of life yet. But as a justification, this issue has inevitably affected many sectors, especially in the economic and social spheres.
He added that the organization of the workshop is part of the implementation of the emergency preparedness and response project, in which the project implementation team of AIMF in collaboration with the Department of Health of Phnom Penh opened the course. Nine trainings have already been conducted, focusing on the general condition of Kovid-19, prevention of infection, use of personal protective equipment, collection and packaging of Kovid-19 patients.
