(Mondulkiri): The Ministry of Environment is investigating to find the perpetrators who illegally set up posts on state land in the area of Keo Seima Wildlife Sanctuary in Purang village, Sen Monorom commune, Orang district, Mondulkiri province. This was confirmed by Mr. Net Pheaktra, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Environment.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra made this statement while leading a group of journalists to explore the implementation of the Red Bosima project of the Keo Seima Wildlife Sanctuary in Mondulkiri province on October 4, 2020.
At the same time, Mr. Net Pheaktra said that the Ministry of Environment has worked to strengthen legal measures to protect protected areas and conserve natural resources, as well as forests, wildlife and other natural resources for the common benefit of all mankind.
The spokesman for the Ministry of Environment added that in the past, despite the Ministry's efforts to prevent all natural resource crimes and encroachment on state land, there are still some criminals taking advantage of the opportunity to set up fence posts to encroach on state land and land. Protected areas are also illegal wildlife sanctuaries. In this case, the Ministry will take legal action against those people without exception.
At the same time, he also strongly warned that all activities should be stopped immediately as it is illegal and the Ministry will enforce the law without exception for those who violate the encroachment and post in the wildlife sanctuary. Protected areas as well as state lands.
In addition, on the day of the field visit at Keo Seima Wildlife Sanctuary, Mr. Neth Pheaktra led officials from the Ministry of Environment together with the Mondulkiri Provincial Department of Environment to remove the wooden and stone fence posts that illegally encroached on state land at Puring village, Sen Monorom commune. About 50 trees in Oreang district, Mondulkiri province, as well as burning and destroying.
He pointed out that in the case of encroachment on forest land as well as state land to be illegally owned, some officials involved were arrested and removed from office, senior officials of the Ministry of Justice and the governor of Koh Nhek district.
