(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports on October 5, 2020 celebrated the Teachers' Day on October 5 under the theme
"Smart Teachers for Digital Education" with the participation of teachers, education staff, Khmer Academic Staff Association, higher education associations and representatives of various relevant development partners.
October 05 Teachers' Day under the theme "Smart Teachers for Digital Education" was held in the presence of Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, which took place at the National Institute of Education for a full day.
Minister Hang Chuon Naron said that in the medium and long term, to prepare and orient teachers to respond to the digital age and new contexts, especially to continue to move towards digital education, the Ministry will continue to Focus on improving the capacity of teachers by continuing to implement teacher training training reforms, focusing on:
1: Development of 4 pedagogical centers (Kandal, Prey Veng, Kampong Cham and Siem Reap)
2: Improving the qualification of teachers to the bachelor's degree
3: Organizing short-term and teacher-oriented teacher training programs towards schools
4: Opening the teacher education channel by organizing a training program that balances the participation of teacher training institutions and schools in teacher training, focusing on: (1) the connection between theory and practice and (2) communication. Between teacher training institutions and schools
5: Linking teacher training with teacher training programs at different stages of the teaching career
6: Reducing the gap in teacher training programs between specialized subjects and teaching methods, and between research and teaching, and between institutes, pedagogues and schools
Taking this opportunity, Minister Hang Chuon Naron would also like to thank the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, relevant ministries and institutions, who always pay attention to all forms of investment in the education sector to facilitate and support education reform, especially the leadership of the Ministry of Education. All levels, teachers, students and all young people who have been actively involved in past and future reforms.
In this program, there is also a lecture by Dr. Hang Chuon Naron on "Smart Teachers for Digital Education in Cambodia" and a discussion forum on 2 main topics: 1: The process of reopening general education schools and digital education. And 2: Teaching and learning through technology systems in higher education institutions as well.
