Park officials continue efforts to prevent and crack down on crime in order to preserve natural resources, forests and wildlife
(Mondulkiri): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesman of the Ministry of Environment, confirmed that 1,200 rangers of the Ministry of Environment have been serving as the Year of Forest Protection and Conservation of Natural Resources and have prevented and suppressed natural resource crimes. Highly responsible in various protected areas in Cambodia.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra made this statement during the three-day visit of a delegation from the Ministry of Environment and a group of journalists to learn about the protection and conservation of natural resources in Mondulkiri province. Until October 5.
According to the spokesman, Cambodia currently has a total of 66 protected areas and biodiversity corridors, including national parks, wildlife sanctuaries, multi-use areas, protected areas and Ramsar sites. A total of 7.3 million hectares, equivalent to 41% of the total land area of Cambodia.
Regarding the protected areas in Mondulkiri province, Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that there are 6 places with a total area of about 1 million hectares, including Keo Seima Wildlife Sanctuary, Sre Pok Wildlife Sanctuary. Nam Lear, Lumphat Wildlife Sanctuary, Phnom Prech Wildlife Sanctuary and Northeast Biodiversity Conservation Corridor.
According to a report by the Mondulkiri Provincial Department of Environment, in the first nine months of 2020, rangers from the Mondulkiri Provincial Department of Environment patrolled 2,995 protected areas, cracking down on 1,528 natural resource crimes. 84 cases were sent to court, 26 were fined, 364 chainsaws were confiscated, 34 cars were seized, and a total of 2,957 traps were removed.
He said that thanks to the efforts of park rangers over the years, large-scale natural resource crimes no longer occur, but small-scale crimes that require specialized authorities to continue to work harder to prevent. And crack down on the conservation of Cambodia's natural resources, forests, and wildlife.
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of October 5, 2020, the National Assembly convened the 5th session of the National Assembly of the 6th legislature to discuss and approve some draft laws. The meeting has 11 agendas, chaired by Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, with the participation of 117 deputies.
1: Message from His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia to the 5th Session of the National Assembly of the 6th Legislature.
2: Report on the activities of the National Assembly between the 4th and 5th sessions of the 6th legislature.
3. Discussion and approval of the draft law on the management of commercial games.
4. Discussion and approval of the draft law on the management, use and disposal of state property.
Discussion and approval of the draft law on the ratification of the Treaty on Mutual Legal Aid in the criminal field between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Republic of Korea.
7. Discussion and approval of the draft law on the approval of the extradition treaty between the Royal Government of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Government of the French Republic.
Discussion and approval of the draft law on the ratification of the Treaty on Mutual Legal Aid in the criminal field between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Russian Federation.
9. Discussion and approval of the draft law on the ratification of the Minamata Convention on Mercury.
Discussion and approval of the draft law on the approval of the amendment of the Montreal Protocol on Ozone Depleting Substances.
Discussion and approval of the draft law on the ratification of the ASEAN Free Trade Agreement: Hong Kong, People's Republic of China.
Please be informed that the opening of the 5th session of the National Assembly of the 6th legislature took place after the National Assembly took a leave of absence from the National Assembly session for the past 3 months. July 2, 2020.
