(Banteay Meanchey): On the night of October 4, 2020, a monk and two other people were bitten by snakes in different places, but fortunately there was no impact on the lives of the victims. Go to Preah Net Preah District Hospital, Banteay Meanchey Province on time.
Dr. Le Chansangvat, Director of Banteay Meanchey Provincial Health Department, said that the three victims were:
According to the doctor's examination and conclusion, the snake may not be poisonous, while the monk's health is normal.
* Name: Mad Sovath, Male, 57 years old, living in Chob Vary Village, Chob Vary Commune, Preah Net Preah District. He arrived at Preah Net Preah Hospital at 6:45 p.m.
* Name: Sam Ling, male, 53 years old, living in Sala Cheh village, Rohal commune, Preah Net Preah district. He arrived at Preah Net Preah Referral Hospital at 8:00 pm, bitten by a snake on his left leg while filling water in a field. He did not know what kind of snake bites, and upon examination, the main symptoms were difficulty breathing, drowsiness, soft eyelids, soft limbs, abdominal pain, swelling and bruising.
Mr. Le Chansangvat appealed and requested all people to be careful when walking at night, especially the business of catching crickets at night in the forest or have grass, be very careful and in case of snake bites must be sent to The nearest hospital as soon as possible to rescue. He said that only public hospitals have doctors who are properly trained, especially with the snakebite vaccine to provide treatment and rescue.
