(Phnom Penh): Oknha Phasok, Dr. Keang Seng, Advisor to Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, was presented with a "Stall" by the King of Cambodia, while his wife, Tuy Simon, was honored by the King. The King conferred the "Maha Sereyvath" medal.
The awarding of the medal after Mr. Oknha Phasok, Dr. Keang Seng and Mrs. Tuy Simon donated a lot of personal funds to humanitarian activities and build achievements in both the realm and the kingdom.
Oknha Dr. Keang Seng and Mrs. Tuy Simon were personally handed over by His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni in the inauguration ceremony of the Royal Health Post of King Bhumibol Adulyadej. In the area of Wat Preah Indrasamakitham, Trapeang Krapeu village, Kraing Makak commune, Ang Snoul district, Kandal province, on October 3, 2020.
Mr. Oknha Keang Seng and Ms. Tuy Simon expressed their unimaginable joy at receiving great honors from the King in awarding medals.
Mr. Keang Seng and Ms. Tuy Simon stated that they will continue to participate in more humanitarian activities in society to contribute to the Royal Government in the development of the national society in both the realm and the Buddhist.
Please be informed that Mr. Oknha Dr. Keang Seng is the Founder of Comfort Center in Cambodia and the Founding President of Comfort in Cambodia as well as the General Director of Keang Seng Simon International Co., Ltd.
Mr. Oknha Dr. Keang Seng was born on Wednesday, 11 Roch Khek Tek, Chhnang Chhlov Panchasak, BE 2516, in Wat Kandal Village, Svay Por Commune, Sangke District, Battambang Province. He was married on December 28, 1995 to Miss Tuy Simon, born on Tuesday, March 6, 2522 in Mor village, Meteuk commune, Bakan district, Pursat province.
Until now, he has 4 sons and 1 daughter. Mr. Oknha graduated from the Secondary School in 1990 in his hometown in Battambang Province.
In 2000, as planned, he was sent to study at the Asian Institute of Technology, based in Bangkok, Thailand.
After graduating in 2002, he continued to work in the old place and did more work with the United Nations Development Program until 2010 under the direction of Professor Dr. P.I. Peter - Founder of Comfort World. Change jobs as a loyal businessman with increasing comfort to humanity.
With this business, he also did not forget to continue his studies until he completed his PhD (Doctor of Comfort) in 2011 in Colombo. Not only did he study science and health, Dr. Keang Seng learned more about the role and ethics of Cambodian priests to contribute to the promotion of Cambodian culture, traditions and customs.
From 2010 until now, he has been awarded the title of Duke and many important medals of the Kingdom of Cambodia, up to the title of Moha Sereyvath and as a stall.
