Authorities start collecting garbage at local level after Cintri employees go on strike
(Phnom Penh): Authorities in each district in Phnom Penh from yesterday and until October 4, 2020 began to collect garbage gradually after Cintri employees went on strike to collect garbage at times. Road.
For two days from Saturday, October 3, 2020 to this Sunday, Cintri staff did not come to collect garbage as usual, causing a lot of garbage congestion along some roads in the district.
For Daun Penh district, as a preliminary solution, Mr. Sok Penh Vuth, District Governor, led the officers under the supervision of Khan People's Protection Force and 11 Sangkat Sanitation Agencies in cooperation with the Phnom Penh Garbage and Solid Waste Management Authority to collect garbage at all major depots to ensure the collection. Clean and transport garbage well, no congestion and does not affect people's health, public order and local hygiene.
On October 3, 2020, the Phnom Penh Municipal Administration yesterday called on all Cintri workers to stop their strike by taking the garbage issue as an enemy. This is according to the announcement of Phnom Penh Capital Administration through Fresh News.
This announcement was made after the strike of Cintri employees, which took place from the evening of October 2, 2020 until now, causing garbage jams on the streets in the capital. Phnom Penh. During the strike, workers demanded that Cintri settle for: seniority pay, severance pay, severance pay, remaining annual leave.
According to the announcement of the Phnom Penh Capital Administration, the above claim is possible only if the company has terminated their work, but apparently the company has not terminated their work, the company is operating normally, so the demands of the company workers Cintri does not comply with labor laws and regulations.
Taking this opportunity, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration would like to call on the people to pack and store their garbage properly in the allotted time.
In order to avoid the congestion of solid waste in Phnom Penh, the Phnom Penh Municipal Administration has been taking action by using the garbage trucks of the Phnom Penh Municipal Administration and for the 14 Khan authorities to release motorbikes, tricycles and forces to collect garbage at the respective districts. Body.
